[{"source": "BREAD_STORAGE_AND_REVIVAL.md", "quote": "- **Days 1–2:** Place the loaf cut-side down directly on a wooden cutting board at room temperature. The cut face protects the crumb and the crust stays crisp. - **Days 3–5:** Transfer the loaf into an unbleached linen bread bag or brown paper sack. Avoid airtight plastic bags, which soften the crust and encourage mold. - **Location:** Keep away from the stove, direct sun, and humid spots. Ideal room temperature is 65°F–72°F (18°C–22°C)."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-003",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "What is in your sourdough bread?",
    "answer": "Our core breads contain only flour (stone-milled in-house or from regional growers), water, wild sourdough starter, and sea salt. We use no commercial yeast, dough conditioners, preservatives, or artificial stabilizers. Seeded and enriched items add ingredients such as sesame, walnuts, cherries, or honey, and each item's label lists everything in it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-STR-001",
    "category": "Bread Care & Storage",
    "question": "Should I keep my sourdough loaf in the refrigerator?",
    "answer": "Never refrigerate fresh artisan bread. Refrigerator temperatures (35\u00b0F-42\u00b0F / 1\u00b0C-5\u00b0C) accelerate starch retrogradation by up to 300%, causing the bread to dry out and go stale much faster. Store it cut-side down on a wooden board for days 1-2, then in a linen or paper bag for days 3-5.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "BREAD_STORAGE_AND_REVIVAL.md", "quote": "1. **Preheat Oven:** Set the oven to **375°F (190°C)**. 2. **Moisten the Crust:** Run the entire unsliced stale loaf under cold tap water for 3 to 5 seconds, or spritz generously with a water bottle. Do not soak. 3. **Bake:** Place the wet loaf directly on the center oven rack for **6 to 8 minutes**. 4. **Rest:** Allow the loaf to rest for 5 minutes before slicing. Steam gelatinizes the interior crumb, which reverses some of the retrogradation, while the crust crisps. **Tips** - Use this for loaves up to about 3 days old. Beyond that the bread is best sliced and toasted, or made into croutons, breadcrumbs, or panzanella. - Half loaves: cut-side down, 4 to 5 minutes. - Revived bread is best eaten the same day, because it will stale faster the second time. - **Mold:** If you see any mold, discard the whole loaf. Do not cut around it."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-004",
    "category": "Wholesale Accounts",
    "question": "What are your payment terms?",
    "answer": "Terms are Net-15 via automated ACH through the wholesale portal. Invoices generate when the delivery departs. New accounts need credit approval before the first delivery, and balances more than 15 days past due pause deliveries.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_ORDERING_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Credit Application:** New accounts submit a credit application and are approved before first delivery. Approval typically takes 3 business days. - **Payment Terms:** Net-15 via automated ACH through the wholesale portal. Invoices generate upon delivery departure. - **Late Payment:** Balances more than 15 days past due pause deliveries. A 1.5% monthly late fee applies after day 30. - **Quality Claims:** Missing, damaged, or unsatisfactory items must be reported within **12 hours of delivery drop** with cross-section photos. Approved claims are credited to the next invoice."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-002",
    "category": "Wholesale Accounts",
    "question": "What is the minimum order for wholesale delivery?",
    "answer": "The minimum order value is $75.00 per delivery drop. Orders below $75.00 incur a $15.00 small-drop surcharge.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CATERING_AND_CUSTOM_CAKES.md", "quote": "- **Delivery Fee:** $35.00 within Zone A (Urban Core) and $65.00 within Zone B (Outer Metro). Locations beyond our zones are quoted individually. - **Delivery Window:** We deliver and set up during a 2-hour window agreed in your contract, finishing at least 90 minutes before service. - **Venue Requirements:** A level table, shade, and a clear loading path. A refrigerated space within the venue is strongly recommended for tiered cakes. - **Tiered Cakes:** Cakes of three or more tiers are assembled on site by a staff member, and an on-site fee of $100.00 applies. - **Equipment:** Stands, boards, and linens are provided on loan with a refundable $75.00 deposit. They must be returned within 5 days. - **Closed Mondays:** Delivery and pickup are not available on Mondays."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-001",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "Are your sourdough breads safe for someone with Celiac Disease?",
    "answer": "No. While our 24-36 hour wild fermentation process breaks down some starches and makes bread easier to digest for many gluten-sensitive people, our facility actively stone-mills grains on-site. Airborne flour particles are present throughout the bakery. We are NOT a certified celiac-safe environment, and we do not make certified gluten-free products.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-003",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "What is in your sourdough bread?",
    "answer": "Our core breads contain only flour (stone-milled in-house or from regional growers), water, wild sourdough starter, and sea salt. We use no commercial yeast, dough conditioners, preservatives, or artificial stabilizers. Seeded and enriched items add ingredients such as sesame, walnuts, cherries, or honey, and each item's label lists everything in it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "ALLERGEN_SAFETY_PROTOCOL.md", "quote": "Cinder & Salt Bakery operates an open-concept bakery and an active stone mill. We mill whole grains (wheat, rye, spelt, einkorn, Red Fife) on-site every week. - **Gluten Presence:** Fine flour particles remain airborne throughout the facility 24 hours a day. No wall, bench, or schedule fully removes them. - **Celiac Disclaimer:** While some items are prepared without gluten-containing ingredients, **our facility is NOT celiac-safe**. We do not produce certified gluten-free products. Customers with Celiac Disease, severe gluten intolerance, or wheat allergy should not consume our products. - **Fermentation Is Not a Safety Claim:** Our 24–36 hour cold fermentation breaks down some starches and phytic acid and makes bread gentler for many people. It does **not** reduce gluten to a celiac-safe level (the regulatory threshold is under 20 ppm). We never market it as doing so. - **Staff Script:** "We're an active stone mill, so flour is in the air all day. We can't make a celiac-safe promise, and we'd rather tell you that honestly than risk your health.""}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-RET-006",
    "category": "Daily Retail & Orders",
    "question": "I received the wrong item or a damaged loaf in my retail order. What now?",
    "answer": "We're sorry about that. Please bring the item or a photo to the counter, or contact us within 24 hours of pickup, and our team will arrange a replacement or refund.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_ORDERING_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Our sourdough breads undergo a mandatory 24-to-36-hour cold fermentation cycle. Because we use no commercial yeast or dough accelerants, **all wholesale orders require a strict 48-hour advance notice**. - **Standing Order Freeze:** Standing orders lock at **2:00 PM** two days prior to delivery. - **Order Modifications:** Additions or reductions must be submitted through the B2B Portal before the 2:00 PM cutoff. Late modifications cannot be accommodated, because the dough is already mixed and committed. - **No Same-Day or Next-Day Orders:** We do not offer rush orders at any price. | Order Placed By (2:00 PM) | Fermentation & Proofing Window | Delivery Window | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | **Sunday** | Monday | **Tuesday Morning** | | **Monday** | Tuesday | **Wednesday Morning** | | **Tuesday** | Wednesday | **Thursday Morning** | | **Wednesday** | Thursday | **Friday Morning** | | **Thursday** | Friday | **Saturday Morning** | | **Friday** | Saturday | **Sunday Morning** | *Table Summary:* [1. The 48-Hour Fermentation Lead Time Rule] - Order Placed By (2:00 PM): Sunday | Fermentation & Proofing Window: Monday | Delivery Window: Tuesday Morning - Order Placed By (2:00 PM): Monday | Fermentation & Proofing Window: Tuesday | Delivery Window: Wednesday Morning - Order Placed By (2:00 PM): Tuesday | Fermentation & Proofing Window: Wednesday | Delivery Window: Thursday Morning - Order Placed By (2:00 PM): Wednesday | Fermentation & Proofing Window: Thursday | Delivery Window: Friday Morning - Order Placed By (2:00 PM): Thursday | Fermentation & Proofing Window: Friday | Delivery Window: Saturday Morning - Order Placed By (2:00 PM): Friday | Fermentation & Proofing Window: Saturday | Delivery Window: Sunday Morning *Note: Retail counter and delivery routes are closed on Mondays. Orders placed on Saturday before 2:00 PM are treated as placed for Monday and are not deliverable. They roll to the Sunday cutoff and deliver Tuesday.*"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-RET-005",
    "category": "Daily Retail & Orders",
    "question": "Which breads are baked on which days?",
    "answer": "Country Sourdough and Sesame Baguettes are baked Tuesday through Sunday. Seeded Dark Rye is baked Tuesday, Thursday, Saturday, and Sunday. Spelt Boule is baked Wednesday, Friday, Saturday, and Sunday. Einkorn Honey Loaf is baked Thursday, Saturday, and Sunday. Seasonal specials are posted on our website each week.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "BREAD_STORAGE_AND_REVIVAL.md", "quote": "- **Days 1–2:** Place the loaf cut-side down directly on a wooden cutting board at room temperature. The cut face protects the crumb and the crust stays crisp. - **Days 3–5:** Transfer the loaf into an unbleached linen bread bag or brown paper sack. Avoid airtight plastic bags, which soften the crust and encourage mold. - **Location:** Keep away from the stove, direct sun, and humid spots. Ideal room temperature is 65°F–72°F (18°C–22°C)."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-STR-001",
    "category": "Bread Care & Storage",
    "question": "Should I keep my sourdough loaf in the refrigerator?",
    "answer": "Never refrigerate fresh artisan bread. Refrigerator temperatures (35\u00b0F-42\u00b0F / 1\u00b0C-5\u00b0C) accelerate starch retrogradation by up to 300%, causing the bread to dry out and go stale much faster. Store it cut-side down on a wooden board for days 1-2, then in a linen or paper bag for days 3-5.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "BREAD_STORAGE_AND_REVIVAL.md", "quote": "Commercial bread uses mono- and diglycerides and chemical preservatives. Cinder & Salt sourdough contains only flour, water, and sea salt. - **Starch Retrogradation:** Staling is not simply drying out. When bread cools after baking, the gelatinized starch molecules gradually recrystallize and push moisture out of the crumb, which makes it firm and leathery. - **The Refrigerator Trap:** Refrigeration temperatures (35°F–42°F / 1°C–5°C) **accelerate retrogradation by up to 300%**. *Never store fresh artisan bread in the refrigerator.* - **Why Sourdough Lasts Longer:** Natural acids from wild fermentation slow mold and retain moisture, which is why a high-hydration loaf like our Country Sourdough (78% hydration) usually stays pleasant for 4 to 5 days. - **Crust Moisture:** Crust softens as moisture migrates outward. That is normal, and it can be reversed (see Section 3)."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-STR-003",
    "category": "Bread Care & Storage",
    "question": "Can I freeze sourdough, and for how long?",
    "answer": "Yes. Slice the loaf, put parchment between slices, and seal it in a freezer bag at 0\u00b0F (-18\u00b0C). It keeps well for up to 3 months. Toast slices straight from frozen.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAT-002",
    "category": "Catering & Events",
    "question": "How does the tasting box work, and what does it cost?",
    "answer": "A tasting box is $45.00 and includes 4 sourdough cake options and 3 seasonal buttercreams or preserves. Boxes are prepared on the 1st and 3rd Saturday of each month and are available for pickup from 10:00 AM to 1:00 PM. The fee is credited toward any final catering contract over $300.00.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAT-001",
    "category": "Catering & Events",
    "question": "How far in advance do I need to book a wedding cake or dessert table?",
    "answer": "We require a minimum of 6 weeks notice for wedding orders and large event catering (100+ guests), 14 days for smaller custom celebratory cakes, and 7 days for small wholesale event trays. Peak wedding season dates (May-October) can close up to 6 months ahead, so early booking is recommended.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CATERING_AND_CUSTOM_CAKES.md", "quote": "- **Fee:** $45.00 per tasting box (includes 4 sourdough cake options and 3 seasonal buttercreams/preserves). - **Credit:** The $45.00 fee is credited toward any final catering contract exceeding **$300.00**. - **Pickup Schedule:** Boxes are prepared on the 1st and 3rd Saturday of every month and are available for pickup between 10:00 AM and 1:00 PM. - **Reservation:** Tasting boxes must be reserved at least 7 days in advance. Unclaimed boxes are not held past 1:00 PM. - **Allergen Note:** Tasting boxes are produced in our standard facility. Tree nuts, dairy, eggs, wheat, and sesame may be present. Our facility is **not celiac-safe**."}, {"source": "CATERING_AND_CUSTOM_CAKES.md", "quote": "- **Weddings & Large Events (100+ guests):** Minimum **6 weeks** notice required. Peak-season dates (May–October) close up to 6 months in advance. - **Bespoke Celebratory Cakes:** Minimum **14 days** notice required. - **Small Wholesale Event Trays:** Minimum **7 days** notice required. - **Rush Requests:** We cannot accommodate bookings inside these windows. Our sourdough cake layers and laminated doughs need 18–36 hours of fermentation, and decorating takes more time on top of that."}]

