[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-002",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "Which major allergens are present in your facility?",
    "answer": "Wheat/gluten, rye, tree nuts (walnuts and almonds), sesame, dairy (butter, milk, cheese), and eggs are all handled in our facility. Nuts, sesame, dairy, and eggs use color-coded dedicated tools, but ovens, mixers, and the mill are shared, so cross-contact is possible. We do not guarantee any item is free of these allergens.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "ALLERGEN_SAFETY_PROTOCOL.md", "quote": "- Every retail item carries a label with ingredients and a "Contains" statement. - A posted notice at the counter and on the website reads: *"Our facility is not celiac-safe. All items may contain traces of wheat, tree nuts, sesame, dairy, and eggs."* - Customers with allergies are never told an item is "safe". They are told what is in it and what is nearby. - Any question we cannot answer from the allergen matrix is passed to the Head Baker, and no guess is offered."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-004",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "Do you have a nut-free or sesame-free bread?",
    "answer": "Several breads contain no nut or sesame ingredients, such as the Country Sourdough and Spelt Boule. We bake plain loaves first, at 2:00 AM, before seeded and nut items at 4:00 AM, and we sanitize at 12:00 PM and 8:00 PM. Shared ovens and airborne particles mean we cannot guarantee a nut-free or sesame-free product, so people with severe allergies should not rely on us.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAT-001",
    "category": "Catering & Events",
    "question": "How far in advance do I need to book a wedding cake or dessert table?",
    "answer": "We require a minimum of 6 weeks notice for wedding orders and large event catering (100+ guests), 14 days for smaller custom celebratory cakes, and 7 days for small wholesale event trays. Peak wedding season dates (May-October) can close up to 6 months ahead, so early booking is recommended.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CATERING_AND_CUSTOM_CAKES.md", "quote": "- **Delivery Fee:** $35.00 within Zone A (Urban Core) and $65.00 within Zone B (Outer Metro). Locations beyond our zones are quoted individually. - **Delivery Window:** We deliver and set up during a 2-hour window agreed in your contract, finishing at least 90 minutes before service. - **Venue Requirements:** A level table, shade, and a clear loading path. A refrigerated space within the venue is strongly recommended for tiered cakes. - **Tiered Cakes:** Cakes of three or more tiers are assembled on site by a staff member, and an on-site fee of $100.00 applies. - **Equipment:** Stands, boards, and linens are provided on loan with a refundable $75.00 deposit. They must be returned within 5 days. - **Closed Mondays:** Delivery and pickup are not available on Mondays."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAT-002",
    "category": "Catering & Events",
    "question": "How does the tasting box work, and what does it cost?",
    "answer": "A tasting box is $45.00 and includes 4 sourdough cake options and 3 seasonal buttercreams or preserves. Boxes are prepared on the 1st and 3rd Saturday of each month and are available for pickup from 10:00 AM to 1:00 PM. The fee is credited toward any final catering contract over $300.00.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CATERING_AND_CUSTOM_CAKES.md", "quote": "- **Weddings & Large Events (100+ guests):** Minimum **6 weeks** notice required. Peak-season dates (May–October) close up to 6 months in advance. - **Bespoke Celebratory Cakes:** Minimum **14 days** notice required. - **Small Wholesale Event Trays:** Minimum **7 days** notice required. - **Rush Requests:** We cannot accommodate bookings inside these windows. Our sourdough cake layers and laminated doughs need 18–36 hours of fermentation, and decorating takes more time on top of that."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-003",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "What is in your sourdough bread?",
    "answer": "Our core breads contain only flour (stone-milled in-house or from regional growers), water, wild sourdough starter, and sea salt. We use no commercial yeast, dough conditioners, preservatives, or artificial stabilizers. Seeded and enriched items add ingredients such as sesame, walnuts, cherries, or honey, and each item's label lists everything in it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-001",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "Are your sourdough breads safe for someone with Celiac Disease?",
    "answer": "No. While our 24-36 hour wild fermentation process breaks down some starches and makes bread easier to digest for many gluten-sensitive people, our facility actively stone-mills grains on-site. Airborne flour particles are present throughout the bakery. We are NOT a certified celiac-safe environment, and we do not make certified gluten-free products.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "ALLERGEN_SAFETY_PROTOCOL.md", "quote": "Cinder & Salt Bakery operates an open-concept bakery and an active stone mill. We mill whole grains (wheat, rye, spelt, einkorn, Red Fife) on-site every week. - **Gluten Presence:** Fine flour particles remain airborne throughout the facility 24 hours a day. No wall, bench, or schedule fully removes them. - **Celiac Disclaimer:** While some items are prepared without gluten-containing ingredients, **our facility is NOT celiac-safe**. We do not produce certified gluten-free products. Customers with Celiac Disease, severe gluten intolerance, or wheat allergy should not consume our products. - **Fermentation Is Not a Safety Claim:** Our 24–36 hour cold fermentation breaks down some starches and phytic acid and makes bread gentler for many people. It does **not** reduce gluten to a celiac-safe level (the regulatory threshold is under 20 ppm). We never market it as doing so. - **Staff Script:** "We're an active stone mill, so flour is in the air all day. We can't make a celiac-safe promise, and we'd rather tell you that honestly than risk your health.""}, {"source": "ALLERGEN_SAFETY_PROTOCOL.md", "quote": "- Every retail item carries a label with ingredients and a "Contains" statement. - A posted notice at the counter and on the website reads: *"Our facility is not celiac-safe. All items may contain traces of wheat, tree nuts, sesame, dairy, and eggs."* - Customers with allergies are never told an item is "safe". They are told what is in it and what is nearby. - Any question we cannot answer from the allergen matrix is passed to the Head Baker, and no guess is offered."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-STR-001",
    "category": "Bread Care & Storage",
    "question": "Should I keep my sourdough loaf in the refrigerator?",
    "answer": "Never refrigerate fresh artisan bread. Refrigerator temperatures (35\u00b0F-42\u00b0F / 1\u00b0C-5\u00b0C) accelerate starch retrogradation by up to 300%, causing the bread to dry out and go stale much faster. Store it cut-side down on a wooden board for days 1-2, then in a linen or paper bag for days 3-5.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-RET-004",
    "category": "Daily Retail & Orders",
    "question": "How much does a Country Sourdough Boule cost?",
    "answer": "The Country Sourdough Boule (850 g baked weight, 78% hydration) is $9.50. Prices for other loaves and pastries are in our daily bake matrix. For example, the Seeded Dark Rye is $10.50, and all prices are subject to change.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "BREAD_STORAGE_AND_REVIVAL.md", "quote": "- **Days 1–2:** Place the loaf cut-side down directly on a wooden cutting board at room temperature. The cut face protects the crumb and the crust stays crisp. - **Days 3–5:** Transfer the loaf into an unbleached linen bread bag or brown paper sack. Avoid airtight plastic bags, which soften the crust and encourage mold. - **Location:** Keep away from the stove, direct sun, and humid spots. Ideal room temperature is 65°F–72°F (18°C–22°C)."}]

[{"source": "BREAD_STORAGE_AND_REVIVAL.md", "quote": "- **Days 1–2:** Place the loaf cut-side down directly on a wooden cutting board at room temperature. The cut face protects the crumb and the crust stays crisp. - **Days 3–5:** Transfer the loaf into an unbleached linen bread bag or brown paper sack. Avoid airtight plastic bags, which soften the crust and encourage mold. - **Location:** Keep away from the stove, direct sun, and humid spots. Ideal room temperature is 65°F–72°F (18°C–22°C)."}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_ORDERING_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Access Requirements:** Partners must supply a reliable keycode or lockbox key for entry. - **Drop Location:** Drops are made directly to the partner's designated walk-in cooler or food-safe staging counter. Fresh bread is placed in breathable paper or cloth bags, never sealed plastic. - **Cold Weather Protection:** From Nov 1 to Apr 1, exterior lockbox drops are strictly prohibited to prevent thermal shock. A staffed or interior access point is required. - **Refrigeration Warning:** Do not refrigerate bread. Cold storage speeds staling (see `BREAD_STORAGE_AND_REVIVAL.md`)."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-RET-003",
    "category": "Daily Retail & Orders",
    "question": "Can I pre-order a loaf for tomorrow?",
    "answer": "Pre-orders need 48 hours of notice because of our cold fermentation. For same-day or next-day needs, the counter holds a limited daily supply, which is first come, first served.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-RET-006",
    "category": "Daily Retail & Orders",
    "question": "I received the wrong item or a damaged loaf in my retail order. What now?",
    "answer": "We're sorry about that. Please bring the item or a photo to the counter, or contact us within 24 hours of pickup, and our team will arrange a replacement or refund.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}]

