[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-006",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "My child had a reaction after eating one of your products. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Please seek medical attention immediately, and call 911 if there is any trouble breathing, swelling, or other signs of anaphylaxis. Once your child is safe, contact us with the product name, purchase time, and any batch code so our Quality Lead can investigate and quarantine the batch.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-002",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "Which major allergens are present in your facility?",
    "answer": "Wheat/gluten, rye, tree nuts (walnuts and almonds), sesame, dairy (butter, milk, cheese), and eggs are all handled in our facility. Nuts, sesame, dairy, and eggs use color-coded dedicated tools, but ovens, mixers, and the mill are shared, so cross-contact is possible. We do not guarantee any item is free of these allergens.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "ALLERGEN_SAFETY_PROTOCOL.md", "quote": "1. **Halt Production:** Flag the affected batch with RED "ALLERGEN CONTAMINATED" tape and stop the line. 2. **Log Incident:** Record batch number, time, and cross-contact source in the Kitchen Shift Log. 3. **Repurpose or Dispose:** The batch cannot be sold under standard labeling. Relabel it internally as staff product with a full allergen declaration, or discard it. 4. **Notification:** Inform the Head Baker and Quality Lead before shift conclusion. 5. **Customer-Facing Incident (Reported Reaction):** - Advise the customer to seek medical attention immediately, and call 911 for breathing difficulty or anaphylaxis. - Record the product, purchase time, and batch code. - Escalate to the Quality Lead within 1 hour. Pull and quarantine remaining units from the same batch. 6. **Root-Cause Review:** Within 72 hours, the Quality Lead documents the cause, the corrective action, and any retraining."}, {"source": "ALLERGEN_SAFETY_PROTOCOL.md", "quote": "- Every retail item carries a label with ingredients and a "Contains" statement. - A posted notice at the counter and on the website reads: *"Our facility is not celiac-safe. All items may contain traces of wheat, tree nuts, sesame, dairy, and eggs."* - Customers with allergies are never told an item is "safe". They are told what is in it and what is nearby. - Any question we cannot answer from the allergen matrix is passed to the Head Baker, and no guess is offered."}]

