[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-004",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "Do you have a nut-free or sesame-free bread?",
    "answer": "Several breads contain no nut or sesame ingredients, such as the Country Sourdough and Spelt Boule. We bake plain loaves first, at 2:00 AM, before seeded and nut items at 4:00 AM, and we sanitize at 12:00 PM and 8:00 PM. Shared ovens and airborne particles mean we cannot guarantee a nut-free or sesame-free product, so people with severe allergies should not rely on us.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-003",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "What is in your sourdough bread?",
    "answer": "Our core breads contain only flour (stone-milled in-house or from regional growers), water, wild sourdough starter, and sea salt. We use no commercial yeast, dough conditioners, preservatives, or artificial stabilizers. Seeded and enriched items add ingredients such as sesame, walnuts, cherries, or honey, and each item's label lists everything in it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "BREAD_STORAGE_AND_REVIVAL.md", "quote": "Commercial bread uses mono- and diglycerides and chemical preservatives. Cinder & Salt sourdough contains only flour, water, and sea salt. - **Starch Retrogradation:** Staling is not simply drying out. When bread cools after baking, the gelatinized starch molecules gradually recrystallize and push moisture out of the crumb, which makes it firm and leathery. - **The Refrigerator Trap:** Refrigeration temperatures (35°F–42°F / 1°C–5°C) **accelerate retrogradation by up to 300%**. *Never store fresh artisan bread in the refrigerator.* - **Why Sourdough Lasts Longer:** Natural acids from wild fermentation slow mold and retain moisture, which is why a high-hydration loaf like our Country Sourdough (78% hydration) usually stays pleasant for 4 to 5 days. - **Crust Moisture:** Crust softens as moisture migrates outward. That is normal, and it can be reversed (see Section 3)."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-003",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "What is in your sourdough bread?",
    "answer": "Our core breads contain only flour (stone-milled in-house or from regional growers), water, wild sourdough starter, and sea salt. We use no commercial yeast, dough conditioners, preservatives, or artificial stabilizers. Seeded and enriched items add ingredients such as sesame, walnuts, cherries, or honey, and each item's label lists everything in it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-004",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "Do you have a nut-free or sesame-free bread?",
    "answer": "Several breads contain no nut or sesame ingredients, such as the Country Sourdough and Spelt Boule. We bake plain loaves first, at 2:00 AM, before seeded and nut items at 4:00 AM, and we sanitize at 12:00 PM and 8:00 PM. Shared ovens and airborne particles mean we cannot guarantee a nut-free or sesame-free product, so people with severe allergies should not rely on us.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "ALLERGEN_SAFETY_PROTOCOL.md", "quote": "Cinder & Salt Bakery operates an open-concept bakery and an active stone mill. We mill whole grains (wheat, rye, spelt, einkorn, Red Fife) on-site every week. - **Gluten Presence:** Fine flour particles remain airborne throughout the facility 24 hours a day. No wall, bench, or schedule fully removes them. - **Celiac Disclaimer:** While some items are prepared without gluten-containing ingredients, **our facility is NOT celiac-safe**. We do not produce certified gluten-free products. Customers with Celiac Disease, severe gluten intolerance, or wheat allergy should not consume our products. - **Fermentation Is Not a Safety Claim:** Our 24–36 hour cold fermentation breaks down some starches and phytic acid and makes bread gentler for many people. It does **not** reduce gluten to a celiac-safe level (the regulatory threshold is under 20 ppm). We never market it as doing so. - **Staff Script:** "We're an active stone mill, so flour is in the air all day. We can't make a celiac-safe promise, and we'd rather tell you that honestly than risk your health.""}, {"source": "BREAD_STORAGE_AND_REVIVAL.md", "quote": "**Cinder & Salt Bakery** — *Wild Yeast. Heritage Grain. Honest Craft.* Our loaves contain only flour, water, and sea salt, with no preservatives. That is what makes them honest, and it also means they need a little care."}]

