    "answer": "Report missing, damaged, or unsatisfactory items within 12 hours of the delivery drop, and include cross-section photos. Approved claims are credited to your next invoice. Claims made after 12 hours cannot be accepted.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "CATERING_AND_CUSTOM_CAKES.md", "quote": "- **Fee:** $45.00 per tasting box (includes 4 sourdough cake options and 3 seasonal buttercreams/preserves). - **Credit:** The $45.00 fee is credited toward any final catering contract exceeding **$300.00**. - **Pickup Schedule:** Boxes are prepared on the 1st and 3rd Saturday of every month and are available for pickup between 10:00 AM and 1:00 PM. - **Reservation:** Tasting boxes must be reserved at least 7 days in advance. Unclaimed boxes are not held past 1:00 PM. - **Allergen Note:** Tasting boxes are produced in our standard facility. Tree nuts, dairy, eggs, wheat, and sesame may be present. Our facility is **not celiac-safe**."}, {"source": "CATERING_AND_CUSTOM_CAKES.md", "quote": "- **Delivery Fee:** $35.00 within Zone A (Urban Core) and $65.00 within Zone B (Outer Metro). Locations beyond our zones are quoted individually. - **Delivery Window:** We deliver and set up during a 2-hour window agreed in your contract, finishing at least 90 minutes before service. - **Venue Requirements:** A level table, shade, and a clear loading path. A refrigerated space within the venue is strongly recommended for tiered cakes. - **Tiered Cakes:** Cakes of three or more tiers are assembled on site by a staff member, and an on-site fee of $100.00 applies. - **Equipment:** Stands, boards, and linens are provided on loan with a refundable $75.00 deposit. They must be returned within 5 days. - **Closed Mondays:** Delivery and pickup are not available on Mondays."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-004",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "Do you have a nut-free or sesame-free bread?",
    "answer": "Several breads contain no nut or sesame ingredients, such as the Country Sourdough and Spelt Boule. We bake plain loaves first, at 2:00 AM, before seeded and nut items at 4:00 AM, and we sanitize at 12:00 PM and 8:00 PM. Shared ovens and airborne particles mean we cannot guarantee a nut-free or sesame-free product, so people with severe allergies should not rely on us.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-003",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "What is in your sourdough bread?",
    "answer": "Our core breads contain only flour (stone-milled in-house or from regional growers), water, wild sourdough starter, and sea salt. We use no commercial yeast, dough conditioners, preservatives, or artificial stabilizers. Seeded and enriched items add ingredients such as sesame, walnuts, cherries, or honey, and each item's label lists everything in it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "BREAD_STORAGE_AND_REVIVAL.md", "quote": "Our products contain wheat or rye and may contain traces of tree nuts, sesame, dairy, and eggs. Our facility is **not celiac-safe**. See `ALLERGEN_SAFETY_PROTOCOL.md`."}, {"source": "ALLERGEN_SAFETY_PROTOCOL.md", "quote": "Cinder & Salt Bakery operates an open-concept bakery and an active stone mill. We mill whole grains (wheat, rye, spelt, einkorn, Red Fife) on-site every week. - **Gluten Presence:** Fine flour particles remain airborne throughout the facility 24 hours a day. No wall, bench, or schedule fully removes them. - **Celiac Disclaimer:** While some items are prepared without gluten-containing ingredients, **our facility is NOT celiac-safe**. We do not produce certified gluten-free products. Customers with Celiac Disease, severe gluten intolerance, or wheat allergy should not consume our products. - **Fermentation Is Not a Safety Claim:** Our 24–36 hour cold fermentation breaks down some starches and phytic acid and makes bread gentler for many people. It does **not** reduce gluten to a celiac-safe level (the regulatory threshold is under 20 ppm). We never market it as doing so. - **Staff Script:** "We're an active stone mill, so flour is in the air all day. We can't make a celiac-safe promise, and we'd rather tell you that honestly than risk your health.""}]

[{"source": "CATERING_AND_CUSTOM_CAKES.md", "quote": "- **Deposit:** 50% non-refundable deposit required at contract signing to reserve the event date. - **Final Balance:** Remaining balance must be paid in full 14 days prior to the event date. - **Cancellations:** - 30+ days prior: deposit retained. - 14–29 days prior: 50% of contract value retained. - Under 14 days: 100% of contract value retained. - **Guest Count Changes:** Final guest count is due 14 days before the event. It can increase by up to 10% within that window, subject to capacity. It cannot decrease after that date."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
