}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_ORDERING_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Our sourdough breads undergo a mandatory 24-to-36-hour cold fermentation cycle. Because we use no commercial yeast or dough accelerants, **all wholesale orders require a strict 48-hour advance notice**. - **Standing Order Freeze:** Standing orders lock at **2:00 PM** two days prior to delivery. - **Order Modifications:** Additions or reductions must be submitted through the B2B Portal before the 2:00 PM cutoff. Late modifications cannot be accommodated, because the dough is already mixed and committed. - **No Same-Day or Next-Day Orders:** We do not offer rush orders at any price. | Order Placed By (2:00 PM) | Fermentation & Proofing Window | Delivery Window | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | **Sunday** | Monday | **Tuesday Morning** | | **Monday** | Tuesday | **Wednesday Morning** | | **Tuesday** | Wednesday | **Thursday Morning** | | **Wednesday** | Thursday | **Friday Morning** | | **Thursday** | Friday | **Saturday Morning** | | **Friday** | Saturday | **Sunday Morning** | *Table Summary:* [1. The 48-Hour Fermentation Lead Time Rule] - Order Placed By (2:00 PM): Sunday | Fermentation & Proofing Window: Monday | Delivery Window: Tuesday Morning - Order Placed By (2:00 PM): Monday | Fermentation & Proofing Window: Tuesday | Delivery Window: Wednesday Morning - Order Placed By (2:00 PM): Tuesday | Fermentation & Proofing Window: Wednesday | Delivery Window: Thursday Morning - Order Placed By (2:00 PM): Wednesday | Fermentation & Proofing Window: Thursday | Delivery Window: Friday Morning - Order Placed By (2:00 PM): Thursday | Fermentation & Proofing Window: Friday | Delivery Window: Saturday Morning - Order Placed By (2:00 PM): Friday | Fermentation & Proofing Window: Saturday | Delivery Window: Sunday Morning *Note: Retail counter and delivery routes are closed on Mondays. Orders placed on Saturday before 2:00 PM are treated as placed for Monday and are not deliverable. They roll to the Sunday cutoff and deliver Tuesday.*"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAT-001",
    "category": "Catering & Events",
    "question": "How far in advance do I need to book a wedding cake or dessert table?",
    "answer": "We require a minimum of 6 weeks notice for wedding orders and large event catering (100+ guests), 14 days for smaller custom celebratory cakes, and 7 days for small wholesale event trays. Peak wedding season dates (May-October) can close up to 6 months ahead, so early booking is recommended.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CATERING_AND_CUSTOM_CAKES.md", "quote": "- **Delivery Fee:** $35.00 within Zone A (Urban Core) and $65.00 within Zone B (Outer Metro). Locations beyond our zones are quoted individually. - **Delivery Window:** We deliver and set up during a 2-hour window agreed in your contract, finishing at least 90 minutes before service. - **Venue Requirements:** A level table, shade, and a clear loading path. A refrigerated space within the venue is strongly recommended for tiered cakes. - **Tiered Cakes:** Cakes of three or more tiers are assembled on site by a staff member, and an on-site fee of $100.00 applies. - **Equipment:** Stands, boards, and linens are provided on loan with a refundable $75.00 deposit. They must be returned within 5 days. - **Closed Mondays:** Delivery and pickup are not available on Mondays."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAT-004",
    "category": "Catering & Events",
    "question": "Can my buttercream cake be displayed outdoors in summer?",
    "answer": "Swiss meringue buttercream softens at 72\u00b0F (22\u00b0C) and collapses above 80\u00b0F (27\u00b0C). Above 72\u00b0F (22\u00b0C), outdoor display is limited to 2 hours maximum, and the cake must stay in complete shade because direct sunlight can cause collapse within 15 minutes. For hot events, ask us about a naked or fondant-finished cake.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CATERING_AND_CUSTOM_CAKES.md", "quote": "- **Weddings & Large Events (100+ guests):** Minimum **6 weeks** notice required. Peak-season dates (May–October) close up to 6 months in advance. - **Bespoke Celebratory Cakes:** Minimum **14 days** notice required. - **Small Wholesale Event Trays:** Minimum **7 days** notice required. - **Rush Requests:** We cannot accommodate bookings inside these windows. Our sourdough cake layers and laminated doughs need 18–36 hours of fermentation, and decorating takes more time on top of that."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAT-003",
    "category": "Catering & Events",
    "question": "What are your deposit and cancellation terms for events?",
    "answer": "A 50% non-refundable deposit is due at contract signing, and the balance is due 14 days before the event. If you cancel 30 or more days ahead we keep the deposit. If you cancel 14-29 days ahead we retain 50% of the contract value, and under 14 days we retain 100%.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAT-001",
    "category": "Catering & Events",
    "question": "How far in advance do I need to book a wedding cake or dessert table?",
    "answer": "We require a minimum of 6 weeks notice for wedding orders and large event catering (100+ guests), 14 days for smaller custom celebratory cakes, and 7 days for small wholesale event trays. Peak wedding season dates (May-October) can close up to 6 months ahead, so early booking is recommended.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CATERING_AND_CUSTOM_CAKES.md", "quote": "- **Weddings & Large Events (100+ guests):** Minimum **6 weeks** notice required. Peak-season dates (May–October) close up to 6 months in advance. - **Bespoke Celebratory Cakes:** Minimum **14 days** notice required. - **Small Wholesale Event Trays:** Minimum **7 days** notice required. - **Rush Requests:** We cannot accommodate bookings inside these windows. Our sourdough cake layers and laminated doughs need 18–36 hours of fermentation, and decorating takes more time on top of that."}, {"source": "CATERING_AND_CUSTOM_CAKES.md", "quote": "- **Deposit:** 50% non-refundable deposit required at contract signing to reserve the event date. - **Final Balance:** Remaining balance must be paid in full 14 days prior to the event date. - **Cancellations:** - 30+ days prior: deposit retained. - 14–29 days prior: 50% of contract value retained. - Under 14 days: 100% of contract value retained. - **Guest Count Changes:** Final guest count is due 14 days before the event. It can increase by up to 10% within that window, subject to capacity. It cannot decrease after that date."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-003",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "What is in your sourdough bread?",
    "answer": "Our core breads contain only flour (stone-milled in-house or from regional growers), water, wild sourdough starter, and sea salt. We use no commercial yeast, dough conditioners, preservatives, or artificial stabilizers. Seeded and enriched items add ingredients such as sesame, walnuts, cherries, or honey, and each item's label lists everything in it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ALG-004",
    "category": "Allergens & Ingredients",
    "question": "Do you have a nut-free or sesame-free bread?",
    "answer": "Several breads contain no nut or sesame ingredients, such as the Country Sourdough and Spelt Boule. We bake plain loaves first, at 2:00 AM, before seeded and nut items at 4:00 AM, and we sanitize at 12:00 PM and 8:00 PM. Shared ovens and airborne particles mean we cannot guarantee a nut-free or sesame-free product, so people with severe allergies should not rely on us.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "ALLERGEN_SAFETY_PROTOCOL.md", "quote": "- Every retail item carries a label with ingredients and a "Contains" statement. - A posted notice at the counter and on the website reads: *"Our facility is not celiac-safe. All items may contain traces of wheat, tree nuts, sesame, dairy, and eggs."* - Customers with allergies are never told an item is "safe". They are told what is in it and what is nearby. - Any question we cannot answer from the allergen matrix is passed to the Head Baker, and no guess is offered."}, {"source": "BREAD_STORAGE_AND_REVIVAL.md", "quote": "Our products contain wheat or rye and may contain traces of tree nuts, sesame, dairy, and eggs. Our facility is **not celiac-safe**. See `ALLERGEN_SAFETY_PROTOCOL.md`."}]

