[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ORD-002",
    "category": "Orders & Shipping",
    "question": "What is your return policy?",
    "answer": "A 45-day field trial. Return unwashed items in original condition with tags attached for a full refund to your original payment method. There are no restocking fees, and inspections are done within 3 business days of receipt. Domestic return shipping is $7.95 deducted from the refund, except for exchanges and defects.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "1. Open the customer portal and select **Start a Return** with your order number. 2. Choose Return or Exchange and a reason. 3. Print the prepaid label (domestic) or show the QR code at a carrier drop-off. 4. Pack the item with tags and ship within 7 days of generating the label. 5. Track your return through the portal. - **Domestic Returns:** Return shipping is deducted from refunds ($7.95 flat), except for exchanges and defective items, which are free. - **International Returns:** Customer pays return shipping, and duties and taxes are not refundable."}, {"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "Complimentary prepaid digital shipping labels are generated automatically via our customer portal for all domestic size and color exchanges. - We ship the replacement when the carrier shows your original item in transit **if** your account is in good standing, or when we receive it. - If the replacement costs more, we charge the difference. If it costs less, we refund the difference. - One free exchange per item. Further exchanges carry a $7.95 shipping charge. - Exchanges are subject to stock availability. If your size is out, we refund in full."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ORD-003",
    "category": "Orders & Shipping",
    "question": "How do I exchange for a different size?",
    "answer": "Start the exchange in the customer portal. A prepaid digital label is generated automatically for domestic size and color exchanges. Your first exchange per item is free.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-004",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "Can I machine wash my waxed canvas coat?",
    "answer": "No. Machine washing or heat drying strips the wax and ruins the water resistance. Brush off dry mud, spot clean with cold water and a soft brush, and air dry. If you already washed it, you can rewax it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-005",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "How do I rewax my coat?",
    "answer": "Clean the canvas with cold water and a soft brush, then let it dry. Rub a paraffin/beeswax bar over the weave in circular motions, then melt it in with a hairdryer on medium or a heat gun on low, held 4 to 6 inches away. Cure it in a cool, dry place for 24 hours.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Rewax once a year, or seasonally for heavy use, or whenever water stops beading. 1. **Clean:** Remove debris using cold water and a soft brush. Let the canvas dry completely. 2. **Apply:** Rub a paraffin/beeswax bar evenly across the canvas weave using circular motions. Focus on seams, shoulders, elbows, and pocket flaps. Use about **one 3 oz bar per coat**. 3. **Melt:** Use a heat gun on its low setting or a hairdryer on medium heat, held **4 to 6 inches (10 to 15 cm)** from the fabric, to melt the wax into the fibers. Keep it moving. Do not exceed about **150°F (65°C)** at the fabric surface. 4. **Even Out:** Wipe off any pooling wax with a clean cloth while it's warm. 5. **Cure:** Allow the canvas to cure flat or hanging in a cool, dry area for **24 hours**. Test on a hidden area first. Fresh wax may darken the canvas slightly."}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "| Mistake | What Happens | Fix | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | Washing a waxed coat in a machine | Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Rewax (Section 2) | | Drying boots by a fire | Leather shrinks and cracks | Replace; prevention only | | Over-oiling | Leather goes soft and sags | Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months | | Storing damp | Mold and mildew | Brush off, dry, and see `REPAIR_POLICY.md` for exclusions | *Table Summary:* [5. Common Mistakes] - Mistake: Washing a waxed coat in a machine | What Happens: Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Fix: Rewax (Section 2) - Mistake: Drying boots by a fire | What Happens: Leather shrinks and cracks | Fix: Replace; prevention only - Mistake: Over-oiling | What Happens: Leather goes soft and sags | Fix: Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months - Mistake: Storing damp | What Happens: Mold and mildew | Fix: Brush off, dry, and see REPAIR_POLICY.md for exclusions Need help? Contact our support team, and we'll walk you through it."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-004",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "Do you handle corporate gifting and tax-exempt purchases?",
    "answer": "Yes, for orders of 25 or more units. Tax-exempt buyers must provide a valid certificate before invoicing. Your account manager will help with gift packaging and delivery schedules.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-001",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "Can we deboss our company logo onto wholesale leather field notebooks?",
    "answer": "Yes. We offer custom hot-stamp debossing on orders meeting our Tier 1 MOQ of 25 units. A one-time $150 brass die tooling fee applies, and artwork must be supplied as a vectorized PDF or AI file.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "Hot-stamp custom logo debossing is available across all leather goods. Co-branded apparel patches are available for Tier 2 and 3 accounts. - **Artwork:** Vector files (.AI or .PDF) are required. Raster files (JPG/PNG) are not accepted. - **Tool-and-Die Fee:** A one-time **$150 tool-and-die brass mold fee** applies per custom artwork submission. Reorders using the same die are free. - **Size Limits:** Maximum deboss area is **2.5 in. × 1.25 in.** on belts and **3 in. × 3 in.** on notebooks and wallets. Minimum line weight is 0.5 pt (1 mm gap between elements). - **Stamp Temperature:** Stamps are applied at roughly **230°F–260°F (110°C–127°C)**. - **Proof Approval:** A digital proof is sent within 3 business days of artwork receipt, and a physical sample deboss is available for $35.00. Production starts only after written proof approval. - **Brand Compliance:** We reserve the right to decline artwork that infringes a trademark or conflicts with our brand. - Custom branded goods are **final sale**."}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "1. Submit the commercial account application (business name, EIN, resale certificate or tax-exempt form if applicable, and trade references). 2. Credit check and review: **3 to 5 business days**. 3. Account manager assigned and portal access granted. Tax-exempt buyers must provide a valid certificate before invoicing. Orders shipped without a certificate are taxed where applicable."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ORD-005",
    "category": "Orders & Shipping",
    "question": "My package arrived damaged or with the wrong item.",
    "answer": "Contact us within 14 days of delivery with photos. We ship a replacement or refund in full with free return shipping.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ORD-004",
    "category": "Orders & Shipping",
    "question": "Which items can't be returned?",
    "answer": "Custom monogrammed leather goods, altered sleeve hems, factory seconds, archived sale batches marked Final Sale, and gift cards. These are still covered by the Heritage Guarantee for defects.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "If you receive the wrong item or one damaged in transit, contact us within **14 days** of delivery with photos. We ship a replacement or refund in full, with free return shipping."}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. **Photo Triage:** Submit clear photos of the damage (close-up plus full item, in daylight) through the customer intake portal. 2. **RMA Issuance:** Receive a Return Merchandise Authorization (RMA) number within **24 hours** (business hours, Mon–Fri). Write the RMA number on the outside of the box. 3. **Incoming Shipping:** Ship the gear to our bench workshop. The customer covers incoming shipping. 4. **Bench Repair:** Our craftsmen repair the item using original heavy-gauge thread and solid brass hardware. Average repair cycle is **10–14 business days** from receipt. 5. **Return Shipping:** The restored item is returned with complimentary ground freight (typically 3 to 7 days, depending on where you are). **Before You Ship** - Empty the pockets and remove personal items. - Do not wash the garment. Dirty is fine. Washing can hide or worsen the damage. - Pack in a sturdy box or mailer. We recommend tracked shipping with insurance."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-005",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "My coat is damaged beyond repair. What are my options?",
    "answer": "When structural repair would compromise safety or integrity, you receive a 40% trade-in credit toward a replacement item, valid for 12 months. A bench craftsperson makes the repair-versus-replace call and we explain it with photos.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-005",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "How do I rewax my coat?",
    "answer": "Clean the canvas with cold water and a soft brush, then let it dry. Rub a paraffin/beeswax bar over the weave in circular motions, then melt it in with a hairdryer on medium or a heat gun on low, held 4 to 6 inches away. Cure it in a cool, dry place for 24 hours.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "| Mistake | What Happens | Fix | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | Washing a waxed coat in a machine | Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Rewax (Section 2) | | Drying boots by a fire | Leather shrinks and cracks | Replace; prevention only | | Over-oiling | Leather goes soft and sags | Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months | | Storing damp | Mold and mildew | Brush off, dry, and see `REPAIR_POLICY.md` for exclusions | *Table Summary:* [5. Common Mistakes] - Mistake: Washing a waxed coat in a machine | What Happens: Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Fix: Rewax (Section 2) - Mistake: Drying boots by a fire | What Happens: Leather shrinks and cracks | Fix: Replace; prevention only - Mistake: Over-oiling | What Happens: Leather goes soft and sags | Fix: Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months - Mistake: Storing damp | What Happens: Mold and mildew | Fix: Brush off, dry, and see REPAIR_POLICY.md for exclusions Need help? Contact our support team, and we'll walk you through it."}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "- **Patina is character, not a defect.** Scratches, darkening, creases, and fading are part of the gear's life. - **Neglect:** Gear left wet and balled up for weeks, mold growth, or leather cracked from never being conditioned is not covered. We will still quote you a paid repair. - **Abuse:** Cutting, burning, using a coat as a tow strap, or hitting a belt with an industrial tool is not "regular field use". - **Third-party work:** A tailor re-stitching a seam voids coverage for that seam only. The rest of the item stays covered."}]

[{"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- Store gear in **breathable canvas storage bags** in well-ventilated spaces. Avoid plastic bags and sealed containers. - Keep the temperature between 50°F and 75°F (10°C and 24°C) and relative humidity under 60% where possible. - Avoid direct UV sunlight, which fades and dries both canvas and leather, and avoid damp basements, which promote mold growth and leather degradation. - Store coats on a wide hanger. Fold waxed canvas as little as possible, because hard creases can crack the wax. - Before storage, make sure everything is completely dry."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-002",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "Is waxed canvas waterproof?",
    "answer": "Water resistant, not waterproof. Waxed canvas sheds rain and snow well, but a sustained downpour will eventually soak through. Rewax once a year, or when water stops beading, to keep it shedding water.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-004",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "Can I machine wash my waxed canvas coat?",
    "answer": "No. Machine washing or heat drying strips the wax and ruins the water resistance. Brush off dry mud, spot clean with cold water and a soft brush, and air dry. If you already washed it, you can rewax it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Rewax once a year, or seasonally for heavy use, or whenever water stops beading. 1. **Clean:** Remove debris using cold water and a soft brush. Let the canvas dry completely. 2. **Apply:** Rub a paraffin/beeswax bar evenly across the canvas weave using circular motions. Focus on seams, shoulders, elbows, and pocket flaps. Use about **one 3 oz bar per coat**. 3. **Melt:** Use a heat gun on its low setting or a hairdryer on medium heat, held **4 to 6 inches (10 to 15 cm)** from the fabric, to melt the wax into the fibers. Keep it moving. Do not exceed about **150°F (65°C)** at the fabric surface. 4. **Even Out:** Wipe off any pooling wax with a clean cloth while it's warm. 5. **Cure:** Allow the canvas to cure flat or hanging in a cool, dry area for **24 hours**. Test on a hidden area first. Fresh wax may darken the canvas slightly."}]

