}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-001",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "Can we deboss our company logo onto wholesale leather field notebooks?",
    "answer": "Yes. We offer custom hot-stamp debossing on orders meeting our Tier 1 MOQ of 25 units. A one-time $150 brass die tooling fee applies, and artwork must be supplied as a vectorized PDF or AI file.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "Hot-stamp custom logo debossing is available across all leather goods. Co-branded apparel patches are available for Tier 2 and 3 accounts. - **Artwork:** Vector files (.AI or .PDF) are required. Raster files (JPG/PNG) are not accepted. - **Tool-and-Die Fee:** A one-time **$150 tool-and-die brass mold fee** applies per custom artwork submission. Reorders using the same die are free. - **Size Limits:** Maximum deboss area is **2.5 in. × 1.25 in.** on belts and **3 in. × 3 in.** on notebooks and wallets. Minimum line weight is 0.5 pt (1 mm gap between elements). - **Stamp Temperature:** Stamps are applied at roughly **230°F–260°F (110°C–127°C)**. - **Proof Approval:** A digital proof is sent within 3 business days of artwork receipt, and a physical sample deboss is available for $35.00. Production starts only after written proof approval. - **Brand Compliance:** We reserve the right to decline artwork that infringes a trademark or conflicts with our brand. - Custom branded goods are **final sale**."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-SIZ-005",
    "category": "Sizing & Fit",
    "question": "Can I get my sleeves hemmed, and can I return a hemmed coat?",
    "answer": "Custom sleeve hemming is available in 0.5 inch increments, up to 3 inches shorter, and adds 5 to 7 business days. Altered items are final sale and excluded from the 45-day return window, so be sure of your measurements first.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "sizing_specs.json", "quote": "custom_tailoring_disclaimer:
{
    "sleeve_hem_requests": "Custom sleeve hemming is available on request on outerwear, in 0.5 inch increments, up to 3 inches shorter.",
    "impact_on_returns": "Items with altered sleeve hems are final sale and excluded from the 45-day field trial return window.",
    "lead_time_days": "Add 5 to 7 business days to standard order processing."
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ORD-002",
    "category": "Orders & Shipping",
    "question": "What is your return policy?",
    "answer": "A 45-day field trial. Return unwashed items in original condition with tags attached for a full refund to your original payment method. There are no restocking fees, and inspections are done within 3 business days of receipt. Domestic return shipping is $7.95 deducted from the refund, except for exchanges and defects.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-004",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "Do you handle corporate gifting and tax-exempt purchases?",
    "answer": "Yes, for orders of 25 or more units. Tax-exempt buyers must provide a valid certificate before invoicing. Your account manager will help with gift packaging and delivery schedules.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "- **Standard Terms:** **Net-30** upon approved credit evaluation. New accounts may begin with a credit limit of $5,000 and increase after 6 months of on-time payment. - **Customized Batches:** **50% deposit** is required on custom co-branded production batches, with the balance due Net-30 from shipment. - **Payment Methods:** ACH, wire, or check. Credit cards are accepted for orders under $2,500 with a 3% processing fee. - **Late Payments:** A 1.5% monthly fee applies after 30 days. Accounts more than 45 days past due are placed on hold."}, {"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "1. Open the customer portal and select **Start a Return** with your order number. 2. Choose Return or Exchange and a reason. 3. Print the prepaid label (domestic) or show the QR code at a carrier drop-off. 4. Pack the item with tags and ship within 7 days of generating the label. 5. Track your return through the portal. - **Domestic Returns:** Return shipping is deducted from refunds ($7.95 flat), except for exchanges and defective items, which are free. - **International Returns:** Customer pays return shipping, and duties and taxes are not refundable."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-005",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "How do I rewax my coat?",
    "answer": "Clean the canvas with cold water and a soft brush, then let it dry. Rub a paraffin/beeswax bar over the weave in circular motions, then melt it in with a hairdryer on medium or a heat gun on low, held 4 to 6 inches away. Cure it in a cool, dry place for 24 hours.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-005",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "My coat is damaged beyond repair. What are my options?",
    "answer": "When structural repair would compromise safety or integrity, you receive a 40% trade-in credit toward a replacement item, valid for 12 months. A bench craftsperson makes the repair-versus-replace call and we explain it with photos.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "| Mistake | What Happens | Fix | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | Washing a waxed coat in a machine | Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Rewax (Section 2) | | Drying boots by a fire | Leather shrinks and cracks | Replace; prevention only | | Over-oiling | Leather goes soft and sags | Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months | | Storing damp | Mold and mildew | Brush off, dry, and see `REPAIR_POLICY.md` for exclusions | *Table Summary:* [5. Common Mistakes] - Mistake: Washing a waxed coat in a machine | What Happens: Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Fix: Rewax (Section 2) - Mistake: Drying boots by a fire | What Happens: Leather shrinks and cracks | Fix: Replace; prevention only - Mistake: Over-oiling | What Happens: Leather goes soft and sags | Fix: Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months - Mistake: Storing damp | What Happens: Mold and mildew | Fix: Brush off, dry, and see REPAIR_POLICY.md for exclusions Need help? Contact our support team, and we'll walk you through it."}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "- **Patina is character, not a defect.** Scratches, darkening, creases, and fading are part of the gear's life. - **Neglect:** Gear left wet and balled up for weeks, mold growth, or leather cracked from never being conditioned is not covered. We will still quote you a paid repair. - **Abuse:** Cutting, burning, using a coat as a tow strap, or hitting a belt with an industrial tool is not "regular field use". - **Third-party work:** A tailor re-stitching a seam voids coverage for that seam only. The rest of the item stays covered."}]

