    "answer": "Yes, for orders of 25 or more units. Tax-exempt buyers must provide a valid certificate before invoicing. Your account manager will help with gift packaging and delivery schedules.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "- Wholesale orders are **final sale** except for manufacturing defects reported within 30 days. - The Heritage Guarantee covers the end user. Defective units may be repaired under `REPAIR_POLICY.md`, or credited against a future order. - Retail partners must not describe products or the guarantee in ways that differ from our published terms."}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "- **Standard Terms:** **Net-30** upon approved credit evaluation. New accounts may begin with a credit limit of $5,000 and increase after 6 months of on-time payment. - **Customized Batches:** **50% deposit** is required on custom co-branded production batches, with the balance due Net-30 from shipment. - **Payment Methods:** ACH, wire, or check. Credit cards are accepted for orders under $2,500 with a 3% processing fee. - **Late Payments:** A 1.5% monthly fee applies after 30 days. Accounts more than 45 days past due are placed on hold."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-001",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "What is covered under the Iron & Oak Heritage Guarantee?",
    "answer": "Our Heritage Guarantee covers structural failures, blown seams, detached rivets, zipper teeth failure, and broken brass hardware resulting from regular field use for the lifetime of the product. It excludes aesthetic patina, deliberate abuse, pet damage, and unauthorized third-party alterations.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "The guarantee covers the **lifetime of the product** for the original purchaser and for any later owner who can show the item's SKU and a serial/lot stamp. | Covered Under Guarantee | Excluded / Non-Covered | | :--- | :--- | | Structural seam splits and blown stitching | Normal wear, cosmetic patina, and surface scuffs | | Broken brass rivets, snaps, and buckles | Mold, pet damage (chewing, scratching), and extreme chemical exposure | | Zipper teeth failure and runner separation | Unauthorized third-party modifications or repairs | | Leather hardware failures (belt keepers, strap loops, buckle tongues) from regular field use | Deliberate abuse, prolonged submersion, and extreme neglect | | Detached pockets, ripped gussets, and failed bar-tacks at stress points | Fading, water-line marks, and wax loss (see `CARE_GUIDE.md`) | *Table Summary:* [1. Iron & Oak Heritage Guarantee Scope] - Covered Under Guarantee: Structural seam splits and blown stitching | Excluded / Non-Covered: Normal wear, cosmetic patina, and surface scuffs - Covered Under Guarantee: Broken brass rivets, snaps, and buckles | Excluded / Non-Covered: Mold, pet damage (chewing, scratching), and extreme chemical exposure - Covered Under Guarantee: Zipper teeth failure and runner separation | Excluded / Non-Covered: Unauthorized third-party modifications or repairs - Covered Under Guarantee: Leather hardware failures (belt keepers, strap loops, buckle tongues) from regular field use | Excluded / Non-Covered: Deliberate abuse, prolonged submersion, and extreme neglect - Covered Under Guarantee: Detached pockets, ripped gussets, and failed bar-tacks at stress points | Excluded / Non-Covered: Fading, water-line marks, and wax loss (see CARE_GUIDE.md)"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-006",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "Is a repair that isn't covered by the guarantee still possible?",
    "answer": "Yes. We quote the work before we start and you approve it or we send the item back unrepaired. Typical prices run $15 to $30 for a seam re-stitch and $45 to $75 for a zipper replacement. The quote is binding for 30 days.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-001",
