    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-001",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "What are your products made from?",
    "answer": "Heavy-gauge organic waxed cotton canvas, full-grain vegetable-tanned leather from domestic American hides, and solid brass hardware from certified conflict-free sources. We use exposed stress points and modular seams so the gear can be serviced for decades.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "Hot-stamp custom logo debossing is available across all leather goods. Co-branded apparel patches are available for Tier 2 and 3 accounts. - **Artwork:** Vector files (.AI or .PDF) are required. Raster files (JPG/PNG) are not accepted. - **Tool-and-Die Fee:** A one-time **$150 tool-and-die brass mold fee** applies per custom artwork submission. Reorders using the same die are free. - **Size Limits:** Maximum deboss area is **2.5 in. × 1.25 in.** on belts and **3 in. × 3 in.** on notebooks and wallets. Minimum line weight is 0.5 pt (1 mm gap between elements). - **Stamp Temperature:** Stamps are applied at roughly **230°F–260°F (110°C–127°C)**. - **Proof Approval:** A digital proof is sent within 3 business days of artwork receipt, and a physical sample deboss is available for $35.00. Production starts only after written proof approval. - **Brand Compliance:** We reserve the right to decline artwork that infringes a trademark or conflicts with our brand. - Custom branded goods are **final sale**."}, {"source": "sizing_specs.json", "quote": "custom_tailoring_disclaimer:
{
    "sleeve_hem_requests": "Custom sleeve hemming is available on request on outerwear, in 0.5 inch increments, up to 3 inches shorter.",
    "impact_on_returns": "Items with altered sleeve hems are final sale and excluded from the 45-day field trial return window.",
    "lead_time_days": "Add 5 to 7 business days to standard order processing."
}"}]

[{"source": "sizing_specs.json", "quote": "sizing_metadata:
{
    "brand": "Iron & Oak Provision Co.",
    "version": "1.2",
    "units": "inches",
    "measurement_disclaimer": "Measurements correspond to garment dimensions, not body measurements. Field Fit accommodates midweight thermal underlayers. Allow +/- 0.5 inch tolerance from hand-cut and hand-sewn production.",
    "last_updated": "2024-10-15"
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-SIZ-002",
    "category": "Sizing & Fit",
    "question": "What is Field Fit?",
    "answer": "Field Fit is relaxed through the shoulders and chest so you can wear a thermal base layer and a midweight knit underneath. Garment measurements are listed in inches in our sizing chart, so compare them to a coat that fits you well.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "sizing_specs.json", "quote": "fit_definitions:
{
    "field_fit": {
        "description": "Relaxed through shoulders and chest with room for movement and layering.",
        "layering_allowance": "Fits over a thermal base layer and a midweight knit (up to approximately 1 inch of garment ease per layer, 2 inches total)",
        "recommended_for": [
            "Timberline Waxed Chore Coat",
            "Ridgeline Wool Overshirt"
        ]
    },
    "tailored_fit": {
        "description": "Closer cut through chest and waist for single-layer wear.",
        "layering_allowance": "Fits over a light shirt or thin base layer only (approximately 1 inch of ease)",
        "note": "Size up one size to wear over a midweight knit."
    }
}"}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Wool Overshirts:** Spot clean when possible. When you must wash, hand wash in cold water (under 86°F / 30°C) with wool-safe detergent, then lay flat to dry. No tumble drying, because it shrinks wool. - **Field Pants (canvas):** Wash cold, inside out, on gentle, and hang dry. Washing will gradually remove wax from waxed finishes, so rewax afterward."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-004",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "Do you handle corporate gifting and tax-exempt purchases?",
    "answer": "Yes, for orders of 25 or more units. Tax-exempt buyers must provide a valid certificate before invoicing. Your account manager will help with gift packaging and delivery schedules.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "| Tier | Quantity (units per order) | Discount off MSRP | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | **Tier 1** | 25–99 units | 40% | | **Tier 2** | 100–499 units | 48% | | **Tier 3** | 500+ units | 55% | *Table Summary:* [1. Tiered Minimum Order Quantities (MOQ)] - Tier: Tier 1 | Quantity (units per order): 25–99 units | Discount off MSRP: 40% - Tier: Tier 2 | Quantity (units per order): 100–499 units | Discount off MSRP: 48% - Tier: Tier 3 | Quantity (units per order): 500+ units | Discount off MSRP: 55% - A "unit" is one finished item (one coat, one belt, one pair of pants). Mixed SKUs may be combined to reach a tier. - Orders of fewer than 25 units are not wholesale and are handled through retail or a gift program. - Tier pricing is locked for **12 months** from account approval, and Tier 2 and 3 accounts can set blanket orders with scheduled releases. - **Sample Program:** Up to 3 sample units are available at Tier 1 pricing, credited back if a first order of 25+ units is placed within 60 days."}, {"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "Complimentary prepaid digital shipping labels are generated automatically via our customer portal for all domestic size and color exchanges. - We ship the replacement when the carrier shows your original item in transit **if** your account is in good standing, or when we receive it. - If the replacement costs more, we charge the difference. If it costs less, we refund the difference. - One free exchange per item. Further exchanges carry a $7.95 shipping charge. - Exchanges are subject to stock availability. If your size is out, we refund in full."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-002",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "What are your wholesale tiers and discounts?",
    "answer": "Tier 1 is 25 to 99 units at 40% off MSRP. Tier 2 is 100 to 499 units at 48% off. Tier 3 is 500 or more units at 55% off. Mixed SKUs count toward the tier.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-SIZ-005",
    "category": "Sizing & Fit",
    "question": "Can I get my sleeves hemmed, and can I return a hemmed coat?",
    "answer": "Custom sleeve hemming is available in 0.5 inch increments, up to 3 inches shorter, and adds 5 to 7 business days. Altered items are final sale and excluded from the 45-day return window, so be sure of your measurements first.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-005",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "My coat is damaged beyond repair. What are my options?",
    "answer": "When structural repair would compromise safety or integrity, you receive a 40% trade-in credit toward a replacement item, valid for 12 months. A bench craftsperson makes the repair-versus-replace call and we explain it with photos.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. **Photo Triage:** Submit clear photos of the damage (close-up plus full item, in daylight) through the customer intake portal. 2. **RMA Issuance:** Receive a Return Merchandise Authorization (RMA) number within **24 hours** (business hours, Mon–Fri). Write the RMA number on the outside of the box. 3. **Incoming Shipping:** Ship the gear to our bench workshop. The customer covers incoming shipping. 4. **Bench Repair:** Our craftsmen repair the item using original heavy-gauge thread and solid brass hardware. Average repair cycle is **10–14 business days** from receipt. 5. **Return Shipping:** The restored item is returned with complimentary ground freight (typically 3 to 7 days, depending on where you are). **Before You Ship** - Empty the pockets and remove personal items. - Do not wash the garment. Dirty is fine. Washing can hide or worsen the damage. - Pack in a sturdy box or mailer. We recommend tracked shipping with insurance."}, {"source": "sizing_specs.json", "quote": "custom_tailoring_disclaimer:
{
    "sleeve_hem_requests": "Custom sleeve hemming is available on request on outerwear, in 0.5 inch increments, up to 3 inches shorter.",
    "impact_on_returns": "Items with altered sleeve hems are final sale and excluded from the 45-day field trial return window.",
    "lead_time_days": "Add 5 to 7 business days to standard order processing."
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-002",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "How do I submit a repair?",
    "answer": "Five steps. Submit clear photos through the customer intake portal, receive your RMA number within 24 hours, ship the gear to our bench workshop, wait 10 to 14 business days for repair, and we return it with complimentary ground shipping. Don't wash the item first.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. **Photo Triage:** Submit clear photos of the damage (close-up plus full item, in daylight) through the customer intake portal. 2. **RMA Issuance:** Receive a Return Merchandise Authorization (RMA) number within **24 hours** (business hours, Mon–Fri). Write the RMA number on the outside of the box. 3. **Incoming Shipping:** Ship the gear to our bench workshop. The customer covers incoming shipping. 4. **Bench Repair:** Our craftsmen repair the item using original heavy-gauge thread and solid brass hardware. Average repair cycle is **10–14 business days** from receipt. 5. **Return Shipping:** The restored item is returned with complimentary ground freight (typically 3 to 7 days, depending on where you are). **Before You Ship** - Empty the pockets and remove personal items. - Do not wash the garment. Dirty is fine. Washing can hide or worsen the damage. - Pack in a sturdy box or mailer. We recommend tracked shipping with insurance."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-001",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "Can we deboss our company logo onto wholesale leather field notebooks?",
    "answer": "Yes. We offer custom hot-stamp debossing on orders meeting our Tier 1 MOQ of 25 units. A one-time $150 brass die tooling fee applies, and artwork must be supplied as a vectorized PDF or AI file.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

