[{"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "- **Patina is character, not a defect.** Scratches, darkening, creases, and fading are part of the gear's life. - **Neglect:** Gear left wet and balled up for weeks, mold growth, or leather cracked from never being conditioned is not covered. We will still quote you a paid repair. - **Abuse:** Cutting, burning, using a coat as a tow strap, or hitting a belt with an industrial tool is not "regular field use". - **Third-party work:** A tailor re-stitching a seam voids coverage for that seam only. The rest of the item stays covered."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-006",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "My leather got soaked. What do I do?",
    "answer": "Blot it with a towel and dry it slowly at room temperature for 24 to 48 hours, away from heat and direct sun. Never use a radiator, stove, or hair dryer. Once dry, condition it. Heat-damaged leather cracks and is not covered by the guarantee.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-001",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "What is covered under the Iron & Oak Heritage Guarantee?",
    "answer": "Our Heritage Guarantee covers structural failures, blown seams, detached rivets, zipper teeth failure, and broken brass hardware resulting from regular field use for the lifetime of the product. It excludes aesthetic patina, deliberate abuse, pet damage, and unauthorized third-party alterations.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. **Photo Triage:** Submit clear photos of the damage (close-up plus full item, in daylight) through the customer intake portal. 2. **RMA Issuance:** Receive a Return Merchandise Authorization (RMA) number within **24 hours** (business hours, Mon–Fri). Write the RMA number on the outside of the box. 3. **Incoming Shipping:** Ship the gear to our bench workshop. The customer covers incoming shipping. 4. **Bench Repair:** Our craftsmen repair the item using original heavy-gauge thread and solid brass hardware. Average repair cycle is **10–14 business days** from receipt. 5. **Return Shipping:** The restored item is returned with complimentary ground freight (typically 3 to 7 days, depending on where you are). **Before You Ship** - Empty the pockets and remove personal items. - Do not wash the garment. Dirty is fine. Washing can hide or worsen the damage. - Pack in a sturdy box or mailer. We recommend tracked shipping with insurance."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
