[{"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "The following are non-returnable and excluded from refund policies: - Custom monogrammed leather goods. - Altered sleeve hems and any other custom tailoring. - Factory seconds. - Archived sale batches, labeled "Final Sale" at checkout. - Gift cards. Monogrammed or hemmed items are still covered by the Heritage Guarantee for defects."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-001",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "What is covered under the Iron & Oak Heritage Guarantee?",
    "answer": "Our Heritage Guarantee covers structural failures, blown seams, detached rivets, zipper teeth failure, and broken brass hardware resulting from regular field use for the lifetime of the product. It excludes aesthetic patina, deliberate abuse, pet damage, and unauthorized third-party alterations.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ORD-004",
    "category": "Orders & Shipping",
    "question": "Which items can't be returned?",
    "answer": "Custom monogrammed leather goods, altered sleeve hems, factory seconds, archived sale batches marked Final Sale, and gift cards. These are still covered by the Heritage Guarantee for defects.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "| Item | Who Pays | | :--- | :--- | | Incoming shipping to workshop | Customer | | Repair labor and materials (covered) | Iron & Oak | | Return ground shipping (U.S. contiguous) | Iron & Oak | | Expedited return shipping (2-day / overnight) | Customer, at carrier rates | | International return shipping | Customer | *Table Summary:* [3. Shipping & Turnaround Rules] - Item: Incoming shipping to workshop | Who Pays: Customer - Item: Repair labor and materials (covered) | Who Pays: Iron & Oak - Item: Return ground shipping (U.S. contiguous) | Who Pays: Iron & Oak - Item: Expedited return shipping (2-day / overnight) | Who Pays: Customer, at carrier rates - Item: International return shipping | Who Pays: Customer - **Repair Time:** 10–14 business days is the average. Peak periods (October through December) can add up to **5 additional business days**, and we will tell you when you get your RMA. - **Updates:** You receive an email on receipt, when repair begins, and when the item ships. - **Unclaimed Items:** Items that remain unclaimed 60 days after repair notification are donated or recycled."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-004",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "Can I machine wash my waxed canvas coat?",
    "answer": "No. Machine washing or heat drying strips the wax and ruins the water resistance. Brush off dry mud, spot clean with cold water and a soft brush, and air dry. If you already washed it, you can rewax it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-005",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "How do I rewax my coat?",
    "answer": "Clean the canvas with cold water and a soft brush, then let it dry. Rub a paraffin/beeswax bar over the weave in circular motions, then melt it in with a hairdryer on medium or a heat gun on low, held 4 to 6 inches away. Cure it in a cool, dry place for 24 hours.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Rewax once a year, or seasonally for heavy use, or whenever water stops beading. 1. **Clean:** Remove debris using cold water and a soft brush. Let the canvas dry completely. 2. **Apply:** Rub a paraffin/beeswax bar evenly across the canvas weave using circular motions. Focus on seams, shoulders, elbows, and pocket flaps. Use about **one 3 oz bar per coat**. 3. **Melt:** Use a heat gun on its low setting or a hairdryer on medium heat, held **4 to 6 inches (10 to 15 cm)** from the fabric, to melt the wax into the fibers. Keep it moving. Do not exceed about **150°F (65°C)** at the fabric surface. 4. **Even Out:** Wipe off any pooling wax with a clean cloth while it's warm. 5. **Cure:** Allow the canvas to cure flat or hanging in a cool, dry area for **24 hours**. Test on a hidden area first. Fresh wax may darken the canvas slightly."}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "| Mistake | What Happens | Fix | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | Washing a waxed coat in a machine | Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Rewax (Section 2) | | Drying boots by a fire | Leather shrinks and cracks | Replace; prevention only | | Over-oiling | Leather goes soft and sags | Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months | | Storing damp | Mold and mildew | Brush off, dry, and see `REPAIR_POLICY.md` for exclusions | *Table Summary:* [5. Common Mistakes] - Mistake: Washing a waxed coat in a machine | What Happens: Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Fix: Rewax (Section 2) - Mistake: Drying boots by a fire | What Happens: Leather shrinks and cracks | Fix: Replace; prevention only - Mistake: Over-oiling | What Happens: Leather goes soft and sags | Fix: Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months - Mistake: Storing damp | What Happens: Mold and mildew | Fix: Brush off, dry, and see REPAIR_POLICY.md for exclusions Need help? Contact our support team, and we'll walk you through it."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-001",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "Can we deboss our company logo onto wholesale leather field notebooks?",
    "answer": "Yes. We offer custom hot-stamp debossing on orders meeting our Tier 1 MOQ of 25 units. A one-time $150 brass die tooling fee applies, and artwork must be supplied as a vectorized PDF or AI file.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-001",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "What are your products made from?",
    "answer": "Heavy-gauge organic waxed cotton canvas, full-grain vegetable-tanned leather from domestic American hides, and solid brass hardware from certified conflict-free sources. We use exposed stress points and modular seams so the gear can be serviced for decades.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "Hot-stamp custom logo debossing is available across all leather goods. Co-branded apparel patches are available for Tier 2 and 3 accounts. - **Artwork:** Vector files (.AI or .PDF) are required. Raster files (JPG/PNG) are not accepted. - **Tool-and-Die Fee:** A one-time **$150 tool-and-die brass mold fee** applies per custom artwork submission. Reorders using the same die are free. - **Size Limits:** Maximum deboss area is **2.5 in. × 1.25 in.** on belts and **3 in. × 3 in.** on notebooks and wallets. Minimum line weight is 0.5 pt (1 mm gap between elements). - **Stamp Temperature:** Stamps are applied at roughly **230°F–260°F (110°C–127°C)**. - **Proof Approval:** A digital proof is sent within 3 business days of artwork receipt, and a physical sample deboss is available for $35.00. Production starts only after written proof approval. - **Brand Compliance:** We reserve the right to decline artwork that infringes a trademark or conflicts with our brand. - Custom branded goods are **final sale**."}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "| Mistake | What Happens | Fix | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | Washing a waxed coat in a machine | Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Rewax (Section 2) | | Drying boots by a fire | Leather shrinks and cracks | Replace; prevention only | | Over-oiling | Leather goes soft and sags | Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months | | Storing damp | Mold and mildew | Brush off, dry, and see `REPAIR_POLICY.md` for exclusions | *Table Summary:* [5. Common Mistakes] - Mistake: Washing a waxed coat in a machine | What Happens: Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Fix: Rewax (Section 2) - Mistake: Drying boots by a fire | What Happens: Leather shrinks and cracks | Fix: Replace; prevention only - Mistake: Over-oiling | What Happens: Leather goes soft and sags | Fix: Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months - Mistake: Storing damp | What Happens: Mold and mildew | Fix: Brush off, dry, and see REPAIR_POLICY.md for exclusions Need help? Contact our support team, and we'll walk you through it."}]

[{"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "- **Manufacturing Lead Time:** Standard **4 to 6 weeks** production window from deposit receipt (or PO approval) to freight delivery. - **In-Stock Items:** Ship within 5 business days. - **Custom Co-Branded Orders:** 4 to 6 weeks after proof approval and deposit. - **Freight:** LTL freight for orders over 150 lb. Small-parcel ground for smaller shipments. Freight is prepaid and billed on the invoice, or the customer may use their own carrier. - **Freight Free Threshold:** Tier 3 orders ship freight-free within the contiguous U.S. - **Receiving:** Inspect and note damage on the bill of lading. Report shortages within **7 days** of delivery."}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "| Tier | Quantity (units per order) | Discount off MSRP | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | **Tier 1** | 25–99 units | 40% | | **Tier 2** | 100–499 units | 48% | | **Tier 3** | 500+ units | 55% | *Table Summary:* [1. Tiered Minimum Order Quantities (MOQ)] - Tier: Tier 1 | Quantity (units per order): 25–99 units | Discount off MSRP: 40% - Tier: Tier 2 | Quantity (units per order): 100–499 units | Discount off MSRP: 48% - Tier: Tier 3 | Quantity (units per order): 500+ units | Discount off MSRP: 55% - A "unit" is one finished item (one coat, one belt, one pair of pants). Mixed SKUs may be combined to reach a tier. - Orders of fewer than 25 units are not wholesale and are handled through retail or a gift program. - Tier pricing is locked for **12 months** from account approval, and Tier 2 and 3 accounts can set blanket orders with scheduled releases. - **Sample Program:** Up to 3 sample units are available at Tier 1 pricing, credited back if a first order of 25+ units is placed within 60 days."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-004",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "Do you handle corporate gifting and tax-exempt purchases?",
    "answer": "Yes, for orders of 25 or more units. Tax-exempt buyers must provide a valid certificate before invoicing. Your account manager will help with gift packaging and delivery schedules.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ORD-001",
    "category": "Orders & Shipping",
    "question": "How long does shipping take?",
    "answer": "Standard ground is 3 to 7 business days, free over $150.00 and $9.95 otherwise. Expedited 2-day is $24.95 and overnight is $39.95. Orders placed before 2:00 PM Mountain, Monday through Friday, ship the same or next business day.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-006",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "Is a repair that isn't covered by the guarantee still possible?",
    "answer": "Yes. We quote the work before we start and you approve it or we send the item back unrepaired. Typical prices run $15 to $30 for a seam re-stitch and $45 to $75 for a zipper replacement. The quote is binding for 30 days.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. **Photo Triage:** Submit clear photos of the damage (close-up plus full item, in daylight) through the customer intake portal. 2. **RMA Issuance:** Receive a Return Merchandise Authorization (RMA) number within **24 hours** (business hours, Mon–Fri). Write the RMA number on the outside of the box. 3. **Incoming Shipping:** Ship the gear to our bench workshop. The customer covers incoming shipping. 4. **Bench Repair:** Our craftsmen repair the item using original heavy-gauge thread and solid brass hardware. Average repair cycle is **10–14 business days** from receipt. 5. **Return Shipping:** The restored item is returned with complimentary ground freight (typically 3 to 7 days, depending on where you are). **Before You Ship** - Empty the pockets and remove personal items. - Do not wash the garment. Dirty is fine. Washing can hide or worsen the damage. - Pack in a sturdy box or mailer. We recommend tracked shipping with insurance."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-002",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "How do I submit a repair?",
    "answer": "Five steps. Submit clear photos through the customer intake portal, receive your RMA number within 24 hours, ship the gear to our bench workshop, wait 10 to 14 business days for repair, and we return it with complimentary ground shipping. Don't wash the item first.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "When structural repair would compromise safety or integrity, or the item is damaged beyond functional repair, the customer receives a **40% trade-in credit** toward a replacement item. - Credit is based on the **current retail price** of the replacement item and applies to a single purchase. - Credit is valid for **12 months**. - We recycle usable brass hardware and leather offcuts. - Trade-in credit is available for items outside the guarantee as well, at the discretion of the bench lead. - The decision on repair versus replacement is made by a bench craftsperson, and we will explain it with photos."}]

