[{"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. **Photo Triage:** Submit clear photos of the damage (close-up plus full item, in daylight) through the customer intake portal. 2. **RMA Issuance:** Receive a Return Merchandise Authorization (RMA) number within **24 hours** (business hours, Mon–Fri). Write the RMA number on the outside of the box. 3. **Incoming Shipping:** Ship the gear to our bench workshop. The customer covers incoming shipping. 4. **Bench Repair:** Our craftsmen repair the item using original heavy-gauge thread and solid brass hardware. Average repair cycle is **10–14 business days** from receipt. 5. **Return Shipping:** The restored item is returned with complimentary ground freight (typically 3 to 7 days, depending on where you are). **Before You Ship** - Empty the pockets and remove personal items. - Do not wash the garment. Dirty is fine. Washing can hide or worsen the damage. - Pack in a sturdy box or mailer. We recommend tracked shipping with insurance."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-002",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "How do I submit a repair?",
    "answer": "Five steps. Submit clear photos through the customer intake portal, receive your RMA number within 24 hours, ship the gear to our bench workshop, wait 10 to 14 business days for repair, and we return it with complimentary ground shipping. Don't wash the item first.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-005",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "My coat is damaged beyond repair. What are my options?",
    "answer": "When structural repair would compromise safety or integrity, you receive a 40% trade-in credit toward a replacement item, valid for 12 months. A bench craftsperson makes the repair-versus-replace call and we explain it with photos.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "When structural repair would compromise safety or integrity, or the item is damaged beyond functional repair, the customer receives a **40% trade-in credit** toward a replacement item. - Credit is based on the **current retail price** of the replacement item and applies to a single purchase. - Credit is valid for **12 months**. - We recycle usable brass hardware and leather offcuts. - Trade-in credit is available for items outside the guarantee as well, at the discretion of the bench lead. - The decision on repair versus replacement is made by a bench craftsperson, and we will explain it with photos."}]

[{"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "The following are non-returnable and excluded from refund policies: - Custom monogrammed leather goods. - Altered sleeve hems and any other custom tailoring. - Factory seconds. - Archived sale batches, labeled "Final Sale" at checkout. - Gift cards. Monogrammed or hemmed items are still covered by the Heritage Guarantee for defects."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ORD-002",
    "category": "Orders & Shipping",
    "question": "What is your return policy?",
    "answer": "A 45-day field trial. Return unwashed items in original condition with tags attached for a full refund to your original payment method. There are no restocking fees, and inspections are done within 3 business days of receipt. Domestic return shipping is $7.95 deducted from the refund, except for exchanges and defects.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-002",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "What are your wholesale tiers and discounts?",
    "answer": "Tier 1 is 25 to 99 units at 40% off MSRP. Tier 2 is 100 to 499 units at 48% off. Tier 3 is 500 or more units at 55% off. Mixed SKUs count toward the tier.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "Test your gear for up to **45 days** from the delivery date. Items returned in **unwashed, original condition with tags attached** receive full refunds to the original payment method. **Eligible:** - Unwashed and unaltered. Light try-on and trail testing is fine. - Original tags attached. - Returned within 45 days of delivery. **Not Eligible:** - Washed, soiled, stained, or damaged items. (If gear fails from defects, use `REPAIR_POLICY.md` instead.) - Items with pet hair, strong odor, or smoke."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-004",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "Do you handle corporate gifting and tax-exempt purchases?",
    "answer": "Yes, for orders of 25 or more units. Tax-exempt buyers must provide a valid certificate before invoicing. Your account manager will help with gift packaging and delivery schedules.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ORD-003",
    "category": "Orders & Shipping",
    "question": "How do I exchange for a different size?",
    "answer": "Start the exchange in the customer portal. A prepaid digital label is generated automatically for domestic size and color exchanges. Your first exchange per item is free.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "- **Standard Terms:** **Net-30** upon approved credit evaluation. New accounts may begin with a credit limit of $5,000 and increase after 6 months of on-time payment. - **Customized Batches:** **50% deposit** is required on custom co-branded production batches, with the balance due Net-30 from shipment. - **Payment Methods:** ACH, wire, or check. Credit cards are accepted for orders under $2,500 with a 3% processing fee. - **Late Payments:** A 1.5% monthly fee applies after 30 days. Accounts more than 45 days past due are placed on hold."}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "| Tier | Quantity (units per order) | Discount off MSRP | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | **Tier 1** | 25–99 units | 40% | | **Tier 2** | 100–499 units | 48% | | **Tier 3** | 500+ units | 55% | *Table Summary:* [1. Tiered Minimum Order Quantities (MOQ)] - Tier: Tier 1 | Quantity (units per order): 25–99 units | Discount off MSRP: 40% - Tier: Tier 2 | Quantity (units per order): 100–499 units | Discount off MSRP: 48% - Tier: Tier 3 | Quantity (units per order): 500+ units | Discount off MSRP: 55% - A "unit" is one finished item (one coat, one belt, one pair of pants). Mixed SKUs may be combined to reach a tier. - Orders of fewer than 25 units are not wholesale and are handled through retail or a gift program. - Tier pricing is locked for **12 months** from account approval, and Tier 2 and 3 accounts can set blanket orders with scheduled releases. - **Sample Program:** Up to 3 sample units are available at Tier 1 pricing, credited back if a first order of 25+ units is placed within 60 days."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-004",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "Can I machine wash my waxed canvas coat?",
    "answer": "No. Machine washing or heat drying strips the wax and ruins the water resistance. Brush off dry mud, spot clean with cold water and a soft brush, and air dry. If you already washed it, you can rewax it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- Brush off dry mud and dust with a soft brush. - Spot clean with **cold water** and a soft brush or sponge. Do not use soap, detergent, or solvents, because they strip the wax. - Hang to air dry, away from direct heat. - **Never** machine wash, dry clean, or tumble dry."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-005",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "How do I rewax my coat?",
    "answer": "Clean the canvas with cold water and a soft brush, then let it dry. Rub a paraffin/beeswax bar over the weave in circular motions, then melt it in with a hairdryer on medium or a heat gun on low, held 4 to 6 inches away. Cure it in a cool, dry place for 24 hours.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Rewax once a year, or seasonally for heavy use, or whenever water stops beading. 1. **Clean:** Remove debris using cold water and a soft brush. Let the canvas dry completely. 2. **Apply:** Rub a paraffin/beeswax bar evenly across the canvas weave using circular motions. Focus on seams, shoulders, elbows, and pocket flaps. Use about **one 3 oz bar per coat**. 3. **Melt:** Use a heat gun on its low setting or a hairdryer on medium heat, held **4 to 6 inches (10 to 15 cm)** from the fabric, to melt the wax into the fibers. Keep it moving. Do not exceed about **150°F (65°C)** at the fabric surface. 4. **Even Out:** Wipe off any pooling wax with a clean cloth while it's warm. 5. **Cure:** Allow the canvas to cure flat or hanging in a cool, dry area for **24 hours**. Test on a hidden area first. Fresh wax may darken the canvas slightly."}]

[{"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "| Item | Who Pays | | :--- | :--- | | Incoming shipping to workshop | Customer | | Repair labor and materials (covered) | Iron & Oak | | Return ground shipping (U.S. contiguous) | Iron & Oak | | Expedited return shipping (2-day / overnight) | Customer, at carrier rates | | International return shipping | Customer | *Table Summary:* [3. Shipping & Turnaround Rules] - Item: Incoming shipping to workshop | Who Pays: Customer - Item: Repair labor and materials (covered) | Who Pays: Iron & Oak - Item: Return ground shipping (U.S. contiguous) | Who Pays: Iron & Oak - Item: Expedited return shipping (2-day / overnight) | Who Pays: Customer, at carrier rates - Item: International return shipping | Who Pays: Customer - **Repair Time:** 10–14 business days is the average. Peak periods (October through December) can add up to **5 additional business days**, and we will tell you when you get your RMA. - **Updates:** You receive an email on receipt, when repair begins, and when the item ships. - **Unclaimed Items:** Items that remain unclaimed 60 days after repair notification are donated or recycled."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-001",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "Can we deboss our company logo onto wholesale leather field notebooks?",
    "answer": "Yes. We offer custom hot-stamp debossing on orders meeting our Tier 1 MOQ of 25 units. A one-time $150 brass die tooling fee applies, and artwork must be supplied as a vectorized PDF or AI file.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-001",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "What is covered under the Iron & Oak Heritage Guarantee?",
    "answer": "Our Heritage Guarantee covers structural failures, blown seams, detached rivets, zipper teeth failure, and broken brass hardware resulting from regular field use for the lifetime of the product. It excludes aesthetic patina, deliberate abuse, pet damage, and unauthorized third-party alterations.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "Hot-stamp custom logo debossing is available across all leather goods. Co-branded apparel patches are available for Tier 2 and 3 accounts. - **Artwork:** Vector files (.AI or .PDF) are required. Raster files (JPG/PNG) are not accepted. - **Tool-and-Die Fee:** A one-time **$150 tool-and-die brass mold fee** applies per custom artwork submission. Reorders using the same die are free. - **Size Limits:** Maximum deboss area is **2.5 in. × 1.25 in.** on belts and **3 in. × 3 in.** on notebooks and wallets. Minimum line weight is 0.5 pt (1 mm gap between elements). - **Stamp Temperature:** Stamps are applied at roughly **230°F–260°F (110°C–127°C)**. - **Proof Approval:** A digital proof is sent within 3 business days of artwork receipt, and a physical sample deboss is available for $35.00. Production starts only after written proof approval. - **Brand Compliance:** We reserve the right to decline artwork that infringes a trademark or conflicts with our brand. - Custom branded goods are **final sale**."}]

