[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-003",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "How often should I condition my leather?",
    "answer": "Every 6 months with natural beeswax or neatsfoot oil balm. In dry climates, every 3 to 4 months. Use a dime-sized amount, work it in with a clean cloth, wait 12 hours, and buff off the excess. Don't over-oil.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-001",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "What are your products made from?",
    "answer": "Heavy-gauge organic waxed cotton canvas, full-grain vegetable-tanned leather from domestic American hides, and solid brass hardware from certified conflict-free sources. We use exposed stress points and modular seams so the gear can be serviced for decades.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Biannual Conditioning:** Apply natural beeswax or neatsfoot oil balm every **6 months** to prevent dry cracking. - Dry climates (under 30% relative humidity): condition every **3 to 4 months**. - Humid climates (over 70%): condition every 6 months, and watch for mildew. - **How to Condition:** 1. Brush off dirt and dust. 2. Wipe with a damp cloth and let it dry for 1 hour at room temperature. 3. Work a **dime-sized amount** of balm in with a clean cloth, using small circles. 4. Let it absorb for 12 hours, then buff off the excess. - Don't over-oil. Too much oil softens the leather and makes it stretch. - **Cleaning Protocol:** Wipe with a damp cloth. Use saddle soap sparingly for deep mud or grease removal, and condition afterward. - **Prohibitions:** *Strictly no machine washing or heat drying.* High temperature strips natural oils and distorts the grain. Keep leather away from radiators, wood stoves, and car dashboards. - **If It Gets Soaked:** Blot with a towel, stuff boots or belts with paper if needed, and dry slowly at room temperature, for **24 to 48 hours**, out of direct sun. Condition after it is dry. - **Patina:** Darkening, scratches, and creases are normal. Veg-tan leather ages to a deeper color the more you use it. - **Hardware:** Solid brass tarnishes. A little tarnish is fine. To clean it, use a dry cloth. Avoid chemical polishes on leather."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ORD-005",
    "category": "Orders & Shipping",
    "question": "My package arrived damaged or with the wrong item.",
    "answer": "Contact us within 14 days of delivery with photos. We ship a replacement or refund in full with free return shipping.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-005",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "My coat is damaged beyond repair. What are my options?",
    "answer": "When structural repair would compromise safety or integrity, you receive a 40% trade-in credit toward a replacement item, valid for 12 months. A bench craftsperson makes the repair-versus-replace call and we explain it with photos.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "If you receive the wrong item or one damaged in transit, contact us within **14 days** of delivery with photos. We ship a replacement or refund in full, with free return shipping."}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. **Photo Triage:** Submit clear photos of the damage (close-up plus full item, in daylight) through the customer intake portal. 2. **RMA Issuance:** Receive a Return Merchandise Authorization (RMA) number within **24 hours** (business hours, Mon–Fri). Write the RMA number on the outside of the box. 3. **Incoming Shipping:** Ship the gear to our bench workshop. The customer covers incoming shipping. 4. **Bench Repair:** Our craftsmen repair the item using original heavy-gauge thread and solid brass hardware. Average repair cycle is **10–14 business days** from receipt. 5. **Return Shipping:** The restored item is returned with complimentary ground freight (typically 3 to 7 days, depending on where you are). **Before You Ship** - Empty the pockets and remove personal items. - Do not wash the garment. Dirty is fine. Washing can hide or worsen the damage. - Pack in a sturdy box or mailer. We recommend tracked shipping with insurance."}]

[{"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "| Tier | Quantity (units per order) | Discount off MSRP | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | **Tier 1** | 25–99 units | 40% | | **Tier 2** | 100–499 units | 48% | | **Tier 3** | 500+ units | 55% | *Table Summary:* [1. Tiered Minimum Order Quantities (MOQ)] - Tier: Tier 1 | Quantity (units per order): 25–99 units | Discount off MSRP: 40% - Tier: Tier 2 | Quantity (units per order): 100–499 units | Discount off MSRP: 48% - Tier: Tier 3 | Quantity (units per order): 500+ units | Discount off MSRP: 55% - A "unit" is one finished item (one coat, one belt, one pair of pants). Mixed SKUs may be combined to reach a tier. - Orders of fewer than 25 units are not wholesale and are handled through retail or a gift program. - Tier pricing is locked for **12 months** from account approval, and Tier 2 and 3 accounts can set blanket orders with scheduled releases. - **Sample Program:** Up to 3 sample units are available at Tier 1 pricing, credited back if a first order of 25+ units is placed within 60 days."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-002",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "What are your wholesale tiers and discounts?",
    "answer": "Tier 1 is 25 to 99 units at 40% off MSRP. Tier 2 is 100 to 499 units at 48% off. Tier 3 is 500 or more units at 55% off. Mixed SKUs count toward the tier.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "- **Manufacturing Lead Time:** Standard **4 to 6 weeks** production window from deposit receipt (or PO approval) to freight delivery. - **In-Stock Items:** Ship within 5 business days. - **Custom Co-Branded Orders:** 4 to 6 weeks after proof approval and deposit. - **Freight:** LTL freight for orders over 150 lb. Small-parcel ground for smaller shipments. Freight is prepaid and billed on the invoice, or the customer may use their own carrier. - **Freight Free Threshold:** Tier 3 orders ship freight-free within the contiguous U.S. - **Receiving:** Inspect and note damage on the bill of lading. Report shortages within **7 days** of delivery."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-004",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "Do you handle corporate gifting and tax-exempt purchases?",
    "answer": "Yes, for orders of 25 or more units. Tax-exempt buyers must provide a valid certificate before invoicing. Your account manager will help with gift packaging and delivery schedules.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}]

