[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-003",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "Who pays for shipping on a repair?",
    "answer": "You cover the incoming shipping to our workshop. We cover repair labor, materials, and return ground shipping. Expedited return shipping is available at carrier rates.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. **Photo Triage:** Submit clear photos of the damage (close-up plus full item, in daylight) through the customer intake portal. 2. **RMA Issuance:** Receive a Return Merchandise Authorization (RMA) number within **24 hours** (business hours, Mon–Fri). Write the RMA number on the outside of the box. 3. **Incoming Shipping:** Ship the gear to our bench workshop. The customer covers incoming shipping. 4. **Bench Repair:** Our craftsmen repair the item using original heavy-gauge thread and solid brass hardware. Average repair cycle is **10–14 business days** from receipt. 5. **Return Shipping:** The restored item is returned with complimentary ground freight (typically 3 to 7 days, depending on where you are). **Before You Ship** - Empty the pockets and remove personal items. - Do not wash the garment. Dirty is fine. Washing can hide or worsen the damage. - Pack in a sturdy box or mailer. We recommend tracked shipping with insurance."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-002",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "How do I submit a repair?",
    "answer": "Five steps. Submit clear photos through the customer intake portal, receive your RMA number within 24 hours, ship the gear to our bench workshop, wait 10 to 14 business days for repair, and we return it with complimentary ground shipping. Don't wash the item first.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "| Item | Who Pays | | :--- | :--- | | Incoming shipping to workshop | Customer | | Repair labor and materials (covered) | Iron & Oak | | Return ground shipping (U.S. contiguous) | Iron & Oak | | Expedited return shipping (2-day / overnight) | Customer, at carrier rates | | International return shipping | Customer | *Table Summary:* [3. Shipping & Turnaround Rules] - Item: Incoming shipping to workshop | Who Pays: Customer - Item: Repair labor and materials (covered) | Who Pays: Iron & Oak - Item: Return ground shipping (U.S. contiguous) | Who Pays: Iron & Oak - Item: Expedited return shipping (2-day / overnight) | Who Pays: Customer, at carrier rates - Item: International return shipping | Who Pays: Customer - **Repair Time:** 10–14 business days is the average. Peak periods (October through December) can add up to **5 additional business days**, and we will tell you when you get your RMA. - **Updates:** You receive an email on receipt, when repair begins, and when the item ships. - **Unclaimed Items:** Items that remain unclaimed 60 days after repair notification are donated or recycled."}]

[{"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "| Mistake | What Happens | Fix | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | Washing a waxed coat in a machine | Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Rewax (Section 2) | | Drying boots by a fire | Leather shrinks and cracks | Replace; prevention only | | Over-oiling | Leather goes soft and sags | Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months | | Storing damp | Mold and mildew | Brush off, dry, and see `REPAIR_POLICY.md` for exclusions | *Table Summary:* [5. Common Mistakes] - Mistake: Washing a waxed coat in a machine | What Happens: Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Fix: Rewax (Section 2) - Mistake: Drying boots by a fire | What Happens: Leather shrinks and cracks | Fix: Replace; prevention only - Mistake: Over-oiling | What Happens: Leather goes soft and sags | Fix: Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months - Mistake: Storing damp | What Happens: Mold and mildew | Fix: Brush off, dry, and see REPAIR_POLICY.md for exclusions Need help? Contact our support team, and we'll walk you through it."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-004",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "Can I machine wash my waxed canvas coat?",
    "answer": "No. Machine washing or heat drying strips the wax and ruins the water resistance. Brush off dry mud, spot clean with cold water and a soft brush, and air dry. If you already washed it, you can rewax it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-005",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "How do I rewax my coat?",
    "answer": "Clean the canvas with cold water and a soft brush, then let it dry. Rub a paraffin/beeswax bar over the weave in circular motions, then melt it in with a hairdryer on medium or a heat gun on low, held 4 to 6 inches away. Cure it in a cool, dry place for 24 hours.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- Store gear in **breathable canvas storage bags** in well-ventilated spaces. Avoid plastic bags and sealed containers. - Keep the temperature between 50°F and 75°F (10°C and 24°C) and relative humidity under 60% where possible. - Avoid direct UV sunlight, which fades and dries both canvas and leather, and avoid damp basements, which promote mold growth and leather degradation. - Store coats on a wide hanger. Fold waxed canvas as little as possible, because hard creases can crack the wax. - Before storage, make sure everything is completely dry."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-001",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "Can we deboss our company logo onto wholesale leather field notebooks?",
    "answer": "Yes. We offer custom hot-stamp debossing on orders meeting our Tier 1 MOQ of 25 units. A one-time $150 brass die tooling fee applies, and artwork must be supplied as a vectorized PDF or AI file.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WHOLESALE_SOP.md", "quote": "Hot-stamp custom logo debossing is available across all leather goods. Co-branded apparel patches are available for Tier 2 and 3 accounts. - **Artwork:** Vector files (.AI or .PDF) are required. Raster files (JPG/PNG) are not accepted. - **Tool-and-Die Fee:** A one-time **$150 tool-and-die brass mold fee** applies per custom artwork submission. Reorders using the same die are free. - **Size Limits:** Maximum deboss area is **2.5 in. × 1.25 in.** on belts and **3 in. × 3 in.** on notebooks and wallets. Minimum line weight is 0.5 pt (1 mm gap between elements). - **Stamp Temperature:** Stamps are applied at roughly **230°F–260°F (110°C–127°C)**. - **Proof Approval:** A digital proof is sent within 3 business days of artwork receipt, and a physical sample deboss is available for $35.00. Production starts only after written proof approval. - **Brand Compliance:** We reserve the right to decline artwork that infringes a trademark or conflicts with our brand. - Custom branded goods are **final sale**."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WHO-004",
    "category": "Wholesale & B2B",
    "question": "Do you handle corporate gifting and tax-exempt purchases?",
    "answer": "Yes, for orders of 25 or more units. Tax-exempt buyers must provide a valid certificate before invoicing. Your account manager will help with gift packaging and delivery schedules.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "The following are non-returnable and excluded from refund policies: - Custom monogrammed leather goods. - Altered sleeve hems and any other custom tailoring. - Factory seconds. - Archived sale batches, labeled "Final Sale" at checkout. - Gift cards. Monogrammed or hemmed items are still covered by the Heritage Guarantee for defects."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-003",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "Who pays for shipping on a repair?",
    "answer": "You cover the incoming shipping to our workshop. We cover repair labor, materials, and return ground shipping. Expedited return shipping is available at carrier rates.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ORD-001",
    "category": "Orders & Shipping",
    "question": "How long does shipping take?",
    "answer": "Standard ground is 3 to 7 business days, free over $150.00 and $9.95 otherwise. Expedited 2-day is $24.95 and overnight is $39.95. Orders placed before 2:00 PM Mountain, Monday through Friday, ship the same or next business day.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "Complimentary prepaid digital shipping labels are generated automatically via our customer portal for all domestic size and color exchanges. - We ship the replacement when the carrier shows your original item in transit **if** your account is in good standing, or when we receive it. - If the replacement costs more, we charge the difference. If it costs less, we refund the difference. - One free exchange per item. Further exchanges carry a $7.95 shipping charge. - Exchanges are subject to stock availability. If your size is out, we refund in full."}, {"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "If you receive the wrong item or one damaged in transit, contact us within **14 days** of delivery with photos. We ship a replacement or refund in full, with free return shipping."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
