[{"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- Store gear in **breathable canvas storage bags** in well-ventilated spaces. Avoid plastic bags and sealed containers. - Keep the temperature between 50°F and 75°F (10°C and 24°C) and relative humidity under 60% where possible. - Avoid direct UV sunlight, which fades and dries both canvas and leather, and avoid damp basements, which promote mold growth and leather degradation. - Store coats on a wide hanger. Fold waxed canvas as little as possible, because hard creases can crack the wax. - Before storage, make sure everything is completely dry."}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "| Mistake | What Happens | Fix | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | Washing a waxed coat in a machine | Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Rewax (Section 2) | | Drying boots by a fire | Leather shrinks and cracks | Replace; prevention only | | Over-oiling | Leather goes soft and sags | Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months | | Storing damp | Mold and mildew | Brush off, dry, and see `REPAIR_POLICY.md` for exclusions | *Table Summary:* [5. Common Mistakes] - Mistake: Washing a waxed coat in a machine | What Happens: Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Fix: Rewax (Section 2) - Mistake: Drying boots by a fire | What Happens: Leather shrinks and cracks | Fix: Replace; prevention only - Mistake: Over-oiling | What Happens: Leather goes soft and sags | Fix: Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months - Mistake: Storing damp | What Happens: Mold and mildew | Fix: Brush off, dry, and see REPAIR_POLICY.md for exclusions Need help? Contact our support team, and we'll walk you through it."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-005",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "My coat is damaged beyond repair. What are my options?",
    "answer": "When structural repair would compromise safety or integrity, you receive a 40% trade-in credit toward a replacement item, valid for 12 months. A bench craftsperson makes the repair-versus-replace call and we explain it with photos.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-006",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "My leather got soaked. What do I do?",
    "answer": "Blot it with a towel and dry it slowly at room temperature for 24 to 48 hours, away from heat and direct sun. Never use a radiator, stove, or hair dryer. Once dry, condition it. Heat-damaged leather cracks and is not covered by the guarantee.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

