[{"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Rewax once a year, or seasonally for heavy use, or whenever water stops beading. 1. **Clean:** Remove debris using cold water and a soft brush. Let the canvas dry completely. 2. **Apply:** Rub a paraffin/beeswax bar evenly across the canvas weave using circular motions. Focus on seams, shoulders, elbows, and pocket flaps. Use about **one 3 oz bar per coat**. 3. **Melt:** Use a heat gun on its low setting or a hairdryer on medium heat, held **4 to 6 inches (10 to 15 cm)** from the fabric, to melt the wax into the fibers. Keep it moving. Do not exceed about **150°F (65°C)** at the fabric surface. 4. **Even Out:** Wipe off any pooling wax with a clean cloth while it's warm. 5. **Cure:** Allow the canvas to cure flat or hanging in a cool, dry area for **24 hours**. Test on a hidden area first. Fresh wax may darken the canvas slightly."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-005",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "How do I rewax my coat?",
    "answer": "Clean the canvas with cold water and a soft brush, then let it dry. Rub a paraffin/beeswax bar over the weave in circular motions, then melt it in with a hairdryer on medium or a heat gun on low, held 4 to 6 inches away. Cure it in a cool, dry place for 24 hours.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MAT-004",
    "category": "Product & Materials",
    "question": "Can I machine wash my waxed canvas coat?",
    "answer": "No. Machine washing or heat drying strips the wax and ruins the water resistance. Brush off dry mud, spot clean with cold water and a soft brush, and air dry. If you already washed it, you can rewax it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "| Mistake | What Happens | Fix | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | Washing a waxed coat in a machine | Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Rewax (Section 2) | | Drying boots by a fire | Leather shrinks and cracks | Replace; prevention only | | Over-oiling | Leather goes soft and sags | Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months | | Storing damp | Mold and mildew | Brush off, dry, and see `REPAIR_POLICY.md` for exclusions | *Table Summary:* [5. Common Mistakes] - Mistake: Washing a waxed coat in a machine | What Happens: Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Fix: Rewax (Section 2) - Mistake: Drying boots by a fire | What Happens: Leather shrinks and cracks | Fix: Replace; prevention only - Mistake: Over-oiling | What Happens: Leather goes soft and sags | Fix: Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months - Mistake: Storing damp | What Happens: Mold and mildew | Fix: Brush off, dry, and see REPAIR_POLICY.md for exclusions Need help? Contact our support team, and we'll walk you through it."}]

[{"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. **Photo Triage:** Submit clear photos of the damage (close-up plus full item, in daylight) through the customer intake portal. 2. **RMA Issuance:** Receive a Return Merchandise Authorization (RMA) number within **24 hours** (business hours, Mon–Fri). Write the RMA number on the outside of the box. 3. **Incoming Shipping:** Ship the gear to our bench workshop. The customer covers incoming shipping. 4. **Bench Repair:** Our craftsmen repair the item using original heavy-gauge thread and solid brass hardware. Average repair cycle is **10–14 business days** from receipt. 5. **Return Shipping:** The restored item is returned with complimentary ground freight (typically 3 to 7 days, depending on where you are). **Before You Ship** - Empty the pockets and remove personal items. - Do not wash the garment. Dirty is fine. Washing can hide or worsen the damage. - Pack in a sturdy box or mailer. We recommend tracked shipping with insurance."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-002",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "How do I submit a repair?",
    "answer": "Five steps. Submit clear photos through the customer intake portal, receive your RMA number within 24 hours, ship the gear to our bench workshop, wait 10 to 14 business days for repair, and we return it with complimentary ground shipping. Don't wash the item first.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "| Item | Who Pays | | :--- | :--- | | Incoming shipping to workshop | Customer | | Repair labor and materials (covered) | Iron & Oak | | Return ground shipping (U.S. contiguous) | Iron & Oak | | Expedited return shipping (2-day / overnight) | Customer, at carrier rates | | International return shipping | Customer | *Table Summary:* [3. Shipping & Turnaround Rules] - Item: Incoming shipping to workshop | Who Pays: Customer - Item: Repair labor and materials (covered) | Who Pays: Iron & Oak - Item: Return ground shipping (U.S. contiguous) | Who Pays: Iron & Oak - Item: Expedited return shipping (2-day / overnight) | Who Pays: Customer, at carrier rates - Item: International return shipping | Who Pays: Customer - **Repair Time:** 10–14 business days is the average. Peak periods (October through December) can add up to **5 additional business days**, and we will tell you when you get your RMA. - **Updates:** You receive an email on receipt, when repair begins, and when the item ships. - **Unclaimed Items:** Items that remain unclaimed 60 days after repair notification are donated or recycled."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-001",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "What is covered under the Iron & Oak Heritage Guarantee?",
    "answer": "Our Heritage Guarantee covers structural failures, blown seams, detached rivets, zipper teeth failure, and broken brass hardware resulting from regular field use for the lifetime of the product. It excludes aesthetic patina, deliberate abuse, pet damage, and unauthorized third-party alterations.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ORD-005",
    "category": "Orders & Shipping",
    "question": "My package arrived damaged or with the wrong item.",
    "answer": "Contact us within 14 days of delivery with photos. We ship a replacement or refund in full with free return shipping.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ORD-004",
    "category": "Orders & Shipping",
    "question": "Which items can't be returned?",
    "answer": "Custom monogrammed leather goods, altered sleeve hems, factory seconds, archived sale batches marked Final Sale, and gift cards. These are still covered by the Heritage Guarantee for defects.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "If you receive the wrong item or one damaged in transit, contact us within **14 days** of delivery with photos. We ship a replacement or refund in full, with free return shipping."}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. **Photo Triage:** Submit clear photos of the damage (close-up plus full item, in daylight) through the customer intake portal. 2. **RMA Issuance:** Receive a Return Merchandise Authorization (RMA) number within **24 hours** (business hours, Mon–Fri). Write the RMA number on the outside of the box. 3. **Incoming Shipping:** Ship the gear to our bench workshop. The customer covers incoming shipping. 4. **Bench Repair:** Our craftsmen repair the item using original heavy-gauge thread and solid brass hardware. Average repair cycle is **10–14 business days** from receipt. 5. **Return Shipping:** The restored item is returned with complimentary ground freight (typically 3 to 7 days, depending on where you are). **Before You Ship** - Empty the pockets and remove personal items. - Do not wash the garment. Dirty is fine. Washing can hide or worsen the damage. - Pack in a sturdy box or mailer. We recommend tracked shipping with insurance."}]

