    "answer": "When structural repair would compromise safety or integrity, you receive a 40% trade-in credit toward a replacement item, valid for 12 months. A bench craftsperson makes the repair-versus-replace call and we explain it with photos.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "If an item falls outside the guarantee, we will send you a quote **before** any work begins. You approve, or we return the item unrepaired. Typical repair price ranges: | Repair | Price Range | | :--- | :--- | | Seam re-stitch (up to 12 in.) | $15–$30 | | Zipper replacement | $45–$75 | | Rivet or snap replacement (each) | $5–$10 | | Belt buckle or keeper replacement | $20–$40 | | Leather re-conditioning and re-dye | $35–$60 | *Table Summary:* [4. Non-Warranty (Paid) Repairs] - Repair: Seam re-stitch (up to 12 in.) | Price Range: $15–$30 - Repair: Zipper replacement | Price Range: $45–$75 - Repair: Rivet or snap replacement (each) | Price Range: $5–$10 - Repair: Belt buckle or keeper replacement | Price Range: $20–$40 - Repair: Leather re-conditioning and re-dye | Price Range: $35–$60 Quote approval window is 10 days. Quotes are binding for 30 days."}, {"source": "CARE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "| Mistake | What Happens | Fix | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | Washing a waxed coat in a machine | Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Rewax (Section 2) | | Drying boots by a fire | Leather shrinks and cracks | Replace; prevention only | | Over-oiling | Leather goes soft and sags | Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months | | Storing damp | Mold and mildew | Brush off, dry, and see `REPAIR_POLICY.md` for exclusions | *Table Summary:* [5. Common Mistakes] - Mistake: Washing a waxed coat in a machine | What Happens: Wax strips out, water resistance gone | Fix: Rewax (Section 2) - Mistake: Drying boots by a fire | What Happens: Leather shrinks and cracks | Fix: Replace; prevention only - Mistake: Over-oiling | What Happens: Leather goes soft and sags | Fix: Let it rest and don't oil again for 6 months - Mistake: Storing damp | What Happens: Mold and mildew | Fix: Brush off, dry, and see REPAIR_POLICY.md for exclusions Need help? Contact our support team, and we'll walk you through it."}]

