    "answer": "A 45-day field trial. Return unwashed items in original condition with tags attached for a full refund to your original payment method. There are no restocking fees, and inspections are done within 3 business days of receipt. Domestic return shipping is $7.95 deducted from the refund, except for exchanges and defects.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "1. Open the customer portal and select **Start a Return** with your order number. 2. Choose Return or Exchange and a reason. 3. Print the prepaid label (domestic) or show the QR code at a carrier drop-off. 4. Pack the item with tags and ship within 7 days of generating the label. 5. Track your return through the portal. - **Domestic Returns:** Return shipping is deducted from refunds ($7.95 flat), except for exchanges and defective items, which are free. - **International Returns:** Customer pays return shipping, and duties and taxes are not refundable."}, {"source": "RETURNS_AND_EXCHANGES.md", "quote": "Complimentary prepaid digital shipping labels are generated automatically via our customer portal for all domestic size and color exchanges. - We ship the replacement when the carrier shows your original item in transit **if** your account is in good standing, or when we receive it. - If the replacement costs more, we charge the difference. If it costs less, we refund the difference. - One free exchange per item. Further exchanges carry a $7.95 shipping charge. - Exchanges are subject to stock availability. If your size is out, we refund in full."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-REP-006",
    "category": "Warranty & Repair",
    "question": "Is a repair that isn't covered by the guarantee still possible?",
    "answer": "Yes. We quote the work before we start and you approve it or we send the item back unrepaired. Typical prices run $15 to $30 for a seam re-stitch and $45 to $75 for a zipper replacement. The quote is binding for 30 days.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-PST-005",
    "category": "Post-Construction Services",
    "question": "Dust came back a few days after you cleaned. Can you return?",
    "answer": "Fine dust can resettle for several days after finishing. We offer a touch-up visit within 7 days of the final clean, and will walk the punch list with you or your contractor within 48 hours.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-SCP-001",
    "category": "Scope of Services",
    "question": "Do you clean unsealed marble or antique wood furniture?",
    "answer": "During your initial walkthrough, our team maps all sensitive surfaces. We use pH-neutral saponified soap washes for hardwood and unsealed stone. We strictly prohibit the use of acidic descalers on marble, limestone, or terrazzo to prevent etching.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WALKTHROUGH_AND_INTAKE_SOP.md", "quote": "| Item | Recorded | | :--- | :--- | | Square footage by room | Yes | | Floor types by room | Yes | | Sensitive surfaces | Yes | | Pre-existing damage (photo log) | Yes | | Pets, infants, allergies | Yes | | Access method and alarm details | Yes (encrypted) | | Parking and loading | Yes | | Water and power access | Yes | | Client-supplied cleaning products | Note: not used unless approved | *Table Summary:* [3. Walkthrough Checklist] - Item: Square footage by room | Recorded: Yes - Item: Floor types by room | Recorded: Yes - Item: Sensitive surfaces | Recorded: Yes - Item: Pre-existing damage (photo log) | Recorded: Yes - Item: Pets, infants, allergies | Recorded: Yes - Item: Access method and alarm details | Recorded: Yes (encrypted) - Item: Parking and loading | Recorded: Yes - Item: Water and power access | Recorded: Yes - Item: Client-supplied cleaning products | Recorded: Note: not used unless approved"}, {"source": "POST_CONSTRUCTION_REMEDIATION_GUIDE.md", "quote": "| Stage | Timing | | :--- | :--- | | Rough clean (Phase 1) | After trade work, before final painting touch-ups | | Final clean (Phases 2–3) | After all trades are done, no earlier than 24–48 hours after last sanding | | Touch-up visit | Within 7 days of the final clean, if needed | *Table Summary:* [5. Scheduling] - Stage: Rough clean (Phase 1) | Timing: After trade work, before final painting touch-ups - Stage: Final clean (Phases 2–3) | Timing: After all trades are done, no earlier than 24–48 hours after last sanding - Stage: Touch-up visit | Timing: Within 7 days of the final clean, if needed Dust can resettle for several days after finishing, which is why a short touch-up visit is offered."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ACC-003",
    "category": "Property Access & Security",
    "question": "What if the alarm goes off during a visit?",
    "answer": "The technician calls you and your alarm company within 5 minutes and gives the verbal passcode. False alarm dispatch fees caused by an incorrect code supplied by the client are the client's responsibility, so please keep your codes current.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ACC-001",
    "category": "Property Access & Security",
    "question": "Do I need to be home when the cleaning collective arrives?",
    "answer": "No. Most residential and commercial clients provide a smart lock code or lockbox key. Our technicians arrive within the designated arrival window, complete the service scope, re-secure all windows and doors, and set the security alarm upon departure.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "PROPERTY_ACCESS_AND_CANCELLATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "* **Digital Keypads & Smart Locks:** Preferred access method. Clients provide a unique service PIN designated exclusively for Kettle & Loom staff. We recommend a PIN that is active only during the service window. * **Physical Lockboxes:** If using physical keys, keys must remain inside a secure on-site lockbox. Technicians will not carry permanent property keys off-site. Lockbox codes are shared only with the assigned team and changed on request. * **Alarm Systems:** Alarm disarm codes and re-arming instructions must be stored in encrypted client profiles. Any false alarm dispatch fees resulting from inaccurate client codes are the client's responsibility. - Technicians disarm on arrival and re-arm on departure. If an alarm triggers, the technician calls the client and the alarm company within **5 minutes** and gives the correct passcode. - Provide your alarm company's name and the verbal passcode for dispatch. * **Departure Procedure:** Technicians re-lock all doors, close windows, set the thermostat to its original setting, turn off lights, and text a completion notice. * **Key Custody:** Access details are visible only to the Operations team and the assigned technicians. Access codes are removed from the technician's device when the contract ends. * **Garage and Gate Codes:** Provide any gate, garage, or elevator access in your profile."}, {"source": "PROPERTY_ACCESS_AND_CANCELLATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "A lockout occurs when technicians cannot enter the property within **20 minutes** of the start of the arrival window because of an incorrect code, a missing key, a deactivated PIN, or a locked interior door. - The technician tries the client's contact numbers and waits up to 20 minutes. - If entry is still not possible, the visit is recorded as a lockout and billed at **100% of the scheduled service fee**. - A one-time free rebooking is not offered for lockouts, but we are glad to help get the next visit set up. - Lockouts due to a building-management error are reviewed on a case-by-case basis."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-003",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "Do I have to pay an initial deep clean?",
    "answer": "Yes, all recurring contracts start with a foundational Initial Deep Clean. It removes buildup, limescale, and synthetic wax residue from earlier cleaners, and typically takes 2.0 to 2.5 times a regular visit. It is quoted as a fixed price during your walkthrough.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-001",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "What happens if I need to cancel my cleaning appointment tomorrow?",
    "answer": "Appointments canceled with less than 24 hours notice are subject to a 100% service fee charge because our collective members are paid for their booked time. If canceled between 24 and 48 hours in advance, a $50 administrative fee applies. Cancellations with over 48 hours notice are completely free.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "WALKTHROUGH_AND_INTAKE_SOP.md", "quote": "All recurring service contracts must undergo a foundational **Initial Deep Clean**. This baseline visit removes pre-existing buildup, limescale, and synthetic wax residues from previous chemical cleaners before beginning botanical maintenance. - **Duration:** Typically **2.0x to 2.5x** the standard maintenance time for the same square footage (for example, a 2,000 sq ft home that takes 150 minutes for maintenance will take about 5 to 6.25 hours of technician time for the deep clean). - **Added Tasks:** Interior oven and refrigerator, baseboards, door casings, window sills and tracks, cabinet interiors on request, descaling of fixtures, and detailed grout work. - **Why It Is Mandatory:** Botanical chemistry cannot lift old synthetic residues on its own, and the baseline sets a measurable standard for every visit after it. - **Short-Term Rental Properties:** A baseline deep clean is required before the first turnover. - **Pricing:** Quoted as a fixed price at the walkthrough. Rates are not charged beyond the quote unless conditions differ from the photos, and the client approves any change first."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-005",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "A cleaning product got in my eye. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Flush your eye with clean water for 10 minutes with the eyelid held open, remove contact lenses if you can, and seek medical attention if irritation persists. For ingestion, rinse the mouth and call Poison Control at 1-800-222-1222. Then contact us so we can provide the SDS and file an incident report.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-003",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "Why do you leave disinfectant wet for 10 minutes?",
    "answer": "Disinfectants only work if the surface stays visibly wet for the product's full contact time. For Bio-Shield that is 10 minutes. Wiping sooner reduces how many germs are killed. OxyPure needs 3 minutes and Citrus-Loom needs 5 minutes.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Wet dwell** means the surface stays visibly wet for the whole period. If it dries early, reapply. - Pre-clean heavy soil first, because disinfectants do not work through grease or grime. - Do not wipe Bio-Shield before 10 minutes have passed. Use a timer. - Disinfection is performed on high-touch surfaces only: toilets, handles, switches, keypads, faucets, and remotes."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-001",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "What happens if I need to cancel my cleaning appointment tomorrow?",
    "answer": "Appointments canceled with less than 24 hours notice are subject to a 100% service fee charge because our collective members are paid for their booked time. If canceled between 24 and 48 hours in advance, a $50 administrative fee applies. Cancellations with over 48 hours notice are completely free.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ACC-004",
    "category": "Property Access & Security",
    "question": "Do I need to put my dog away during cleaning?",
    "answer": "Yes. For technician safety and to prevent pets from darting out exterior doors, dogs and cats must be secured in a designated room or crate, unless we've confirmed other arrangements in writing. A technician may decline to enter if a dog is not secured, and the visit is treated as a lockout.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "PROPERTY_ACCESS_AND_CANCELLATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "We love pets, but for technician safety and to prevent pets from darting out exterior doors, dogs and cats must be secured in a designated room or crate during service unless prior written arrangements are confirmed. - Mark the room with a sign, and make sure the room has water. - Tell us about any pets that bite, escape, or react to strangers when you book. - Technicians may decline to enter a property where a dog is not secured, and the visit is treated as a lockout. - Exotic pets, reptiles, and aquariums are not touched or cleaned. - Pets must not be left in spaces with wet floors."}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- Clients with fragrance sensitivities, asthma, or chemical allergies are recorded at intake. We use unscented formulations on request. - Pets and infants should be kept out of a room while a surface is wet. Surfaces are safe for contact once dry. - We list ingredients by name and provide SDS copies to any client on request."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-005",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "A cleaning product got in my eye. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Flush your eye with clean water for 10 minutes with the eyelid held open, remove contact lenses if you can, and seek medical attention if irritation persists. For ingestion, rinse the mouth and call Poison Control at 1-800-222-1222. Then contact us so we can provide the SDS and file an incident report.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-003",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "Why do you leave disinfectant wet for 10 minutes?",
    "answer": "Disinfectants only work if the surface stays visibly wet for the product's full contact time. For Bio-Shield that is 10 minutes. Wiping sooner reduces how many germs are killed. OxyPure needs 3 minutes and Citrus-Loom needs 5 minutes.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Every product has a Safety Data Sheet (SDS) in the technician binder and the mobile app, readable offline. | Exposure | Response | | :--- | :--- | | **Inhalation** | Low-hazard, zero-VOC formulations. Move to fresh air if anyone has irritation and ventilate the room. Seek medical attention if symptoms last more than 15 minutes. | | **Eye Contact** | In case of direct splash, flush eyes with potable water for **10 minutes**, holding the eyelids open. Remove contact lenses if easy to do. Seek medical attention if irritation continues. | | **Skin Contact** | Rinse with water for **5 minutes**. Remove contaminated clothing. Seek medical advice if redness persists. | | **Ingestion** | Rinse mouth. Do not induce vomiting. Call Poison Control at **1-800-222-1222** (U.S.) and follow their directions. | *Table Summary:* [3. SDS Exposure Protocols & First Aid] - Exposure: Inhalation | Response: Low-hazard, zero-VOC formulations. Move to fresh air if anyone has irritation and ventilate the room. Seek medical attention if symptoms last more than 15 minutes. - Exposure: Eye Contact | Response: In case of direct splash, flush eyes with potable water for 10 minutes, holding the eyelids open. Remove contact lenses if easy to do. Seek medical attention if irritation continues. - Exposure: Skin Contact | Response: Rinse with water for 5 minutes. Remove contaminated clothing. Seek medical advice if redness persists. - Exposure: Ingestion | Response: Rinse mouth. Do not induce vomiting. Call Poison Control at 1-800-222-1222 (U.S.) and follow their directions. **Note:** Concentrated 3% hydrogen peroxide and 8% citric acid can irritate eyes and skin. Wear nitrile gloves and eye protection when pouring or diluting concentrates."}]

[{"source": "POST_CONSTRUCTION_REMEDIATION_GUIDE.md", "quote": "* **Equipment Standard:** Commercial HEPA vacuums certified to capture **99.97% of particulates down to 0.3 microns**. Certification labels must be on the machine, and filters are inspected before every project. * **Filter Maintenance:** Replace or clean HEPA filters when the indicator shows full, or at least every **40 hours** of use. Empty bags and canisters outdoors or into a sealed bag at the end of every shift, away from the work area. * **Air Scrubbers:** For projects with heavy dust, place a HEPA air scrubber (rated at 4+ air changes per hour for the room volume) in the room during Phase 2, and keep it running for 4 hours afterward. * **Microfiber Fold Technique:** Microfiber cloths must be folded into **8 clean quadrants** and flipped continuously to prevent spreading dry drywall dust across painted walls. - When all 8 quadrants are soiled, the cloth goes in the used pile. Never dip a used cloth back in the clean solution. - Use the multi-bucket system: one bucket of clean solution, one of rinse, and fresh cloths from a clean stack. - Use **damp**, not wet, cloths, wrung out so that no water drips. Wet cloths turn drywall dust into a paste. * **Surface Cleaner:** OxyPure, diluted to label, or plain water on delicate finishes. See `CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md`."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-PST-002",
    "category": "Post-Construction Services",
    "question": "What is a HEPA vacuum and why do you use one?",
    "answer": "A certified HEPA vacuum captures 99.97% of particles down to 0.3 microns. Household vacuums blow fine drywall dust back into the air, whereas HEPA machines trap it.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "service_scope_matrix.json", "quote": "{
    "tier_id": "TIER-PCN-04",
    "tier_name": "Post-Construction Remediation",
    "frequency_options": [
        "One-time (three phases)",
        "Touch-up visit within 7 days"
    ],
    "requires_initial_deep_clean": false,
    "zones": {
        "phase_1_rough_debris_pass": [
            "Remove construction packaging, protective films, stickers, and tape residue",
            "Scrape paint splatter with plastic blades",
            "Rough sweep floors with HEPA capture"
        ],
        "phase_2_high_to_low_hepa_vacuuming": [
            "HEPA vacuum ceiling joists, fans, HVAC diffusers, and light fixtures",
            "HEPA vacuum door casings, window tracks, and cabinet tops",
            "HEPA vacuum baseboards and floors (99.97% at 0.3 microns)"
        ],
        "phase_3_wet_microfiber_sparkle_pass": [
            "Damp wipe all surfaces with 8-quadrant folded microfiber",
            "Clean cabinet interiors, glass, and fixtures",
            "Final HEPA vacuum and white-glove inspection (3 sample points per room)"
        ]
