[{"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "* **Strict Acid Prohibition:** *Citrus-Loom Descaler and acidic solutions must NEVER be applied to unsealed natural marble, travertine, limestone, or terrazzo.* Acid etching permanently damages calcite stone. * **Hardwood Neutrality:** Wood flooring must be cleaned exclusively with pH-neutral PureLoom wash. Never saturate it with standing water. * **Granite & Quartz:** Use OxyPure only. No descaler on sealed stone unless the sealer is confirmed intact and the surface is rinsed within 5 minutes. * **Oil-Rubbed Bronze & Unlacquered Brass:** Dry microfiber only. No acids or peroxide, as they strip the finish. * **Unsealed Butcher Block:** Damp wipe with PureLoom diluted to the label ratio. Do not apply disinfectant to unsealed wood for a full dwell time. * **Wool Rugs & Natural Fibers:** Do not apply hydrogen peroxide, because it may bleach dyed fibers. Spot test first in a hidden area. Always check the client's Surface Sensitivity Map (see `WALKTHROUGH_AND_INTAKE_SOP.md`) before opening a product."}, {"source": "service_scope_matrix.json", "quote": "Cleaning of unsealed natural stone with acidic products"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-SCP-001",
    "category": "Scope of Services",
    "question": "Do you clean unsealed marble or antique wood furniture?",
    "answer": "During your initial walkthrough, our team maps all sensitive surfaces. We use pH-neutral saponified soap washes for hardwood and unsealed stone. We strictly prohibit the use of acidic descalers on marble, limestone, or terrazzo to prevent etching.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-002",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "What ingredients do you use?",
    "answer": "Bio-Shield Disinfectant uses 0.05% thymol, OxyPure uses stabilized 3% hydrogen peroxide, Citrus-Loom Descaler uses 8% food-grade citric acid, and PureLoom Floor Wash is a saponified coconut and olive oil soap. We provide Safety Data Sheets for every product on request.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "PROPERTY_ACCESS_AND_CANCELLATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "* **Digital Keypads & Smart Locks:** Preferred access method. Clients provide a unique service PIN designated exclusively for Kettle & Loom staff. We recommend a PIN that is active only during the service window. * **Physical Lockboxes:** If using physical keys, keys must remain inside a secure on-site lockbox. Technicians will not carry permanent property keys off-site. Lockbox codes are shared only with the assigned team and changed on request. * **Alarm Systems:** Alarm disarm codes and re-arming instructions must be stored in encrypted client profiles. Any false alarm dispatch fees resulting from inaccurate client codes are the client's responsibility. - Technicians disarm on arrival and re-arm on departure. If an alarm triggers, the technician calls the client and the alarm company within **5 minutes** and gives the correct passcode. - Provide your alarm company's name and the verbal passcode for dispatch. * **Departure Procedure:** Technicians re-lock all doors, close windows, set the thermostat to its original setting, turn off lights, and text a completion notice. * **Key Custody:** Access details are visible only to the Operations team and the assigned technicians. Access codes are removed from the technician's device when the contract ends. * **Garage and Gate Codes:** Provide any gate, garage, or elevator access in your profile."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ACC-001",
    "category": "Property Access & Security",
    "question": "Do I need to be home when the cleaning collective arrives?",
    "answer": "No. Most residential and commercial clients provide a smart lock code or lockbox key. Our technicians arrive within the designated arrival window, complete the service scope, re-secure all windows and doors, and set the security alarm upon departure.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ACC-004",
    "category": "Property Access & Security",
    "question": "Do I need to put my dog away during cleaning?",
    "answer": "Yes. For technician safety and to prevent pets from darting out exterior doors, dogs and cats must be secured in a designated room or crate, unless we've confirmed other arrangements in writing. A technician may decline to enter if a dog is not secured, and the visit is treated as a lockout.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "POST_CONSTRUCTION_REMEDIATION_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **White Glove Test:** A clean white microfiber cloth wiped across a horizontal surface at **3 sample locations per room** should pick up no visible dust. - **Flashlight Inspection:** A raking-light check of painted surfaces and glass at a low angle. - **Walkthrough:** The client or general contractor does a final walkthrough with the Site Lead, with a punch list completed within **48 hours**. - HVAC: Replace the system filter after the final pass. Ducts are not cleaned under this service."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-001",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "Are your cleaning products safe for homes with infants and pets?",
    "answer": "Our products are zero-VOC, plant- or mineral-derived, and EPA Design for the Environment (DfE) and Green Seal certified. Our hospital-grade disinfectant uses 0.05% thymol, a thyme extract, and kills 99.99% of bacteria and enveloped viruses on a 10-minute wet dwell. Botanical does not mean harmless, so we ask that pets and infants stay out of a room until surfaces dry.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-002",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "What ingredients do you use?",
    "answer": "Bio-Shield Disinfectant uses 0.05% thymol, OxyPure uses stabilized 3% hydrogen peroxide, Citrus-Loom Descaler uses 8% food-grade citric acid, and PureLoom Floor Wash is a saponified coconut and olive oil soap. We provide Safety Data Sheets for every product on request.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "**Kettle & Loom Cleaning Collective** — *Pure Ingredients. Meticulous Spaces. Uncompromising Clean.* This SOP supports OSHA Hazard Communication and EPA compliance. It tells our technicians what we use, how long to leave it on a surface, and what to do if something goes wrong. Botanical does not mean harmless, and we handle every product with care."}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- Clients with fragrance sensitivities, asthma, or chemical allergies are recorded at intake. We use unscented formulations on request. - Pets and infants should be kept out of a room while a surface is wet. Surfaces are safe for contact once dry. - We list ingredients by name and provide SDS copies to any client on request."}]

