[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-004",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "How do you price a cleaning?",
    "answer": "Estimates use our scope matrix and a base rate of $55.00 per technician-hour. Maintenance cleans take about 75 minutes per 1,000 sq ft, short-term rental turnovers about 110 minutes, and commercial offices about 45 minutes. You receive a fixed-price proposal after your 30-minute walkthrough.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-SCP-003",
    "category": "Scope of Services",
    "question": "Do you clean short-term rentals between guests?",
    "answer": "Yes. Our turnover service takes about 110 minutes per 1,000 sq ft per technician and includes laundering linens with hypoallergenic wash, hotel-standard bed making, restocking amenities, sanitizing high-touch surfaces, and checking for left-behind property, with photos sent when finished.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WALKTHROUGH_AND_INTAKE_SOP.md", "quote": "All recurring service contracts must undergo a foundational **Initial Deep Clean**. This baseline visit removes pre-existing buildup, limescale, and synthetic wax residues from previous chemical cleaners before beginning botanical maintenance. - **Duration:** Typically **2.0x to 2.5x** the standard maintenance time for the same square footage (for example, a 2,000 sq ft home that takes 150 minutes for maintenance will take about 5 to 6.25 hours of technician time for the deep clean). - **Added Tasks:** Interior oven and refrigerator, baseboards, door casings, window sills and tracks, cabinet interiors on request, descaling of fixtures, and detailed grout work. - **Why It Is Mandatory:** Botanical chemistry cannot lift old synthetic residues on its own, and the baseline sets a measurable standard for every visit after it. - **Short-Term Rental Properties:** A baseline deep clean is required before the first turnover. - **Pricing:** Quoted as a fixed price at the walkthrough. Rates are not charged beyond the quote unless conditions differ from the photos, and the client approves any change first."}, {"source": "service_scope_matrix.json", "quote": "{
    "name": "Interior oven or refrigerator",
    "estimated_minutes_each": 30
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ACC-005",
    "category": "Property Access & Security",
    "question": "Something in my home was damaged during a cleaning. What now?",
    "answer": "Report it within 24 hours with photos. We maintain liability insurance and bonding, and claims are reviewed within 5 business days. We will compare against the pre-existing condition photos taken at your walkthrough.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-001",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "What happens if I need to cancel my cleaning appointment tomorrow?",
    "answer": "Appointments canceled with less than 24 hours notice are subject to a 100% service fee charge because our collective members are paid for their booked time. If canceled between 24 and 48 hours in advance, a $50 administrative fee applies. Cancellations with over 48 hours notice are completely free.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "WALKTHROUGH_AND_INTAKE_SOP.md", "quote": "1. **Initial Property Audit:** Conduct a **30-minute** on-site assessment with the client or property manager. Measure and record the square footage of each room and total conditioned space, and note the number of bedrooms, bathrooms, and floor types. Confirm that the square footage on the booking is within 10% of the measured figure. 2. **Surface Sensitivity Mapping:** Log all sensitive materials (honed Carrara marble, unsealed butcher block, oil-rubbed bronze hardware, wool area rugs). Each entry has the room, material, and the approved product (see `CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md`). 3. **Pre-Existing Condition Documentation:** Photograph existing carpet stains, scratched wood floors, and chipped tiles. Upload to the client profile with a date stamp. Take at least **3 photos per room** (wide shot plus close-ups), and a photo of each existing defect with a coin or ruler for scale. 4. **Air Quality & Allergen Assessment:** Identify presence of pets, dust sensitivities, or fragrance allergies to tailor hypoallergenic essential oils or go fully unscented. 5. **Estimate & Scope Confirmation:** Generate a fixed-price proposal detailing initial deep-clean baseline hours and ongoing maintenance frequencies. The estimate uses `service_scope_matrix.json` and a base rate of $55.00 per technician-hour. **Output:** A signed Property Profile containing the sensitivity map, photo log, access and alarm details (stored encrypted), pet details, and scope."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-002",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "What is a lockout and what does it cost?",
    "answer": "A lockout means we can't enter within 20 minutes of the start of the arrival window, for example because of a wrong code or a missing key. It is billed at 100% of the scheduled service fee.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-001",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "What happens if I need to cancel my cleaning appointment tomorrow?",
    "answer": "Appointments canceled with less than 24 hours notice are subject to a 100% service fee charge because our collective members are paid for their booked time. If canceled between 24 and 48 hours in advance, a $50 administrative fee applies. Cancellations with over 48 hours notice are completely free.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "PROPERTY_ACCESS_AND_CANCELLATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "* **48-Hour Free Cancellation:** Services may be canceled or rescheduled without penalty up to **48 hours** prior to the scheduled arrival window. * **Late Cancellation (Within 24–48 Hours):** Incurs a **$50.00 administrative rescheduling fee**. * **Same-Day Cancellation / Lockout (Under 24 Hours):** Charged at **100% of the scheduled service fee**. Our collective technicians are scheduled and paid for their booked time. | Notice Given | Fee | | :--- | :--- | | More than 48 hours | $0.00 | | 24 to 48 hours | $50.00 | | Under 24 hours | 100% of scheduled service fee | | Lockout on arrival | 100% of scheduled service fee | *Table Summary:* [2. Cancellation & Rescheduling Cutoff Schedules] - Notice Given: More than 48 hours | Fee: $0.00 - Notice Given: 24 to 48 hours | Fee: $50.00 - Notice Given: Under 24 hours | Fee: 100% of scheduled service fee - Notice Given: Lockout on arrival | Fee: 100% of scheduled service fee **Cancellation Details** - Notice is counted from the start of your scheduled arrival window. - Cancel through the client portal, by phone, or by email. Messages received after business hours (6:00 PM) count as received the next business morning. - **Weather & Emergencies:** If unsafe travel conditions or a documented emergency prevent service, we reschedule without a fee. - **Short-Term Rental Turnovers:** Cancellations of a turnover tied to a booking that was itself canceled by a guest are free when notified within 24 hours of the guest's cancellation."}, {"source": "service_scope_matrix.json", "quote": "scope_matrix_metadata:
{
    "company": "Kettle & Loom Cleaning Collective",
