[{"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- All botanical concentrates must remain in labeled, UV-resistant amber dispensers at **50°F–80°F (10°C–27°C)**. - Never store in vehicles overnight, and never decant into unlabeled bottles or food containers. - Keep stored products out of direct sunlight and away from heat sources. - Rotate stock. Hydrogen peroxide has a shelf life of about 12 months from the opening date, and open dates must be written on the bottle. - Dispose of spent solutions down a sanitary drain with running water. Never pour them into storm drains."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-PST-005",
    "category": "Post-Construction Services",
    "question": "Dust came back a few days after you cleaned. Can you return?",
    "answer": "Fine dust can resettle for several days after finishing. We offer a touch-up visit within 7 days of the final clean, and will walk the punch list with you or your contractor within 48 hours.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-003",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "Why do you leave disinfectant wet for 10 minutes?",
    "answer": "Disinfectants only work if the surface stays visibly wet for the product's full contact time. For Bio-Shield that is 10 minutes. Wiping sooner reduces how many germs are killed. OxyPure needs 3 minutes and Citrus-Loom needs 5 minutes.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "**Kettle & Loom Cleaning Collective** — *Pure Ingredients. Meticulous Spaces. Uncompromising Clean.* This SOP supports OSHA Hazard Communication and EPA compliance. It tells our technicians what we use, how long to leave it on a surface, and what to do if something goes wrong. Botanical does not mean harmless, and we handle every product with care."}]

