    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Every product has a Safety Data Sheet (SDS) in the technician binder and the mobile app, readable offline. | Exposure | Response | | :--- | :--- | | **Inhalation** | Low-hazard, zero-VOC formulations. Move to fresh air if anyone has irritation and ventilate the room. Seek medical attention if symptoms last more than 15 minutes. | | **Eye Contact** | In case of direct splash, flush eyes with potable water for **10 minutes**, holding the eyelids open. Remove contact lenses if easy to do. Seek medical attention if irritation continues. | | **Skin Contact** | Rinse with water for **5 minutes**. Remove contaminated clothing. Seek medical advice if redness persists. | | **Ingestion** | Rinse mouth. Do not induce vomiting. Call Poison Control at **1-800-222-1222** (U.S.) and follow their directions. | *Table Summary:* [3. SDS Exposure Protocols & First Aid] - Exposure: Inhalation | Response: Low-hazard, zero-VOC formulations. Move to fresh air if anyone has irritation and ventilate the room. Seek medical attention if symptoms last more than 15 minutes. - Exposure: Eye Contact | Response: In case of direct splash, flush eyes with potable water for 10 minutes, holding the eyelids open. Remove contact lenses if easy to do. Seek medical attention if irritation continues. - Exposure: Skin Contact | Response: Rinse with water for 5 minutes. Remove contaminated clothing. Seek medical advice if redness persists. - Exposure: Ingestion | Response: Rinse mouth. Do not induce vomiting. Call Poison Control at 1-800-222-1222 (U.S.) and follow their directions. **Note:** Concentrated 3% hydrogen peroxide and 8% citric acid can irritate eyes and skin. Wear nitrile gloves and eye protection when pouring or diluting concentrates."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-002",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "What is a lockout and what does it cost?",
    "answer": "A lockout means we can't enter within 20 minutes of the start of the arrival window, for example because of a wrong code or a missing key. It is billed at 100% of the scheduled service fee.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-003",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "Do I have to pay an initial deep clean?",
    "answer": "Yes, all recurring contracts start with a foundational Initial Deep Clean. It removes buildup, limescale, and synthetic wax residue from earlier cleaners, and typically takes 2.0 to 2.5 times a regular visit. It is quoted as a fixed price during your walkthrough.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "PROPERTY_ACCESS_AND_CANCELLATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "* **48-Hour Free Cancellation:** Services may be canceled or rescheduled without penalty up to **48 hours** prior to the scheduled arrival window. * **Late Cancellation (Within 24–48 Hours):** Incurs a **$50.00 administrative rescheduling fee**. * **Same-Day Cancellation / Lockout (Under 24 Hours):** Charged at **100% of the scheduled service fee**. Our collective technicians are scheduled and paid for their booked time. | Notice Given | Fee | | :--- | :--- | | More than 48 hours | $0.00 | | 24 to 48 hours | $50.00 | | Under 24 hours | 100% of scheduled service fee | | Lockout on arrival | 100% of scheduled service fee | *Table Summary:* [2. Cancellation & Rescheduling Cutoff Schedules] - Notice Given: More than 48 hours | Fee: $0.00 - Notice Given: 24 to 48 hours | Fee: $50.00 - Notice Given: Under 24 hours | Fee: 100% of scheduled service fee - Notice Given: Lockout on arrival | Fee: 100% of scheduled service fee **Cancellation Details** - Notice is counted from the start of your scheduled arrival window. - Cancel through the client portal, by phone, or by email. Messages received after business hours (6:00 PM) count as received the next business morning. - **Weather & Emergencies:** If unsafe travel conditions or a documented emergency prevent service, we reschedule without a fee. - **Short-Term Rental Turnovers:** Cancellations of a turnover tied to a booking that was itself canceled by a guest are free when notified within 24 hours of the guest's cancellation."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-PST-001",
    "category": "Post-Construction Services",
    "question": "Why does post-construction cleaning require multiple passes?",
    "answer": "Drywall and sawdust particles remain suspended in the air for up to 48 hours after construction wraps up. We utilize certified 0.3-micron HEPA vacuums and a structured three-phase process (rough pass, deep vacuum, damp microfiber sparkle wipe) to prevent settling dust from coating surfaces after cleaning.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-PST-005",
    "category": "Post-Construction Services",
    "question": "Dust came back a few days after you cleaned. Can you return?",
    "answer": "Fine dust can resettle for several days after finishing. We offer a touch-up visit within 7 days of the final clean, and will walk the punch list with you or your contractor within 48 hours.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "POST_CONSTRUCTION_REMEDIATION_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Post-construction cleaning requires a sequential three-phase approach to capture settling airborne drywall gypsum and sawdust: 1. **Phase 1: Rough Debris Pass:** Removal of construction packaging, protective films, tape residue, and rough floor sweeping with HEPA capture. 2. **Phase 2: High-to-Low HEPA Vacuuming:** Dry particle extraction starting from ceiling joists, HVAC diffusers, door casings, down to baseboards. 3. **Phase 3: Wet Microfiber Sparkle Pass:** Multi-bucket damp wipe using electrostatic microfiber cloths to capture remaining microscopic dust films."}, {"source": "POST_CONSTRUCTION_REMEDIATION_GUIDE.md", "quote": "**Kettle & Loom Cleaning Collective** — *Pure Ingredients. Meticulous Spaces. Uncompromising Clean.* Construction dust is fine, clings to surfaces, and is easily disturbed. Drywall gypsum, sawdust, and, in some cases, crystalline silica (from cutting concrete, tile, or masonry) require a methodical, top-to-bottom process."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ACC-002",
    "category": "Property Access & Security",
    "question": "How do you handle my keys and door codes?",
    "answer": "A smart lock with a unique service PIN is preferred. If you use physical keys, they stay in an on-site lockbox, and technicians never carry permanent property keys off-site. Alarm and access codes are stored in encrypted profiles.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ACC-001",
    "category": "Property Access & Security",
    "question": "Do I need to be home when the cleaning collective arrives?",
    "answer": "No. Most residential and commercial clients provide a smart lock code or lockbox key. Our technicians arrive within the designated arrival window, complete the service scope, re-secure all windows and doors, and set the security alarm upon departure.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "PROPERTY_ACCESS_AND_CANCELLATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "* **Digital Keypads & Smart Locks:** Preferred access method. Clients provide a unique service PIN designated exclusively for Kettle & Loom staff. We recommend a PIN that is active only during the service window. * **Physical Lockboxes:** If using physical keys, keys must remain inside a secure on-site lockbox. Technicians will not carry permanent property keys off-site. Lockbox codes are shared only with the assigned team and changed on request. * **Alarm Systems:** Alarm disarm codes and re-arming instructions must be stored in encrypted client profiles. Any false alarm dispatch fees resulting from inaccurate client codes are the client's responsibility. - Technicians disarm on arrival and re-arm on departure. If an alarm triggers, the technician calls the client and the alarm company within **5 minutes** and gives the correct passcode. - Provide your alarm company's name and the verbal passcode for dispatch. * **Departure Procedure:** Technicians re-lock all doors, close windows, set the thermostat to its original setting, turn off lights, and text a completion notice. * **Key Custody:** Access details are visible only to the Operations team and the assigned technicians. Access codes are removed from the technician's device when the contract ends. * **Garage and Gate Codes:** Provide any gate, garage, or elevator access in your profile."}, {"source": "PROPERTY_ACCESS_AND_CANCELLATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "We love pets, but for technician safety and to prevent pets from darting out exterior doors, dogs and cats must be secured in a designated room or crate during service unless prior written arrangements are confirmed. - Mark the room with a sign, and make sure the room has water. - Tell us about any pets that bite, escape, or react to strangers when you book. - Technicians may decline to enter a property where a dog is not secured, and the visit is treated as a lockout. - Exotic pets, reptiles, and aquariums are not touched or cleaned. - Pets must not be left in spaces with wet floors."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-005",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "A cleaning product got in my eye. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Flush your eye with clean water for 10 minutes with the eyelid held open, remove contact lenses if you can, and seek medical attention if irritation persists. For ingestion, rinse the mouth and call Poison Control at 1-800-222-1222. Then contact us so we can provide the SDS and file an incident report.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-003",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "Why do you leave disinfectant wet for 10 minutes?",
    "answer": "Disinfectants only work if the surface stays visibly wet for the product's full contact time. For Bio-Shield that is 10 minutes. Wiping sooner reduces how many germs are killed. OxyPure needs 3 minutes and Citrus-Loom needs 5 minutes.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Every product has a Safety Data Sheet (SDS) in the technician binder and the mobile app, readable offline. | Exposure | Response | | :--- | :--- | | **Inhalation** | Low-hazard, zero-VOC formulations. Move to fresh air if anyone has irritation and ventilate the room. Seek medical attention if symptoms last more than 15 minutes. | | **Eye Contact** | In case of direct splash, flush eyes with potable water for **10 minutes**, holding the eyelids open. Remove contact lenses if easy to do. Seek medical attention if irritation continues. | | **Skin Contact** | Rinse with water for **5 minutes**. Remove contaminated clothing. Seek medical advice if redness persists. | | **Ingestion** | Rinse mouth. Do not induce vomiting. Call Poison Control at **1-800-222-1222** (U.S.) and follow their directions. | *Table Summary:* [3. SDS Exposure Protocols & First Aid] - Exposure: Inhalation | Response: Low-hazard, zero-VOC formulations. Move to fresh air if anyone has irritation and ventilate the room. Seek medical attention if symptoms last more than 15 minutes. - Exposure: Eye Contact | Response: In case of direct splash, flush eyes with potable water for 10 minutes, holding the eyelids open. Remove contact lenses if easy to do. Seek medical attention if irritation continues. - Exposure: Skin Contact | Response: Rinse with water for 5 minutes. Remove contaminated clothing. Seek medical advice if redness persists. - Exposure: Ingestion | Response: Rinse mouth. Do not induce vomiting. Call Poison Control at 1-800-222-1222 (U.S.) and follow their directions. **Note:** Concentrated 3% hydrogen peroxide and 8% citric acid can irritate eyes and skin. Wear nitrile gloves and eye protection when pouring or diluting concentrates."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-PST-004",
    "category": "Post-Construction Services",
    "question": "Can you clean up silica dust from cutting tile or concrete?",
    "answer": "We use wet methods and HEPA only, with proper respirators, and never dry sweep. Large silica contamination or suspected asbestos or lead should be assessed by a certified abatement contractor, so please call us before work begins.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ACC-005",
    "category": "Property Access & Security",
    "question": "Something in my home was damaged during a cleaning. What now?",
    "answer": "Report it within 24 hours with photos. We maintain liability insurance and bonding, and claims are reviewed within 5 business days. We will compare against the pre-existing condition photos taken at your walkthrough.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "WALKTHROUGH_AND_INTAKE_SOP.md", "quote": "1. **Initial Property Audit:** Conduct a **30-minute** on-site assessment with the client or property manager. Measure and record the square footage of each room and total conditioned space, and note the number of bedrooms, bathrooms, and floor types. Confirm that the square footage on the booking is within 10% of the measured figure. 2. **Surface Sensitivity Mapping:** Log all sensitive materials (honed Carrara marble, unsealed butcher block, oil-rubbed bronze hardware, wool area rugs). Each entry has the room, material, and the approved product (see `CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md`). 3. **Pre-Existing Condition Documentation:** Photograph existing carpet stains, scratched wood floors, and chipped tiles. Upload to the client profile with a date stamp. Take at least **3 photos per room** (wide shot plus close-ups), and a photo of each existing defect with a coin or ruler for scale. 4. **Air Quality & Allergen Assessment:** Identify presence of pets, dust sensitivities, or fragrance allergies to tailor hypoallergenic essential oils or go fully unscented. 5. **Estimate & Scope Confirmation:** Generate a fixed-price proposal detailing initial deep-clean baseline hours and ongoing maintenance frequencies. The estimate uses `service_scope_matrix.json` and a base rate of $55.00 per technician-hour. **Output:** A signed Property Profile containing the sensitivity map, photo log, access and alarm details (stored encrypted), pet details, and scope."}]

