    "answer": "Fine dust can resettle for several days after finishing. We offer a touch-up visit within 7 days of the final clean, and will walk the punch list with you or your contractor within 48 hours.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "POST_CONSTRUCTION_REMEDIATION_GUIDE.md", "quote": "| Stage | Timing | | :--- | :--- | | Rough clean (Phase 1) | After trade work, before final painting touch-ups | | Final clean (Phases 2–3) | After all trades are done, no earlier than 24–48 hours after last sanding | | Touch-up visit | Within 7 days of the final clean, if needed | *Table Summary:* [5. Scheduling] - Stage: Rough clean (Phase 1) | Timing: After trade work, before final painting touch-ups - Stage: Final clean (Phases 2–3) | Timing: After all trades are done, no earlier than 24–48 hours after last sanding - Stage: Touch-up visit | Timing: Within 7 days of the final clean, if needed Dust can resettle for several days after finishing, which is why a short touch-up visit is offered."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-PST-001",
    "category": "Post-Construction Services",
    "question": "Why does post-construction cleaning require multiple passes?",
    "answer": "Drywall and sawdust particles remain suspended in the air for up to 48 hours after construction wraps up. We utilize certified 0.3-micron HEPA vacuums and a structured three-phase process (rough pass, deep vacuum, damp microfiber sparkle wipe) to prevent settling dust from coating surfaces after cleaning.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "service_scope_matrix.json", "quote": "{
