[{"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Kettle & Loom exclusively deploys EPA Design for the Environment (DfE) and Green Seal certified cleaning chemistry: | Product / Formulation | Active Botanical Base | Target Pathogens / Soils | Dwell Time Required | | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | | **Bio-Shield Hospital Disinfectant** | Thymol (0.05% botanical thyme extract) | 99.99% bacteria, enveloped viruses, fungi (per label claims) | 10 minutes (wet dwell) | | **OxyPure Multi-Surface Cleaner** | Hydrogen Peroxide (stabilized 3%) | Soap scum, organic grease, protein soils | 3 minutes | | **Citrus-Loom Mineral Descaler** | Organic Citric Acid (food-grade 8%) | Hard water scale, calcium deposits, rust | 5 minutes | | **PureLoom Floor Wash** | Saponified Coconut & Olive Oil Soap | Hardwood, engineered plank, stone tiles | Immediate mop dry | *Table Summary:* [1. Approved Botanical Formulations & Active Ingredients] - Product / Formulation: Bio-Shield Hospital Disinfectant | Active Botanical Base: Thymol (0.05% botanical thyme extract) | Target Pathogens / Soils: 99.99% bacteria, enveloped viruses, fungi (per label claims) | Dwell Time Required: 10 minutes (wet dwell) - Product / Formulation: OxyPure Multi-Surface Cleaner | Active Botanical Base: Hydrogen Peroxide (stabilized 3%) | Target Pathogens / Soils: Soap scum, organic grease, protein soils | Dwell Time Required: 3 minutes - Product / Formulation: Citrus-Loom Mineral Descaler | Active Botanical Base: Organic Citric Acid (food-grade 8%) | Target Pathogens / Soils: Hard water scale, calcium deposits, rust | Dwell Time Required: 5 minutes - Product / Formulation: PureLoom Floor Wash | Active Botanical Base: Saponified Coconut & Olive Oil Soap | Target Pathogens / Soils: Hardwood, engineered plank, stone tiles | Dwell Time Required: Immediate mop dry"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-001",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "Are your cleaning products safe for homes with infants and pets?",
    "answer": "Our products are zero-VOC, plant- or mineral-derived, and EPA Design for the Environment (DfE) and Green Seal certified. Our hospital-grade disinfectant uses 0.05% thymol, a thyme extract, and kills 99.99% of bacteria and enveloped viruses on a 10-minute wet dwell. Botanical does not mean harmless, so we ask that pets and infants stay out of a room until surfaces dry.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-002",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "What ingredients do you use?",
    "answer": "Bio-Shield Disinfectant uses 0.05% thymol, OxyPure uses stabilized 3% hydrogen peroxide, Citrus-Loom Descaler uses 8% food-grade citric acid, and PureLoom Floor Wash is a saponified coconut and olive oil soap. We provide Safety Data Sheets for every product on request.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-004",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "How do you price a cleaning?",
    "answer": "Estimates use our scope matrix and a base rate of $55.00 per technician-hour. Maintenance cleans take about 75 minutes per 1,000 sq ft, short-term rental turnovers about 110 minutes, and commercial offices about 45 minutes. You receive a fixed-price proposal after your 30-minute walkthrough.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WALKTHROUGH_AND_INTAKE_SOP.md", "quote": "1. **Initial Property Audit:** Conduct a **30-minute** on-site assessment with the client or property manager. Measure and record the square footage of each room and total conditioned space, and note the number of bedrooms, bathrooms, and floor types. Confirm that the square footage on the booking is within 10% of the measured figure. 2. **Surface Sensitivity Mapping:** Log all sensitive materials (honed Carrara marble, unsealed butcher block, oil-rubbed bronze hardware, wool area rugs). Each entry has the room, material, and the approved product (see `CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md`). 3. **Pre-Existing Condition Documentation:** Photograph existing carpet stains, scratched wood floors, and chipped tiles. Upload to the client profile with a date stamp. Take at least **3 photos per room** (wide shot plus close-ups), and a photo of each existing defect with a coin or ruler for scale. 4. **Air Quality & Allergen Assessment:** Identify presence of pets, dust sensitivities, or fragrance allergies to tailor hypoallergenic essential oils or go fully unscented. 5. **Estimate & Scope Confirmation:** Generate a fixed-price proposal detailing initial deep-clean baseline hours and ongoing maintenance frequencies. The estimate uses `service_scope_matrix.json` and a base rate of $55.00 per technician-hour. **Output:** A signed Property Profile containing the sensitivity map, photo log, access and alarm details (stored encrypted), pet details, and scope."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-PST-003",
    "category": "Post-Construction Services",
    "question": "How long does a post-construction clean take?",
    "answer": "About 240 technician-minutes per 1,000 sq ft across all three phases. That is roughly 20% rough debris, 40% HEPA vacuuming, and 40% wet microfiber. A 2,000 sq ft home takes about 8 technician-hours, spread over two visits so dust can settle.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "WALKTHROUGH_AND_INTAKE_SOP.md", "quote": "| Item | Recorded | | :--- | :--- | | Square footage by room | Yes | | Floor types by room | Yes | | Sensitive surfaces | Yes | | Pre-existing damage (photo log) | Yes | | Pets, infants, allergies | Yes | | Access method and alarm details | Yes (encrypted) | | Parking and loading | Yes | | Water and power access | Yes | | Client-supplied cleaning products | Note: not used unless approved | *Table Summary:* [3. Walkthrough Checklist] - Item: Square footage by room | Recorded: Yes - Item: Floor types by room | Recorded: Yes - Item: Sensitive surfaces | Recorded: Yes - Item: Pre-existing damage (photo log) | Recorded: Yes - Item: Pets, infants, allergies | Recorded: Yes - Item: Access method and alarm details | Recorded: Yes (encrypted) - Item: Parking and loading | Recorded: Yes - Item: Water and power access | Recorded: Yes - Item: Client-supplied cleaning products | Recorded: Note: not used unless approved"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-SCP-001",
    "category": "Scope of Services",
    "question": "Do you clean unsealed marble or antique wood furniture?",
    "answer": "During your initial walkthrough, our team maps all sensitive surfaces. We use pH-neutral saponified soap washes for hardwood and unsealed stone. We strictly prohibit the use of acidic descalers on marble, limestone, or terrazzo to prevent etching.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ACC-005",
    "category": "Property Access & Security",
    "question": "Something in my home was damaged during a cleaning. What now?",
    "answer": "Report it within 24 hours with photos. We maintain liability insurance and bonding, and claims are reviewed within 5 business days. We will compare against the pre-existing condition photos taken at your walkthrough.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-001",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "Are your cleaning products safe for homes with infants and pets?",
    "answer": "Our products are zero-VOC, plant- or mineral-derived, and EPA Design for the Environment (DfE) and Green Seal certified. Our hospital-grade disinfectant uses 0.05% thymol, a thyme extract, and kills 99.99% of bacteria and enveloped viruses on a 10-minute wet dwell. Botanical does not mean harmless, so we ask that pets and infants stay out of a room until surfaces dry.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- All botanical concentrates must remain in labeled, UV-resistant amber dispensers at **50°F–80°F (10°C–27°C)**. - Never store in vehicles overnight, and never decant into unlabeled bottles or food containers. - Keep stored products out of direct sunlight and away from heat sources. - Rotate stock. Hydrogen peroxide has a shelf life of about 12 months from the opening date, and open dates must be written on the bottle. - Dispose of spent solutions down a sanitary drain with running water. Never pour them into storm drains."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-SCP-004",
    "category": "Scope of Services",
    "question": "Is there anything you won't clean?",
    "answer": "We do not handle biohazards, mold remediation, or asbestos and lead abatement, and we don't move furniture over 50 lb. We also do not use acid on unsealed natural stone.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

