[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-001",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "What happens if I need to cancel my cleaning appointment tomorrow?",
    "answer": "Appointments canceled with less than 24 hours notice are subject to a 100% service fee charge because our collective members are paid for their booked time. If canceled between 24 and 48 hours in advance, a $50 administrative fee applies. Cancellations with over 48 hours notice are completely free.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-003",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "Do I have to pay an initial deep clean?",
    "answer": "Yes, all recurring contracts start with a foundational Initial Deep Clean. It removes buildup, limescale, and synthetic wax residue from earlier cleaners, and typically takes 2.0 to 2.5 times a regular visit. It is quoted as a fixed price during your walkthrough.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "PROPERTY_ACCESS_AND_CANCELLATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "* **48-Hour Free Cancellation:** Services may be canceled or rescheduled without penalty up to **48 hours** prior to the scheduled arrival window. * **Late Cancellation (Within 24–48 Hours):** Incurs a **$50.00 administrative rescheduling fee**. * **Same-Day Cancellation / Lockout (Under 24 Hours):** Charged at **100% of the scheduled service fee**. Our collective technicians are scheduled and paid for their booked time. | Notice Given | Fee | | :--- | :--- | | More than 48 hours | $0.00 | | 24 to 48 hours | $50.00 | | Under 24 hours | 100% of scheduled service fee | | Lockout on arrival | 100% of scheduled service fee | *Table Summary:* [2. Cancellation & Rescheduling Cutoff Schedules] - Notice Given: More than 48 hours | Fee: $0.00 - Notice Given: 24 to 48 hours | Fee: $50.00 - Notice Given: Under 24 hours | Fee: 100% of scheduled service fee - Notice Given: Lockout on arrival | Fee: 100% of scheduled service fee **Cancellation Details** - Notice is counted from the start of your scheduled arrival window. - Cancel through the client portal, by phone, or by email. Messages received after business hours (6:00 PM) count as received the next business morning. - **Weather & Emergencies:** If unsafe travel conditions or a documented emergency prevent service, we reschedule without a fee. - **Short-Term Rental Turnovers:** Cancellations of a turnover tied to a booking that was itself canceled by a guest are free when notified within 24 hours of the guest's cancellation."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-PST-001",
    "category": "Post-Construction Services",
    "question": "Why does post-construction cleaning require multiple passes?",
    "answer": "Drywall and sawdust particles remain suspended in the air for up to 48 hours after construction wraps up. We utilize certified 0.3-micron HEPA vacuums and a structured three-phase process (rough pass, deep vacuum, damp microfiber sparkle wipe) to prevent settling dust from coating surfaces after cleaning.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "POST_CONSTRUCTION_REMEDIATION_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Post-construction cleaning requires a sequential three-phase approach to capture settling airborne drywall gypsum and sawdust: 1. **Phase 1: Rough Debris Pass:** Removal of construction packaging, protective films, tape residue, and rough floor sweeping with HEPA capture. 2. **Phase 2: High-to-Low HEPA Vacuuming:** Dry particle extraction starting from ceiling joists, HVAC diffusers, door casings, down to baseboards. 3. **Phase 3: Wet Microfiber Sparkle Pass:** Multi-bucket damp wipe using electrostatic microfiber cloths to capture remaining microscopic dust films."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-SCP-001",
    "category": "Scope of Services",
    "question": "Do you clean unsealed marble or antique wood furniture?",
    "answer": "During your initial walkthrough, our team maps all sensitive surfaces. We use pH-neutral saponified soap washes for hardwood and unsealed stone. We strictly prohibit the use of acidic descalers on marble, limestone, or terrazzo to prevent etching.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "service_scope_matrix.json", "quote": "Moving heavy furniture (over 50 lb)"}]

[{"source": "PROPERTY_ACCESS_AND_CANCELLATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "* **Digital Keypads & Smart Locks:** Preferred access method. Clients provide a unique service PIN designated exclusively for Kettle & Loom staff. We recommend a PIN that is active only during the service window. * **Physical Lockboxes:** If using physical keys, keys must remain inside a secure on-site lockbox. Technicians will not carry permanent property keys off-site. Lockbox codes are shared only with the assigned team and changed on request. * **Alarm Systems:** Alarm disarm codes and re-arming instructions must be stored in encrypted client profiles. Any false alarm dispatch fees resulting from inaccurate client codes are the client's responsibility. - Technicians disarm on arrival and re-arm on departure. If an alarm triggers, the technician calls the client and the alarm company within **5 minutes** and gives the correct passcode. - Provide your alarm company's name and the verbal passcode for dispatch. * **Departure Procedure:** Technicians re-lock all doors, close windows, set the thermostat to its original setting, turn off lights, and text a completion notice. * **Key Custody:** Access details are visible only to the Operations team and the assigned technicians. Access codes are removed from the technician's device when the contract ends. * **Garage and Gate Codes:** Provide any gate, garage, or elevator access in your profile."}, {"source": "PROPERTY_ACCESS_AND_CANCELLATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "- Report any damage within **24 hours** of service. Photos are required. - Kettle & Loom maintains general liability insurance and bonding. Claims are reviewed within 5 business days. - Fragile and valuable items (jewelry, cash, and collectibles) should be secured. Technicians do not move items worth over $250 unless asked."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-003",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "Do I have to pay an initial deep clean?",
    "answer": "Yes, all recurring contracts start with a foundational Initial Deep Clean. It removes buildup, limescale, and synthetic wax residue from earlier cleaners, and typically takes 2.0 to 2.5 times a regular visit. It is quoted as a fixed price during your walkthrough.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-CAN-001",
    "category": "Booking & Cancellations",
    "question": "What happens if I need to cancel my cleaning appointment tomorrow?",
    "answer": "Appointments canceled with less than 24 hours notice are subject to a 100% service fee charge because our collective members are paid for their booked time. If canceled between 24 and 48 hours in advance, a $50 administrative fee applies. Cancellations with over 48 hours notice are completely free.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-005",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "A cleaning product got in my eye. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Flush your eye with clean water for 10 minutes with the eyelid held open, remove contact lenses if you can, and seek medical attention if irritation persists. For ingestion, rinse the mouth and call Poison Control at 1-800-222-1222. Then contact us so we can provide the SDS and file an incident report.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-002",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "What ingredients do you use?",
    "answer": "Bio-Shield Disinfectant uses 0.05% thymol, OxyPure uses stabilized 3% hydrogen peroxide, Citrus-Loom Descaler uses 8% food-grade citric acid, and PureLoom Floor Wash is a saponified coconut and olive oil soap. We provide Safety Data Sheets for every product on request.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "* **Strict Acid Prohibition:** *Citrus-Loom Descaler and acidic solutions must NEVER be applied to unsealed natural marble, travertine, limestone, or terrazzo.* Acid etching permanently damages calcite stone. * **Hardwood Neutrality:** Wood flooring must be cleaned exclusively with pH-neutral PureLoom wash. Never saturate it with standing water. * **Granite & Quartz:** Use OxyPure only. No descaler on sealed stone unless the sealer is confirmed intact and the surface is rinsed within 5 minutes. * **Oil-Rubbed Bronze & Unlacquered Brass:** Dry microfiber only. No acids or peroxide, as they strip the finish. * **Unsealed Butcher Block:** Damp wipe with PureLoom diluted to the label ratio. Do not apply disinfectant to unsealed wood for a full dwell time. * **Wool Rugs & Natural Fibers:** Do not apply hydrogen peroxide, because it may bleach dyed fibers. Spot test first in a hidden area. Always check the client's Surface Sensitivity Map (see `WALKTHROUGH_AND_INTAKE_SOP.md`) before opening a product."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-PST-005",
    "category": "Post-Construction Services",
    "question": "Dust came back a few days after you cleaned. Can you return?",
    "answer": "Fine dust can resettle for several days after finishing. We offer a touch-up visit within 7 days of the final clean, and will walk the punch list with you or your contractor within 48 hours.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-PST-001",
    "category": "Post-Construction Services",
    "question": "Why does post-construction cleaning require multiple passes?",
    "answer": "Drywall and sawdust particles remain suspended in the air for up to 48 hours after construction wraps up. We utilize certified 0.3-micron HEPA vacuums and a structured three-phase process (rough pass, deep vacuum, damp microfiber sparkle wipe) to prevent settling dust from coating surfaces after cleaning.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "POST_CONSTRUCTION_REMEDIATION_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Post-construction cleaning requires a sequential three-phase approach to capture settling airborne drywall gypsum and sawdust: 1. **Phase 1: Rough Debris Pass:** Removal of construction packaging, protective films, tape residue, and rough floor sweeping with HEPA capture. 2. **Phase 2: High-to-Low HEPA Vacuuming:** Dry particle extraction starting from ceiling joists, HVAC diffusers, door casings, down to baseboards. 3. **Phase 3: Wet Microfiber Sparkle Pass:** Multi-bucket damp wipe using electrostatic microfiber cloths to capture remaining microscopic dust films."}, {"source": "POST_CONSTRUCTION_REMEDIATION_GUIDE.md", "quote": "**Kettle & Loom Cleaning Collective** — *Pure Ingredients. Meticulous Spaces. Uncompromising Clean.* Construction dust is fine, clings to surfaces, and is easily disturbed. Drywall gypsum, sawdust, and, in some cases, crystalline silica (from cutting concrete, tile, or masonry) require a methodical, top-to-bottom process."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-003",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "Why do you leave disinfectant wet for 10 minutes?",
    "answer": "Disinfectants only work if the surface stays visibly wet for the product's full contact time. For Bio-Shield that is 10 minutes. Wiping sooner reduces how many germs are killed. OxyPure needs 3 minutes and Citrus-Loom needs 5 minutes.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-002",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "What ingredients do you use?",
    "answer": "Bio-Shield Disinfectant uses 0.05% thymol, OxyPure uses stabilized 3% hydrogen peroxide, Citrus-Loom Descaler uses 8% food-grade citric acid, and PureLoom Floor Wash is a saponified coconut and olive oil soap. We provide Safety Data Sheets for every product on request.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Kettle & Loom exclusively deploys EPA Design for the Environment (DfE) and Green Seal certified cleaning chemistry: | Product / Formulation | Active Botanical Base | Target Pathogens / Soils | Dwell Time Required | | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | | **Bio-Shield Hospital Disinfectant** | Thymol (0.05% botanical thyme extract) | 99.99% bacteria, enveloped viruses, fungi (per label claims) | 10 minutes (wet dwell) | | **OxyPure Multi-Surface Cleaner** | Hydrogen Peroxide (stabilized 3%) | Soap scum, organic grease, protein soils | 3 minutes | | **Citrus-Loom Mineral Descaler** | Organic Citric Acid (food-grade 8%) | Hard water scale, calcium deposits, rust | 5 minutes | | **PureLoom Floor Wash** | Saponified Coconut & Olive Oil Soap | Hardwood, engineered plank, stone tiles | Immediate mop dry | *Table Summary:* [1. Approved Botanical Formulations & Active Ingredients] - Product / Formulation: Bio-Shield Hospital Disinfectant | Active Botanical Base: Thymol (0.05% botanical thyme extract) | Target Pathogens / Soils: 99.99% bacteria, enveloped viruses, fungi (per label claims) | Dwell Time Required: 10 minutes (wet dwell) - Product / Formulation: OxyPure Multi-Surface Cleaner | Active Botanical Base: Hydrogen Peroxide (stabilized 3%) | Target Pathogens / Soils: Soap scum, organic grease, protein soils | Dwell Time Required: 3 minutes - Product / Formulation: Citrus-Loom Mineral Descaler | Active Botanical Base: Organic Citric Acid (food-grade 8%) | Target Pathogens / Soils: Hard water scale, calcium deposits, rust | Dwell Time Required: 5 minutes - Product / Formulation: PureLoom Floor Wash | Active Botanical Base: Saponified Coconut & Olive Oil Soap | Target Pathogens / Soils: Hardwood, engineered plank, stone tiles | Dwell Time Required: Immediate mop dry"}]

