    "answer": "No. Most residential and commercial clients provide a smart lock code or lockbox key. Our technicians arrive within the designated arrival window, complete the service scope, re-secure all windows and doors, and set the security alarm upon departure.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "PROPERTY_ACCESS_AND_CANCELLATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "* **Digital Keypads & Smart Locks:** Preferred access method. Clients provide a unique service PIN designated exclusively for Kettle & Loom staff. We recommend a PIN that is active only during the service window. * **Physical Lockboxes:** If using physical keys, keys must remain inside a secure on-site lockbox. Technicians will not carry permanent property keys off-site. Lockbox codes are shared only with the assigned team and changed on request. * **Alarm Systems:** Alarm disarm codes and re-arming instructions must be stored in encrypted client profiles. Any false alarm dispatch fees resulting from inaccurate client codes are the client's responsibility. - Technicians disarm on arrival and re-arm on departure. If an alarm triggers, the technician calls the client and the alarm company within **5 minutes** and gives the correct passcode. - Provide your alarm company's name and the verbal passcode for dispatch. * **Departure Procedure:** Technicians re-lock all doors, close windows, set the thermostat to its original setting, turn off lights, and text a completion notice. * **Key Custody:** Access details are visible only to the Operations team and the assigned technicians. Access codes are removed from the technician's device when the contract ends. * **Garage and Gate Codes:** Provide any gate, garage, or elevator access in your profile."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-005",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "A cleaning product got in my eye. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Flush your eye with clean water for 10 minutes with the eyelid held open, remove contact lenses if you can, and seek medical attention if irritation persists. For ingestion, rinse the mouth and call Poison Control at 1-800-222-1222. Then contact us so we can provide the SDS and file an incident report.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "* **Strict Acid Prohibition:** *Citrus-Loom Descaler and acidic solutions must NEVER be applied to unsealed natural marble, travertine, limestone, or terrazzo.* Acid etching permanently damages calcite stone. * **Hardwood Neutrality:** Wood flooring must be cleaned exclusively with pH-neutral PureLoom wash. Never saturate it with standing water. * **Granite & Quartz:** Use OxyPure only. No descaler on sealed stone unless the sealer is confirmed intact and the surface is rinsed within 5 minutes. * **Oil-Rubbed Bronze & Unlacquered Brass:** Dry microfiber only. No acids or peroxide, as they strip the finish. * **Unsealed Butcher Block:** Damp wipe with PureLoom diluted to the label ratio. Do not apply disinfectant to unsealed wood for a full dwell time. * **Wool Rugs & Natural Fibers:** Do not apply hydrogen peroxide, because it may bleach dyed fibers. Spot test first in a hidden area. Always check the client's Surface Sensitivity Map (see `WALKTHROUGH_AND_INTAKE_SOP.md`) before opening a product."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-002",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "What ingredients do you use?",
    "answer": "Bio-Shield Disinfectant uses 0.05% thymol, OxyPure uses stabilized 3% hydrogen peroxide, Citrus-Loom Descaler uses 8% food-grade citric acid, and PureLoom Floor Wash is a saponified coconut and olive oil soap. We provide Safety Data Sheets for every product on request.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "service_scope_matrix.json", "quote": "Cleaning of unsealed natural stone with acidic products"}]

[{"source": "WALKTHROUGH_AND_INTAKE_SOP.md", "quote": "All recurring service contracts must undergo a foundational **Initial Deep Clean**. This baseline visit removes pre-existing buildup, limescale, and synthetic wax residues from previous chemical cleaners before beginning botanical maintenance. - **Duration:** Typically **2.0x to 2.5x** the standard maintenance time for the same square footage (for example, a 2,000 sq ft home that takes 150 minutes for maintenance will take about 5 to 6.25 hours of technician time for the deep clean). - **Added Tasks:** Interior oven and refrigerator, baseboards, door casings, window sills and tracks, cabinet interiors on request, descaling of fixtures, and detailed grout work. - **Why It Is Mandatory:** Botanical chemistry cannot lift old synthetic residues on its own, and the baseline sets a measurable standard for every visit after it. - **Short-Term Rental Properties:** A baseline deep clean is required before the first turnover. - **Pricing:** Quoted as a fixed price at the walkthrough. Rates are not charged beyond the quote unless conditions differ from the photos, and the client approves any change first."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-SCP-005",
    "category": "Scope of Services",
    "question": "Do you provide commercial office cleaning?",
    "answer": "Yes. Nightly, 3x weekly, or weekly service covering workstations, restrooms, break rooms, and common areas, at about 45 minutes per 1,000 sq ft per technician. Our technicians are W-2 employees of the cooperative, so you see the same familiar faces.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-SCP-002",
    "category": "Scope of Services",
    "question": "What does a standard residential clean include?",
    "answer": "Kitchen: cabinet faces, countertops, stainless exteriors, sink, and floors. Bathrooms: grout, tubs, toilets, mirrors, and fixtures. Plus dusting, HEPA vacuuming, and damp mopping in living areas and bedrooms. Interior ovens, refrigerators, and cabinets are add-ons.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "service_scope_matrix.json", "quote": "{
    "name": "Interior oven or refrigerator",
    "estimated_minutes_each": 30
}"}]

[{"source": "POST_CONSTRUCTION_REMEDIATION_GUIDE.md", "quote": "* **Equipment Standard:** Commercial HEPA vacuums certified to capture **99.97% of particulates down to 0.3 microns**. Certification labels must be on the machine, and filters are inspected before every project. * **Filter Maintenance:** Replace or clean HEPA filters when the indicator shows full, or at least every **40 hours** of use. Empty bags and canisters outdoors or into a sealed bag at the end of every shift, away from the work area. * **Air Scrubbers:** For projects with heavy dust, place a HEPA air scrubber (rated at 4+ air changes per hour for the room volume) in the room during Phase 2, and keep it running for 4 hours afterward. * **Microfiber Fold Technique:** Microfiber cloths must be folded into **8 clean quadrants** and flipped continuously to prevent spreading dry drywall dust across painted walls. - When all 8 quadrants are soiled, the cloth goes in the used pile. Never dip a used cloth back in the clean solution. - Use the multi-bucket system: one bucket of clean solution, one of rinse, and fresh cloths from a clean stack. - Use **damp**, not wet, cloths, wrung out so that no water drips. Wet cloths turn drywall dust into a paste. * **Surface Cleaner:** OxyPure, diluted to label, or plain water on delicate finishes. See `CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md`."}, {"source": "service_scope_matrix.json", "quote": "{
    "tier_id": "TIER-PCN-04",
    "tier_name": "Post-Construction Remediation",
    "frequency_options": [
        "One-time (three phases)",
        "Touch-up visit within 7 days"
    ],
    "requires_initial_deep_clean": false,
    "zones": {
        "phase_1_rough_debris_pass": [
            "Remove construction packaging, protective films, stickers, and tape residue",
            "Scrape paint splatter with plastic blades",
            "Rough sweep floors with HEPA capture"
        ],
        "phase_2_high_to_low_hepa_vacuuming": [
            "HEPA vacuum ceiling joists, fans, HVAC diffusers, and light fixtures",
            "HEPA vacuum door casings, window tracks, and cabinet tops",
            "HEPA vacuum baseboards and floors (99.97% at 0.3 microns)"
        ],
        "phase_3_wet_microfiber_sparkle_pass": [
            "Damp wipe all surfaces with 8-quadrant folded microfiber",
            "Clean cabinet interiors, glass, and fixtures",
            "Final HEPA vacuum and white-glove inspection (3 sample points per room)"
        ]
    },
    "phase_labor_share_percent": {
        "phase_1": 20,
        "phase_2": 40,
        "phase_3": 40
    },
    "estimated_minutes_per_1000_sqft": 240
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-003",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "Why do you leave disinfectant wet for 10 minutes?",
    "answer": "Disinfectants only work if the surface stays visibly wet for the product's full contact time. For Bio-Shield that is 10 minutes. Wiping sooner reduces how many germs are killed. OxyPure needs 3 minutes and Citrus-Loom needs 5 minutes.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ECO-002",
    "category": "Chemical Safety & Eco-Standards",
    "question": "What ingredients do you use?",
    "answer": "Bio-Shield Disinfectant uses 0.05% thymol, OxyPure uses stabilized 3% hydrogen peroxide, Citrus-Loom Descaler uses 8% food-grade citric acid, and PureLoom Floor Wash is a saponified coconut and olive oil soap. We provide Safety Data Sheets for every product on request.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Wet dwell** means the surface stays visibly wet for the whole period. If it dries early, reapply. - Pre-clean heavy soil first, because disinfectants do not work through grease or grime. - Do not wipe Bio-Shield before 10 minutes have passed. Use a timer. - Disinfection is performed on high-touch surfaces only: toilets, handles, switches, keypads, faucets, and remotes."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-PST-005",
    "category": "Post-Construction Services",
    "question": "Dust came back a few days after you cleaned. Can you return?",
    "answer": "Fine dust can resettle for several days after finishing. We offer a touch-up visit within 7 days of the final clean, and will walk the punch list with you or your contractor within 48 hours.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-ACC-005",
    "category": "Property Access & Security",
