}"}, {"source": "CHEMICAL_SAFETY_AND_SDS_GUIDE.md", "quote": "* **Strict Acid Prohibition:** *Citrus-Loom Descaler and acidic solutions must NEVER be applied to unsealed natural marble, travertine, limestone, or terrazzo.* Acid etching permanently damages calcite stone. * **Hardwood Neutrality:** Wood flooring must be cleaned exclusively with pH-neutral PureLoom wash. Never saturate it with standing water. * **Granite & Quartz:** Use OxyPure only. No descaler on sealed stone unless the sealer is confirmed intact and the surface is rinsed within 5 minutes. * **Oil-Rubbed Bronze & Unlacquered Brass:** Dry microfiber only. No acids or peroxide, as they strip the finish. * **Unsealed Butcher Block:** Damp wipe with PureLoom diluted to the label ratio. Do not apply disinfectant to unsealed wood for a full dwell time. * **Wool Rugs & Natural Fibers:** Do not apply hydrogen peroxide, because it may bleach dyed fibers. Spot test first in a hidden area. Always check the client's Surface Sensitivity Map (see `WALKTHROUGH_AND_INTAKE_SOP.md`) before opening a product."}, {"source": "WALKTHROUGH_AND_INTAKE_SOP.md", "quote": "| Item | Recorded | | :--- | :--- | | Square footage by room | Yes | | Floor types by room | Yes | | Sensitive surfaces | Yes | | Pre-existing damage (photo log) | Yes | | Pets, infants, allergies | Yes | | Access method and alarm details | Yes (encrypted) | | Parking and loading | Yes | | Water and power access | Yes | | Client-supplied cleaning products | Note: not used unless approved | *Table Summary:* [3. Walkthrough Checklist] - Item: Square footage by room | Recorded: Yes - Item: Floor types by room | Recorded: Yes - Item: Sensitive surfaces | Recorded: Yes - Item: Pre-existing damage (photo log) | Recorded: Yes - Item: Pets, infants, allergies | Recorded: Yes - Item: Access method and alarm details | Recorded: Yes (encrypted) - Item: Parking and loading | Recorded: Yes - Item: Water and power access | Recorded: Yes - Item: Client-supplied cleaning products | Recorded: Note: not used unless approved"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-APPT-004",
    "category": "Appointments & Loaners",
    "question": "My car was damaged while at your shop. What do I do?",
    "answer": "Please tell us right away, ideally before leaving the lot, or within 24 hours, and bring photos. A manager reviews every damage report and will contact you.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-004",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "What happens if you find more problems after taking my car apart?",
    "answer": "Work stops immediately and we send a supplement estimate by SMS with photos. You must approve it separately before we continue. The final bill will not exceed the authorized total by more than 10% or $50.00, whichever is less, without a new approval.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "Fleet vehicles are placed ahead of retail customers in the bay queue, with safety-critical repairs and customer emergencies taking precedence over both. | Service Class | Examples | Guaranteed Turnaround | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | **Preventative Maintenance (PM Tier 1)** | Oil and filter, tire rotation, DVI | **Same-day (under 4 hours)** for drop-offs before **08:30 AM** | | **Minor Mechanical Repairs** | Brakes, alternators, starters | **24-hour** turnaround window | | **Major Drivetrain Overhauls** | Transmission, engine, differential | Dedicated bay allocation with **daily status progress dispatch** | *Table Summary:* [1. Priority Triage & Guaranteed Turnaround (SLA)] - Service Class: Preventative Maintenance (PM Tier 1) | Examples: Oil and filter, tire rotation, DVI | Guaranteed Turnaround: Same-day (under 4 hours) for drop-offs before 08:30 AM - Service Class: Minor Mechanical Repairs | Examples: Brakes, alternators, starters | Guaranteed Turnaround: 24-hour turnaround window - Service Class: Major Drivetrain Overhauls | Examples: Transmission, engine, differential | Guaranteed Turnaround: Dedicated bay allocation with daily status progress dispatch - **Clock Start:** The SLA clock starts when the vehicle is logged into our shop management software, and when diagnostic approval is received if the repair requires authorization above the pre-authorized limit. - **Parts Delays:** If a part is not available locally, we source it from a second supplier. We notify the fleet manager within **2 hours** of discovering a delay, with the new estimated completion time. - **SLA Exceptions:** Delays caused by awaiting approval, hidden damage found during teardown (see `ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md`), or manufacturer back-orders pause the SLA clock. - **Severe-Duty Notice:** Vehicles with GVWR above 14,000 lb are outside the light-fleet scope. Call us to discuss them."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-APPT-004",
    "category": "Appointments & Loaners",
    "question": "My car was damaged while at your shop. What do I do?",
    "answer": "Please tell us right away, ideally before leaving the lot, or within 24 hours, and bring photos. A manager reviews every damage report and will contact you.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-APPT-001",
    "category": "Appointments & Loaners",
    "question": "Do you offer loaner vehicles or shuttle services while my car is being serviced?",
    "answer": "Yes. We offer complimentary local shuttle rides within a 10-mile radius. For repairs exceeding $600 or taking longer than 24 hours, complimentary courtesy loaner cars are available upon reservation request (subject to driver license and insurance verification).",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Wash:** Rinse the vehicle every **10 to 14 days** during salt season, and after any storm, particularly the undercarriage, wheel wells, and rocker panels. Wash when temperatures are above 32°F (0°C) so the doors and locks don't freeze. - **Inspect:** Brake lines, fuel lines, and suspension components rust first. These are checked in the DVI. - **Protect:** Undercoating or wax-based rust inhibitors in the fall protect exposed metal, and a coat of wax on the paint protects the finish. - **Dry:** Lubricate door seals with silicone spray to prevent freezing. Wipe door jambs. - **Brake Components:** Salt corrodes calipers and slide pins, so we clean and lubricate them at each brake service."}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "NorthStar carries garage liability insurance. Report any damage that occurred while your vehicle was in our care **before leaving the lot**, or within 24 hours, and we will investigate."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-005",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "Do you service heavy-duty trucks?",
    "answer": "We service commercial light fleets, such as vans and light trucks. Vehicles above 14,000 lb GVWR are outside our standard scope, so please call us to discuss your unit.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-001",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "How do after-hours drop-offs work for commercial fleet vehicles?",
    "answer": "Park your vehicle in our secure Fleet North Lot stalls, complete the Fleet Work Order envelope with your fleet unit number, odometer, and driver notes, and place the key in the tamper-evident dual-locking drop safe at the Bay 1 exterior wall. Our early-shift dispatch team logs all vehicles at 6:30 AM for priority triage.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "1. Secure vehicle in designated Fleet North Lot parking stalls. 2. Complete the Fleet Work Order envelope detailing unit ID, current odometer, and primary driver complaint. 3. Deposit key into the tamper-evident dual-locking night drop safe located at the Bay 1 exterior wall. 4. Early shift dispatch technician logs intake scans into shop management software at **06:30 AM**. **Notes** - Lock the vehicle and remove valuables, fuel cards, and tools. - Any vehicle dropped after-hours is treated as received at 06:30 AM for SLA purposes. It does not qualify for the 08:30 AM same-day PM guarantee unless it was in the lot before 08:30 AM and logged by 06:30 AM, which is the standard case. - NorthStar is not responsible for items left in vehicles. - Our lot is lit and under camera surveillance."}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "- Fleet managers designate a **pre-authorized repair limit (standard: $350.00)** to expedite workflow without waiting for written authorizations. - Repairs at or under the limit proceed immediately after the DVI. They are documented on the invoice. - Repairs **over the limit** need written authorization through the SMS or email approval link from a designated authorized contact. Alternatively, call the fleet desk. - The limit applies **per vehicle, per visit**, not per line item, and cannot be split to avoid authorization. - Limits can be raised in writing, up to $1,000.00 for approved Net-30 accounts, and can be set per unit ID. - Safety-critical RED items are always reported to the fleet manager, even if under the limit."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MNT-004",
    "category": "Routine Maintenance",
    "question": "What coolant mix protects against freezing?",
    "answer": "A 50/50 mix of ethylene glycol and deionized water protects to -34\u00b0F (-37\u00b0C). We check it with a hydrometer. Richer than about 70% glycol actually freezes at a higher temperature, so more is not better. Don't mix different coolant types.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Wash:** Rinse the vehicle every **10 to 14 days** during salt season, and after any storm, particularly the undercarriage, wheel wells, and rocker panels. Wash when temperatures are above 32°F (0°C) so the doors and locks don't freeze. - **Inspect:** Brake lines, fuel lines, and suspension components rust first. These are checked in the DVI. - **Protect:** Undercoating or wax-based rust inhibitors in the fall protect exposed metal, and a coat of wax on the paint protects the finish. - **Dry:** Lubricate door seals with silicone spray to prevent freezing. Wipe door jambs. - **Brake Components:** Salt corrodes calipers and slide pins, so we clean and lubricate them at each brake service."}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Concentration Target:** 50/50 ethylene glycol and deionized water mixture providing freeze protection down to **-34°F (-37°C)**. - **Testing:** A hydrometer or refractometer measures the density of the coolant, and the reading is converted to a freeze point. We test it when the engine is cool. - **Pass:** -34°F (-37°C) or lower. - **Marginal:** -20°F to -33°F (-29°C to -36°C), so we top off with proper mix or flush the system. - **Fail:** Warmer than -20°F (-29°C). Flush and refill. - **Don't Overconcentrate:** A mix richer than 70% glycol freezes at a *higher* temperature and transfers heat less effectively. Use pre-mixed or deionized water, and never tap water. - **Boil-over & Corrosion Protection:** Fresh inhibitor additives prevent internal engine block scale and heater core pinhole corrosion. A 50/50 mix also raises the boiling point to about 265°F (129°C) with a 15 psi cap. - **Coolant Types:** Use the type your manufacturer requires (OAT, HOAT, or IAT) and don't mix types, because they can gel. Typical service interval is 30,000 to 60,000 miles for extended-life coolants (see `service_intervals_matrix.json`)."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-003",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "Are brake pads covered under warranty?",
    "answer": "A defect in a part or in our installation is covered, but normal friction wear is not. If pads fail early because of a defect or poor installation, we fix them. Pads that simply wear down with normal use are excluded.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-006",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "Can I keep the parts you replace?",
    "answer": "Yes. Ask when you authorize the work and we'll bag and tag them. Exchange items with a core charge, like alternators and starters, can be inspected on-site, but they must be returned to the distributor.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "Under state automotive repair regulations, customers retain the right to inspect and keep all replaced mechanical parts (excluding exchange items subject to manufacturer core charges, which may be inspected on-site before return to distributor). - Ask for your old parts when you authorize the work, and we will bag and tag them at the front desk. - Core-charge items (alternators, starters, brake calipers, and batteries) can be viewed on-site, but must go back to the distributor. Core charges are listed on the estimate. - Parts that are hazardous (batteries, fluids) will be handed over in sealed containers or disposed of in compliance with the rules. - Unclaimed parts are kept for **7 days** after pickup of the vehicle."}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. Stop driving the vehicle if the problem is a safety issue (brakes, steering, overheating). 2. Call NorthStar or the nationwide warranty hotline with your original invoice number. 3. Bring the vehicle to NorthStar or a participating facility. A technician will diagnose the failure. If it is covered, you pay $0 for parts and labor. 4. Keep your invoice and the maintenance records for your vehicle, because the warranty requires evidence of routine fluid maintenance. If we need to diagnose a failure that turns out not to be covered, the diagnostic fee applies (see Section 3)."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-001",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "What is covered under the NorthStar Peace of Mind Warranty?",
    "answer": "Our warranty covers parts and labor on qualifying mechanical repairs for 24 months or 24,000 miles, whichever comes first. It is honored at over 35,000 certified facilities nationwide. It excludes customer-supplied parts, routine friction wear (wiper blades, brake pads), commercial severe-duty abuse, racing, and failures from skipped routine fluid maintenance.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

