[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-002",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "A part you replaced failed while I'm traveling. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Call us or the nationwide warranty hotline before authorizing any repair, and have your invoice number ready. If you are at a participating facility, they diagnose the failure, and a covered repair costs you $0 for parts and labor.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-006",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "Can I keep the parts you replace?",
    "answer": "Yes. Ask when you authorize the work and we'll bag and tag them. Exchange items with a core charge, like alternators and starters, can be inspected on-site, but they must be returned to the distributor.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "| Covered | Not Covered | | :--- | :--- | | A water pump we replaced starts leaking at 14 months | Brake pads worn thin after 18,000 miles of normal driving | | A caliper seal leaks within warranty | Wiper blades that streak | | A starter we installed fails because of a defective part | A repair on a part you supplied | | A serpentine belt tensioner we installed was misinstalled | Failure caused by skipping oil changes or ignoring a DVI RED item | | A loose connection from our labor | Damage from racing, off-road use, or collision | *Table Summary:* [Clear Examples] - Covered: A water pump we replaced starts leaking at 14 months | Not Covered: Brake pads worn thin after 18,000 miles of normal driving - Covered: A caliper seal leaks within warranty | Not Covered: Wiper blades that streak - Covered: A starter we installed fails because of a defective part | Not Covered: A repair on a part you supplied - Covered: A serpentine belt tensioner we installed was misinstalled | Not Covered: Failure caused by skipping oil changes or ignoring a DVI RED item - Covered: A loose connection from our labor | Not Covered: Damage from racing, off-road use, or collision"}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. Stop driving the vehicle if the problem is a safety issue (brakes, steering, overheating). 2. Call NorthStar or the nationwide warranty hotline with your original invoice number. 3. Bring the vehicle to NorthStar or a participating facility. A technician will diagnose the failure. If it is covered, you pay $0 for parts and labor. 4. Keep your invoice and the maintenance records for your vehicle, because the warranty requires evidence of routine fluid maintenance. If we need to diagnose a failure that turns out not to be covered, the diagnostic fee applies (see Section 3)."}]

