    "answer": "Call us or the nationwide warranty hotline before authorizing any repair, and have your invoice number ready. If you are at a participating facility, they diagnose the failure, and a covered repair costs you $0 for parts and labor.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "- Morning dispatch begins at **06:30 AM** with the early-shift dispatch technician logging after-hours drop-offs and arranging the day's bay assignments. - **Priority Order:** (1) Safety-critical (RED) fleet repairs, (2) PM Tier 1 drop-offs received before 08:30 AM, (3) scheduled minor repairs, (4) other fleet work, (5) retail customers. - Fleet managers receive a text and email with a work-order number for each unit by **07:30 AM**. - Fleet DVI reports are issued within **90 minutes** of drop-off, with photos and a color grade for each of the 40 inspection points. - Pickup updates: Units are staged in the Fleet North Lot, and keys are available at the front desk from 7:00 AM."}, {"source": "service_intervals_matrix.json", "quote": "{
    "service": "Tire mount, balance, and install (set of 4)",
    "labor_hours": 1.2
}"}]

[{"source": "service_intervals_matrix.json", "quote": "{
    "service": "Brake fluid exchange (DOT 4)",
    "labor_hours": 0.7
}"}, {"source": "service_intervals_matrix.json", "quote": "{
    "service": "Rear brake pads and rotors, per axle",
    "labor_hours": 1.4
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MNT-002",
    "category": "Routine Maintenance",
    "question": "What happens at the 30,000-mile service?",
    "answer": "Tier 3 includes a full synthetic oil change, a DOT 4 brake fluid exchange, engine and cabin air filters, a cooling system freeze-point and pH audit, and a battery CCA conductance test. It takes about 2.5 labor hours and the base package is $349.50.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-002",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "How fast will you turn around my fleet vehicles?",
    "answer": "Preventative maintenance (PM Tier 1) is same-day, under 4 hours, for drop-offs before 8:30 AM. Minor repairs such as brakes, alternators, and starters have a 24-hour window. Major drivetrain overhauls get a dedicated bay and a daily status update.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-APPT-004",
    "category": "Appointments & Loaners",
    "question": "My car was damaged while at your shop. What do I do?",
    "answer": "Please tell us right away, ideally before leaving the lot, or within 24 hours, and bring photos. A manager reviews every damage report and will contact you.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Wash:** Rinse the vehicle every **10 to 14 days** during salt season, and after any storm, particularly the undercarriage, wheel wells, and rocker panels. Wash when temperatures are above 32°F (0°C) so the doors and locks don't freeze. - **Inspect:** Brake lines, fuel lines, and suspension components rust first. These are checked in the DVI. - **Protect:** Undercoating or wax-based rust inhibitors in the fall protect exposed metal, and a coat of wax on the paint protects the finish. - **Dry:** Lubricate door seals with silicone spray to prevent freezing. Wipe door jambs. - **Brake Components:** Salt corrodes calipers and slide pins, so we clean and lubricate them at each brake service."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MNT-003",
    "category": "Routine Maintenance",
    "question": "How do you test whether my battery will survive winter?",
    "answer": "We use a conductance tester that compares the battery's output with its rated cold cranking amps (CCA). Batteries that test below 70% of rated CCA are flagged for replacement. Batteries can lose up to 50% of their cranking power below 32\u00b0F (0\u00b0C).",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "Under state automotive repair regulations, customers retain the right to inspect and keep all replaced mechanical parts (excluding exchange items subject to manufacturer core charges, which may be inspected on-site before return to distributor). - Ask for your old parts when you authorize the work, and we will bag and tag them at the front desk. - Core-charge items (alternators, starters, brake calipers, and batteries) can be viewed on-site, but must go back to the distributor. Core charges are listed on the estimate. - Parts that are hazardous (batteries, fluids) will be handed over in sealed containers or disposed of in compliance with the rules. - Unclaimed parts are kept for **7 days** after pickup of the vehicle."}]

[{"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "Under state automotive repair regulations, customers retain the right to inspect and keep all replaced mechanical parts (excluding exchange items subject to manufacturer core charges, which may be inspected on-site before return to distributor). - Ask for your old parts when you authorize the work, and we will bag and tag them at the front desk. - Core-charge items (alternators, starters, brake calipers, and batteries) can be viewed on-site, but must go back to the distributor. Core charges are listed on the estimate. - Parts that are hazardous (batteries, fluids) will be handed over in sealed containers or disposed of in compliance with the rules. - Unclaimed parts are kept for **7 days** after pickup of the vehicle."}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "- Parts are warranted at the level of the manufacturer or longer. If the manufacturer's warranty is shorter than 24 months, NorthStar covers the remainder of our 24 months or 24,000 miles. - **Consequential Damage:** Towing, rental cars, lost time, and secondary damage are not covered, except where required by law. - Where state law gives you greater rights, the law applies."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-004",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "Does the warranty cover towing or a rental car?",
    "answer": "No. The warranty covers the repaired part and labor, and not towing, rentals, lost time, or consequential damage, except where state law requires otherwise.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-006",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "Can I keep the parts you replace?",
    "answer": "Yes. Ask when you authorize the work and we'll bag and tag them. Exchange items with a core charge, like alternators and starters, can be inspected on-site, but they must be returned to the distributor.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

