}"}, {"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "Under state automotive repair regulations, customers retain the right to inspect and keep all replaced mechanical parts (excluding exchange items subject to manufacturer core charges, which may be inspected on-site before return to distributor). - Ask for your old parts when you authorize the work, and we will bag and tag them at the front desk. - Core-charge items (alternators, starters, brake calipers, and batteries) can be viewed on-site, but must go back to the distributor. Core charges are listed on the estimate. - Parts that are hazardous (batteries, fluids) will be handed over in sealed containers or disposed of in compliance with the rules. - Unclaimed parts are kept for **7 days** after pickup of the vehicle."}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "- Parts are warranted at the level of the manufacturer or longer. If the manufacturer's warranty is shorter than 24 months, NorthStar covers the remainder of our 24 months or 24,000 miles. - **Consequential Damage:** Towing, rental cars, lost time, and secondary damage are not covered, except where required by law. - Where state law gives you greater rights, the law applies."}]

[{"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "| Covered | Not Covered | | :--- | :--- | | A water pump we replaced starts leaking at 14 months | Brake pads worn thin after 18,000 miles of normal driving | | A caliper seal leaks within warranty | Wiper blades that streak | | A starter we installed fails because of a defective part | A repair on a part you supplied | | A serpentine belt tensioner we installed was misinstalled | Failure caused by skipping oil changes or ignoring a DVI RED item | | A loose connection from our labor | Damage from racing, off-road use, or collision | *Table Summary:* [Clear Examples] - Covered: A water pump we replaced starts leaking at 14 months | Not Covered: Brake pads worn thin after 18,000 miles of normal driving - Covered: A caliper seal leaks within warranty | Not Covered: Wiper blades that streak - Covered: A starter we installed fails because of a defective part | Not Covered: A repair on a part you supplied - Covered: A serpentine belt tensioner we installed was misinstalled | Not Covered: Failure caused by skipping oil changes or ignoring a DVI RED item - Covered: A loose connection from our labor | Not Covered: Damage from racing, off-road use, or collision"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-002",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "A part you replaced failed while I'm traveling. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Call us or the nationwide warranty hotline before authorizing any repair, and have your invoice number ready. If you are at a participating facility, they diagnose the failure, and a covered repair costs you $0 for parts and labor.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. Stop driving the vehicle if the problem is a safety issue (brakes, steering, overheating). 2. Call NorthStar or the nationwide warranty hotline with your original invoice number. 3. Bring the vehicle to NorthStar or a participating facility. A technician will diagnose the failure. If it is covered, you pay $0 for parts and labor. 4. Keep your invoice and the maintenance records for your vehicle, because the warranty requires evidence of routine fluid maintenance. If we need to diagnose a failure that turns out not to be covered, the diagnostic fee applies (see Section 3)."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-005",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "Do I need to keep service records to keep my warranty valid?",
    "answer": "Yes. Keep your invoice and records of routine fluid maintenance such as oil and coolant changes. A failure caused by skipped routine maintenance is excluded.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

