}"}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Wash:** Rinse the vehicle every **10 to 14 days** during salt season, and after any storm, particularly the undercarriage, wheel wells, and rocker panels. Wash when temperatures are above 32°F (0°C) so the doors and locks don't freeze. - **Inspect:** Brake lines, fuel lines, and suspension components rust first. These are checked in the DVI. - **Protect:** Undercoating or wax-based rust inhibitors in the fall protect exposed metal, and a coat of wax on the paint protects the finish. - **Dry:** Lubricate door seals with silicone spray to prevent freezing. Wipe door jambs. - **Brake Components:** Salt corrodes calipers and slide pins, so we clean and lubricate them at each brake service."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-004",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "Does the warranty cover towing or a rental car?",
    "answer": "No. The warranty covers the repaired part and labor, and not towing, rentals, lost time, or consequential damage, except where state law requires otherwise.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "Under state automotive repair regulations, customers retain the right to inspect and keep all replaced mechanical parts (excluding exchange items subject to manufacturer core charges, which may be inspected on-site before return to distributor). - Ask for your old parts when you authorize the work, and we will bag and tag them at the front desk. - Core-charge items (alternators, starters, brake calipers, and batteries) can be viewed on-site, but must go back to the distributor. Core charges are listed on the estimate. - Parts that are hazardous (batteries, fluids) will be handed over in sealed containers or disposed of in compliance with the rules. - Unclaimed parts are kept for **7 days** after pickup of the vehicle."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-006",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "Can I keep the parts you replace?",
    "answer": "Yes. Ask when you authorize the work and we'll bag and tag them. Exchange items with a core charge, like alternators and starters, can be inspected on-site, but they must be returned to the distributor.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "- Parts are warranted at the level of the manufacturer or longer. If the manufacturer's warranty is shorter than 24 months, NorthStar covers the remainder of our 24 months or 24,000 miles. - **Consequential Damage:** Towing, rental cars, lost time, and secondary damage are not covered, except where required by law. - Where state law gives you greater rights, the law applies."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-003",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "Can I pre-authorize repairs so my drivers don't wait?",
    "answer": "Yes. Fleet managers set a pre-authorized repair limit per vehicle, per visit. The standard limit is $350.00, and it can be raised in writing for approved accounts. Repairs over the limit need written authorization.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-004",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "What are your billing terms for commercial accounts?",
    "answer": "Net-30 invoicing after a credit review. Consolidated monthly statements are itemized by VIN and your internal fleet unit ID, and issue on the first business day of each month.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "- Fleet managers designate a **pre-authorized repair limit (standard: $350.00)** to expedite workflow without waiting for written authorizations. - Repairs at or under the limit proceed immediately after the DVI. They are documented on the invoice. - Repairs **over the limit** need written authorization through the SMS or email approval link from a designated authorized contact. Alternatively, call the fleet desk. - The limit applies **per vehicle, per visit**, not per line item, and cannot be split to avoid authorization. - Limits can be raised in writing, up to $1,000.00 for approved Net-30 accounts, and can be set per unit ID. - Safety-critical RED items are always reported to the fleet manager, even if under the limit."}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "- **Terms:** Net-30 invoicing upon credit review approval. Credit review takes up to 3 business days. - **Consolidated Monthly Statements:** Itemized billing grouped by vehicle VIN and internal company fleet unit ID. Statements issue on the **1st business day** of each month for the previous month's work, due 30 days from the statement date. - **Late Balances:** Accounts more than 15 days past due may lose priority scheduling until the account is current. A 1.5% monthly finance charge applies after 30 days. - **Disputes:** Raise invoice questions within 14 days of the statement date. - **Warranty:** Fleet repairs receive the same 24-month/24,000-mile warranty as retail repairs, subject to the severe-duty exclusions in `WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md`."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-002",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "A part you replaced failed while I'm traveling. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Call us or the nationwide warranty hotline before authorizing any repair, and have your invoice number ready. If you are at a participating facility, they diagnose the failure, and a covered repair costs you $0 for parts and labor.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "| Covered | Not Covered | | :--- | :--- | | A water pump we replaced starts leaking at 14 months | Brake pads worn thin after 18,000 miles of normal driving | | A caliper seal leaks within warranty | Wiper blades that streak | | A starter we installed fails because of a defective part | A repair on a part you supplied | | A serpentine belt tensioner we installed was misinstalled | Failure caused by skipping oil changes or ignoring a DVI RED item | | A loose connection from our labor | Damage from racing, off-road use, or collision | *Table Summary:* [Clear Examples] - Covered: A water pump we replaced starts leaking at 14 months | Not Covered: Brake pads worn thin after 18,000 miles of normal driving - Covered: A caliper seal leaks within warranty | Not Covered: Wiper blades that streak - Covered: A starter we installed fails because of a defective part | Not Covered: A repair on a part you supplied - Covered: A serpentine belt tensioner we installed was misinstalled | Not Covered: Failure caused by skipping oil changes or ignoring a DVI RED item - Covered: A loose connection from our labor | Not Covered: Damage from racing, off-road use, or collision"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-005",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "Do I need to keep service records to keep my warranty valid?",
    "answer": "Yes. Keep your invoice and records of routine fluid maintenance such as oil and coolant changes. A failure caused by skipped routine maintenance is excluded.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. Stop driving the vehicle if the problem is a safety issue (brakes, steering, overheating). 2. Call NorthStar or the nationwide warranty hotline with your original invoice number. 3. Bring the vehicle to NorthStar or a participating facility. A technician will diagnose the failure. If it is covered, you pay $0 for parts and labor. 4. Keep your invoice and the maintenance records for your vehicle, because the warranty requires evidence of routine fluid maintenance. If we need to diagnose a failure that turns out not to be covered, the diagnostic fee applies (see Section 3)."}]

[{"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "1. Secure vehicle in designated Fleet North Lot parking stalls. 2. Complete the Fleet Work Order envelope detailing unit ID, current odometer, and primary driver complaint. 3. Deposit key into the tamper-evident dual-locking night drop safe located at the Bay 1 exterior wall. 4. Early shift dispatch technician logs intake scans into shop management software at **06:30 AM**. **Notes** - Lock the vehicle and remove valuables, fuel cards, and tools. - Any vehicle dropped after-hours is treated as received at 06:30 AM for SLA purposes. It does not qualify for the 08:30 AM same-day PM guarantee unless it was in the lot before 08:30 AM and logged by 06:30 AM, which is the standard case. - NorthStar is not responsible for items left in vehicles. - Our lot is lit and under camera surveillance."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-001",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "How do after-hours drop-offs work for commercial fleet vehicles?",
    "answer": "Park your vehicle in our secure Fleet North Lot stalls, complete the Fleet Work Order envelope with your fleet unit number, odometer, and driver notes, and place the key in the tamper-evident dual-locking drop safe at the Bay 1 exterior wall. Our early-shift dispatch team logs all vehicles at 6:30 AM for priority triage.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "**NorthStar Auto Care** — *Precision Diagnostics. Honest Service. Road-Ready Reliability.* Downtime costs a business money. This SOP sets out what fleet customers can expect from us, and what we need from you."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-005",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "Do you service heavy-duty trucks?",
    "answer": "We service commercial light fleets, such as vans and light trucks. Vehicles above 14,000 lb GVWR are outside our standard scope, so please call us to discuss your unit.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}]

