    }
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-005",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "Do I need to keep service records to keep my warranty valid?",
    "answer": "Yes. Keep your invoice and records of routine fluid maintenance such as oil and coolant changes. A failure caused by skipped routine maintenance is excluded.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-005",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "Do you service heavy-duty trucks?",
    "answer": "We service commercial light fleets, such as vans and light trucks. Vehicles above 14,000 lb GVWR are outside our standard scope, so please call us to discuss your unit.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MNT-002",
    "category": "Routine Maintenance",
    "question": "What happens at the 30,000-mile service?",
    "answer": "Tier 3 includes a full synthetic oil change, a DOT 4 brake fluid exchange, engine and cabin air filters, a cooling system freeze-point and pH audit, and a battery CCA conductance test. It takes about 2.5 labor hours and the base package is $349.50.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "Fleet vehicles are placed ahead of retail customers in the bay queue, with safety-critical repairs and customer emergencies taking precedence over both. | Service Class | Examples | Guaranteed Turnaround | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | **Preventative Maintenance (PM Tier 1)** | Oil and filter, tire rotation, DVI | **Same-day (under 4 hours)** for drop-offs before **08:30 AM** | | **Minor Mechanical Repairs** | Brakes, alternators, starters | **24-hour** turnaround window | | **Major Drivetrain Overhauls** | Transmission, engine, differential | Dedicated bay allocation with **daily status progress dispatch** | *Table Summary:* [1. Priority Triage & Guaranteed Turnaround (SLA)] - Service Class: Preventative Maintenance (PM Tier 1) | Examples: Oil and filter, tire rotation, DVI | Guaranteed Turnaround: Same-day (under 4 hours) for drop-offs before 08:30 AM - Service Class: Minor Mechanical Repairs | Examples: Brakes, alternators, starters | Guaranteed Turnaround: 24-hour turnaround window - Service Class: Major Drivetrain Overhauls | Examples: Transmission, engine, differential | Guaranteed Turnaround: Dedicated bay allocation with daily status progress dispatch - **Clock Start:** The SLA clock starts when the vehicle is logged into our shop management software, and when diagnostic approval is received if the repair requires authorization above the pre-authorized limit. - **Parts Delays:** If a part is not available locally, we source it from a second supplier. We notify the fleet manager within **2 hours** of discovering a delay, with the new estimated completion time. - **SLA Exceptions:** Delays caused by awaiting approval, hidden damage found during teardown (see `ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md`), or manufacturer back-orders pause the SLA clock. - **Severe-Duty Notice:** Vehicles with GVWR above 14,000 lb are outside the light-fleet scope. Call us to discuss them."}, {"source": "service_intervals_matrix.json", "quote": "{
    "service": "Front brake pads and rotors, per axle",
    "labor_hours": 1.5
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MNT-005",
    "category": "Routine Maintenance",
    "question": "How much tread do my tires need in winter?",
    "answer": "At least 4/32 inch for snow traction, even though the legal minimum is 2/32 inch. All-season rubber also hardens below 45\u00b0F (7\u00b0C), so dedicated winter tires are recommended for sub-freezing driving.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Winter Tread Minimum:** All-season tires require a minimum of **4/32 inch** tread depth for snow traction (replacing normal 2/32 inch legal limit). - **How to Check:** Insert a quarter upside down with Washington's head into the groove. If the top of his head is visible, you are below 4/32 inch. We measure all four tires with a depth gauge during the DVI. - **Compound Glass Transition:** All-season rubber compounds harden below 45°F (7°C), significantly increasing braking distances. Dedicated winter tires recommended for sub-freezing regional travel. - **Winter Tires:** Look for the three-peak mountain snowflake symbol. Install a full set of four, and never just two. - **Tire Pressure:** Pressure drops about **1 psi for every 10°F (5.5°C)** drop in temperature. Check monthly with the tires cold, and set to the pressure on the driver-door placard."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MNT-001",
    "category": "Routine Maintenance",
    "question": "How often should I change my oil?",
    "answer": "Every 5,000 miles or 6 months with a full synthetic oil that meets API SP / ILSAC GF-6 (0W-20 or 5W-30, per your owner's manual). Our Tier 1 service includes the oil and OEM filter, a tire rotation, a brake measurement, and a 40-point inspection for $89.95.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "service_intervals_matrix.json", "quote": "{
    "service": "Tire mount, balance, and install (set of 4)",
    "labor_hours": 1.2
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-APPT-001",
    "category": "Appointments & Loaners",
    "question": "Do you offer loaner vehicles or shuttle services while my car is being serviced?",
    "answer": "Yes. We offer complimentary local shuttle rides within a 10-mile radius. For repairs exceeding $600 or taking longer than 24 hours, complimentary courtesy loaner cars are available upon reservation request (subject to driver license and insurance verification).",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "- Parts are warranted at the level of the manufacturer or longer. If the manufacturer's warranty is shorter than 24 months, NorthStar covers the remainder of our 24 months or 24,000 miles. - **Consequential Damage:** Towing, rental cars, lost time, and secondary damage are not covered, except where required by law. - Where state law gives you greater rights, the law applies."}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "NorthStar carries garage liability insurance. Report any damage that occurred while your vehicle was in our care **before leaving the lot**, or within 24 hours, and we will investigate."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-003",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "Can I pre-authorize repairs so my drivers don't wait?",
    "answer": "Yes. Fleet managers set a pre-authorized repair limit per vehicle, per visit. The standard limit is $350.00, and it can be raised in writing for approved accounts. Repairs over the limit need written authorization.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "| Covered | Not Covered | | :--- | :--- | | A water pump we replaced starts leaking at 14 months | Brake pads worn thin after 18,000 miles of normal driving | | A caliper seal leaks within warranty | Wiper blades that streak | | A starter we installed fails because of a defective part | A repair on a part you supplied | | A serpentine belt tensioner we installed was misinstalled | Failure caused by skipping oil changes or ignoring a DVI RED item | | A loose connection from our labor | Damage from racing, off-road use, or collision | *Table Summary:* [Clear Examples] - Covered: A water pump we replaced starts leaking at 14 months | Not Covered: Brake pads worn thin after 18,000 miles of normal driving - Covered: A caliper seal leaks within warranty | Not Covered: Wiper blades that streak - Covered: A starter we installed fails because of a defective part | Not Covered: A repair on a part you supplied - Covered: A serpentine belt tensioner we installed was misinstalled | Not Covered: Failure caused by skipping oil changes or ignoring a DVI RED item - Covered: A loose connection from our labor | Not Covered: Damage from racing, off-road use, or collision"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-002",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "A part you replaced failed while I'm traveling. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Call us or the nationwide warranty hotline before authorizing any repair, and have your invoice number ready. If you are at a participating facility, they diagnose the failure, and a covered repair costs you $0 for parts and labor.",
