[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-APPT-004",
    "category": "Appointments & Loaners",
    "question": "My car was damaged while at your shop. What do I do?",
    "answer": "Please tell us right away, ideally before leaving the lot, or within 24 hours, and bring photos. A manager reviews every damage report and will contact you.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-002",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "A part you replaced failed while I'm traveling. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Call us or the nationwide warranty hotline before authorizing any repair, and have your invoice number ready. If you are at a participating facility, they diagnose the failure, and a covered repair costs you $0 for parts and labor.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "Under state automotive repair regulations, customers retain the right to inspect and keep all replaced mechanical parts (excluding exchange items subject to manufacturer core charges, which may be inspected on-site before return to distributor). - Ask for your old parts when you authorize the work, and we will bag and tag them at the front desk. - Core-charge items (alternators, starters, brake calipers, and batteries) can be viewed on-site, but must go back to the distributor. Core charges are listed on the estimate. - Parts that are hazardous (batteries, fluids) will be handed over in sealed containers or disposed of in compliance with the rules. - Unclaimed parts are kept for **7 days** after pickup of the vehicle."}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Wash:** Rinse the vehicle every **10 to 14 days** during salt season, and after any storm, particularly the undercarriage, wheel wells, and rocker panels. Wash when temperatures are above 32°F (0°C) so the doors and locks don't freeze. - **Inspect:** Brake lines, fuel lines, and suspension components rust first. These are checked in the DVI. - **Protect:** Undercoating or wax-based rust inhibitors in the fall protect exposed metal, and a coat of wax on the paint protects the finish. - **Dry:** Lubricate door seals with silicone spray to prevent freezing. Wipe door jambs. - **Brake Components:** Salt corrodes calipers and slide pins, so we clean and lubricate them at each brake service."}]

