    "answer": "Yes. We offer complimentary local shuttle rides within a 10-mile radius. For repairs exceeding $600 or taking longer than 24 hours, complimentary courtesy loaner cars are available upon reservation request (subject to driver license and insurance verification).",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-002",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "How fast will you turn around my fleet vehicles?",
    "answer": "Preventative maintenance (PM Tier 1) is same-day, under 4 hours, for drop-offs before 8:30 AM. Minor repairs such as brakes, alternators, and starters have a 24-hour window. Major drivetrain overhauls get a dedicated bay and a daily status update.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "| Covered | Not Covered | | :--- | :--- | | A water pump we replaced starts leaking at 14 months | Brake pads worn thin after 18,000 miles of normal driving | | A caliper seal leaks within warranty | Wiper blades that streak | | A starter we installed fails because of a defective part | A repair on a part you supplied | | A serpentine belt tensioner we installed was misinstalled | Failure caused by skipping oil changes or ignoring a DVI RED item | | A loose connection from our labor | Damage from racing, off-road use, or collision | *Table Summary:* [Clear Examples] - Covered: A water pump we replaced starts leaking at 14 months | Not Covered: Brake pads worn thin after 18,000 miles of normal driving - Covered: A caliper seal leaks within warranty | Not Covered: Wiper blades that streak - Covered: A starter we installed fails because of a defective part | Not Covered: A repair on a part you supplied - Covered: A serpentine belt tensioner we installed was misinstalled | Not Covered: Failure caused by skipping oil changes or ignoring a DVI RED item - Covered: A loose connection from our labor | Not Covered: Damage from racing, off-road use, or collision"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "- **Terms:** Net-30 invoicing upon credit review approval. Credit review takes up to 3 business days. - **Consolidated Monthly Statements:** Itemized billing grouped by vehicle VIN and internal company fleet unit ID. Statements issue on the **1st business day** of each month for the previous month's work, due 30 days from the statement date. - **Late Balances:** Accounts more than 15 days past due may lose priority scheduling until the account is current. A 1.5% monthly finance charge applies after 30 days. - **Disputes:** Raise invoice questions within 14 days of the statement date. - **Warranty:** Fleet repairs receive the same 24-month/24,000-mile warranty as retail repairs, subject to the severe-duty exclusions in `WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md`."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-005",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "Do you service heavy-duty trucks?",
    "answer": "We service commercial light fleets, such as vans and light trucks. Vehicles above 14,000 lb GVWR are outside our standard scope, so please call us to discuss your unit.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-001",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "How do after-hours drop-offs work for commercial fleet vehicles?",
    "answer": "Park your vehicle in our secure Fleet North Lot stalls, complete the Fleet Work Order envelope with your fleet unit number, odometer, and driver notes, and place the key in the tamper-evident dual-locking drop safe at the Bay 1 exterior wall. Our early-shift dispatch team logs all vehicles at 6:30 AM for priority triage.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "Fleet vehicles are placed ahead of retail customers in the bay queue, with safety-critical repairs and customer emergencies taking precedence over both. | Service Class | Examples | Guaranteed Turnaround | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | **Preventative Maintenance (PM Tier 1)** | Oil and filter, tire rotation, DVI | **Same-day (under 4 hours)** for drop-offs before **08:30 AM** | | **Minor Mechanical Repairs** | Brakes, alternators, starters | **24-hour** turnaround window | | **Major Drivetrain Overhauls** | Transmission, engine, differential | Dedicated bay allocation with **daily status progress dispatch** | *Table Summary:* [1. Priority Triage & Guaranteed Turnaround (SLA)] - Service Class: Preventative Maintenance (PM Tier 1) | Examples: Oil and filter, tire rotation, DVI | Guaranteed Turnaround: Same-day (under 4 hours) for drop-offs before 08:30 AM - Service Class: Minor Mechanical Repairs | Examples: Brakes, alternators, starters | Guaranteed Turnaround: 24-hour turnaround window - Service Class: Major Drivetrain Overhauls | Examples: Transmission, engine, differential | Guaranteed Turnaround: Dedicated bay allocation with daily status progress dispatch - **Clock Start:** The SLA clock starts when the vehicle is logged into our shop management software, and when diagnostic approval is received if the repair requires authorization above the pre-authorized limit. - **Parts Delays:** If a part is not available locally, we source it from a second supplier. We notify the fleet manager within **2 hours** of discovering a delay, with the new estimated completion time. - **SLA Exceptions:** Delays caused by awaiting approval, hidden damage found during teardown (see `ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md`), or manufacturer back-orders pause the SLA clock. - **Severe-Duty Notice:** Vehicles with GVWR above 14,000 lb are outside the light-fleet scope. Call us to discuss them."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-004",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "What happens if you find more problems after taking my car apart?",
    "answer": "Work stops immediately and we send a supplement estimate by SMS with photos. You must approve it separately before we continue. The final bill will not exceed the authorized total by more than 10% or $50.00, whichever is less, without a new approval.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-APPT-001",
    "category": "Appointments & Loaners",
    "question": "Do you offer loaner vehicles or shuttle services while my car is being serviced?",
    "answer": "Yes. We offer complimentary local shuttle rides within a 10-mile radius. For repairs exceeding $600 or taking longer than 24 hours, complimentary courtesy loaner cars are available upon reservation request (subject to driver license and insurance verification).",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "- **Terms:** Net-30 invoicing upon credit review approval. Credit review takes up to 3 business days. - **Consolidated Monthly Statements:** Itemized billing grouped by vehicle VIN and internal company fleet unit ID. Statements issue on the **1st business day** of each month for the previous month's work, due 30 days from the statement date. - **Late Balances:** Accounts more than 15 days past due may lose priority scheduling until the account is current. A 1.5% monthly finance charge applies after 30 days. - **Disputes:** Raise invoice questions within 14 days of the statement date. - **Warranty:** Fleet repairs receive the same 24-month/24,000-mile warranty as retail repairs, subject to the severe-duty exclusions in `WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md`."}, {"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "- If more work is found, the technician stops, photographs the issue, and the advisor sends a **supplement estimate** by SMS. - Supplements follow the same approval workflow, and the original authorization does not cover them. - If the supplement is declined, we reassemble the vehicle. Teardown and reassembly labor already performed is billed at the quoted rate, and we explain it before starting. - **Price Variance Rule:** The final bill won't exceed the authorized total by more than 10% or $50.00 (whichever is less) without a new written approval."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-006",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "Can I keep the parts you replace?",
    "answer": "Yes. Ask when you authorize the work and we'll bag and tag them. Exchange items with a core charge, like alternators and starters, can be inspected on-site, but they must be returned to the distributor.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-004",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "Does the warranty cover towing or a rental car?",
    "answer": "No. The warranty covers the repaired part and labor, and not towing, rentals, lost time, or consequential damage, except where state law requires otherwise.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "- Parts are warranted at the level of the manufacturer or longer. If the manufacturer's warranty is shorter than 24 months, NorthStar covers the remainder of our 24 months or 24,000 miles. - **Consequential Damage:** Towing, rental cars, lost time, and secondary damage are not covered, except where required by law. - Where state law gives you greater rights, the law applies."}, {"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "Under state automotive repair regulations, customers retain the right to inspect and keep all replaced mechanical parts (excluding exchange items subject to manufacturer core charges, which may be inspected on-site before return to distributor). - Ask for your old parts when you authorize the work, and we will bag and tag them at the front desk. - Core-charge items (alternators, starters, brake calipers, and batteries) can be viewed on-site, but must go back to the distributor. Core charges are listed on the estimate. - Parts that are hazardous (batteries, fluids) will be handed over in sealed containers or disposed of in compliance with the rules. - Unclaimed parts are kept for **7 days** after pickup of the vehicle."}]

[{"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Wash:** Rinse the vehicle every **10 to 14 days** during salt season, and after any storm, particularly the undercarriage, wheel wells, and rocker panels. Wash when temperatures are above 32°F (0°C) so the doors and locks don't freeze. - **Inspect:** Brake lines, fuel lines, and suspension components rust first. These are checked in the DVI. - **Protect:** Undercoating or wax-based rust inhibitors in the fall protect exposed metal, and a coat of wax on the paint protects the finish. - **Dry:** Lubricate door seals with silicone spray to prevent freezing. Wipe door jambs. - **Brake Components:** Salt corrodes calipers and slide pins, so we clean and lubricate them at each brake service."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MNT-004",
    "category": "Routine Maintenance",
    "question": "What coolant mix protects against freezing?",
    "answer": "A 50/50 mix of ethylene glycol and deionized water protects to -34\u00b0F (-37\u00b0C). We check it with a hydrometer. Richer than about 70% glycol actually freezes at a higher temperature, so more is not better. Don't mix different coolant types.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "| Item | What We Do | Why | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | Engine oil | Check viscosity grade (0W-20 or 5W-30 full synthetic as specified) | Thick oil strains the starter | | Wiper blades | Replace if streaking, and use winter-rated washer fluid rated to -20°F (-29°C) | Visibility | | Brake fluid | Test moisture content, replace if above 3% | Moisture freezes and corrodes | | Belts and hoses | Inspect for cracks | Cold makes rubber brittle | | Heater and defroster | Test output | Safety | *Table Summary:* [5. Other Cold-Weather Checks] - Item: Engine oil | What We Do: Check viscosity grade (0W-20 or 5W-30 full synthetic as specified) | Why: Thick oil strains the starter - Item: Wiper blades | What We Do: Replace if streaking, and use winter-rated washer fluid rated to -20°F (-29°C) | Why: Visibility - Item: Brake fluid | What We Do: Test moisture content, replace if above 3% | Why: Moisture freezes and corrodes - Item: Belts and hoses | What We Do: Inspect for cracks | Why: Cold makes rubber brittle - Item: Heater and defroster | What We Do: Test output | Why: Safety"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-004",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "Does the warranty cover towing or a rental car?",
    "answer": "No. The warranty covers the repaired part and labor, and not towing, rentals, lost time, or consequential damage, except where state law requires otherwise.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-004",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "What happens if you find more problems after taking my car apart?",
    "answer": "Work stops immediately and we send a supplement estimate by SMS with photos. You must approve it separately before we continue. The final bill will not exceed the authorized total by more than 10% or $50.00, whichever is less, without a new approval.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-003",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "Will you start work before I approve the estimate?",
    "answer": "No. Estimates are sent by SMS and email with inspection photos, and you approve or decline each line item individually. No repair work begins without a digital or written signature.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. The service advisor sends the estimate by SMS (secure link) and email, listing each line item with parts, labor hours, tax, and the total. 2. The customer opens the link and sees the DVI photos and notes for each item. 3. The customer **approves or declines each line item individually**, then signs digitally. 4. The system timestamps the approval and sends a confirmation message with the authorized total. 5. If we haven't heard from you in **2 hours**, we call. We never begin work on silence. 6. Customers without a smartphone can approve in person or by phone with the advisor, and we record the call with consent."}, {"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "- **No Verbal Guesswork:** Written estimates are delivered via SMS and email with embedded inspection photos. - **Explicit Customer Approval:** No repair work commences without digital or physical written signature authorization. - **Teardown Supplements:** If hidden mechanical damage is discovered post-disassembly, work stops immediately, and a formal supplement estimate is dispatched."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MNT-001",
    "category": "Routine Maintenance",
