    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "Fleet vehicles are placed ahead of retail customers in the bay queue, with safety-critical repairs and customer emergencies taking precedence over both. | Service Class | Examples | Guaranteed Turnaround | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | **Preventative Maintenance (PM Tier 1)** | Oil and filter, tire rotation, DVI | **Same-day (under 4 hours)** for drop-offs before **08:30 AM** | | **Minor Mechanical Repairs** | Brakes, alternators, starters | **24-hour** turnaround window | | **Major Drivetrain Overhauls** | Transmission, engine, differential | Dedicated bay allocation with **daily status progress dispatch** | *Table Summary:* [1. Priority Triage & Guaranteed Turnaround (SLA)] - Service Class: Preventative Maintenance (PM Tier 1) | Examples: Oil and filter, tire rotation, DVI | Guaranteed Turnaround: Same-day (under 4 hours) for drop-offs before 08:30 AM - Service Class: Minor Mechanical Repairs | Examples: Brakes, alternators, starters | Guaranteed Turnaround: 24-hour turnaround window - Service Class: Major Drivetrain Overhauls | Examples: Transmission, engine, differential | Guaranteed Turnaround: Dedicated bay allocation with daily status progress dispatch - **Clock Start:** The SLA clock starts when the vehicle is logged into our shop management software, and when diagnostic approval is received if the repair requires authorization above the pre-authorized limit. - **Parts Delays:** If a part is not available locally, we source it from a second supplier. We notify the fleet manager within **2 hours** of discovering a delay, with the new estimated completion time. - **SLA Exceptions:** Delays caused by awaiting approval, hidden damage found during teardown (see `ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md`), or manufacturer back-orders pause the SLA clock. - **Severe-Duty Notice:** Vehicles with GVWR above 14,000 lb are outside the light-fleet scope. Call us to discuss them."}, {"source": "service_intervals_matrix.json", "quote": "{
