[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-002",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "A part you replaced failed while I'm traveling. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Call us or the nationwide warranty hotline before authorizing any repair, and have your invoice number ready. If you are at a participating facility, they diagnose the failure, and a covered repair costs you $0 for parts and labor.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "service_intervals_matrix.json", "quote": "{
    "service": "Serpentine belt replacement",
    "labor_hours": 0.8
}"}, {"source": "service_intervals_matrix.json", "quote": "maintenance_matrix_metadata:
{
    "shop": "NorthStar Auto Care",
    "standard_version": "2024.1",
    "labor_rate_standard_hourly": 145.0,
    "currency": "USD",
    "mileage_units": "miles",
    "note": "Intervals are baselines. The manufacturer's published schedule takes priority. Whichever of mileage or months occurs first triggers service. Package costs exclude tax and any repairs found during inspection."
}"}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "NorthStar Auto Care warrants all parts and labor performed by our ASE-certified technicians for **24 months or 24,000 miles**, whichever occurs first. - **Coverage:** Mechanical parts replacement failure, installation labor defects, and hydraulic seal leaks. Both **parts and labor** are covered at no charge for the repaired component. - **Nationwide Protection:** Valid at over 35,000 certified participating repair centers across North America. If you are more than 25 miles from NorthStar, call the warranty hotline before authorizing any repair so the claim can be validated. - **Exclusions:** Commercial severe-duty abuse, auto racing, lack of subsequent routine fluid maintenance, customer-supplied parts, and normal brake pad/wiper friction wear."}]

[{"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "1. Secure vehicle in designated Fleet North Lot parking stalls. 2. Complete the Fleet Work Order envelope detailing unit ID, current odometer, and primary driver complaint. 3. Deposit key into the tamper-evident dual-locking night drop safe located at the Bay 1 exterior wall. 4. Early shift dispatch technician logs intake scans into shop management software at **06:30 AM**. **Notes** - Lock the vehicle and remove valuables, fuel cards, and tools. - Any vehicle dropped after-hours is treated as received at 06:30 AM for SLA purposes. It does not qualify for the 08:30 AM same-day PM guarantee unless it was in the lot before 08:30 AM and logged by 06:30 AM, which is the standard case. - NorthStar is not responsible for items left in vehicles. - Our lot is lit and under camera surveillance."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-003",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "Can I pre-authorize repairs so my drivers don't wait?",
    "answer": "Yes. Fleet managers set a pre-authorized repair limit per vehicle, per visit. The standard limit is $350.00, and it can be raised in writing for approved accounts. Repairs over the limit need written authorization.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-001",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "How do after-hours drop-offs work for commercial fleet vehicles?",
    "answer": "Park your vehicle in our secure Fleet North Lot stalls, complete the Fleet Work Order envelope with your fleet unit number, odometer, and driver notes, and place the key in the tamper-evident dual-locking drop safe at the Bay 1 exterior wall. Our early-shift dispatch team logs all vehicles at 6:30 AM for priority triage.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. Stop driving the vehicle if the problem is a safety issue (brakes, steering, overheating). 2. Call NorthStar or the nationwide warranty hotline with your original invoice number. 3. Bring the vehicle to NorthStar or a participating facility. A technician will diagnose the failure. If it is covered, you pay $0 for parts and labor. 4. Keep your invoice and the maintenance records for your vehicle, because the warranty requires evidence of routine fluid maintenance. If we need to diagnose a failure that turns out not to be covered, the diagnostic fee applies (see Section 3)."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MNT-004",
    "category": "Routine Maintenance",
    "question": "What coolant mix protects against freezing?",
    "answer": "A 50/50 mix of ethylene glycol and deionized water protects to -34\u00b0F (-37\u00b0C). We check it with a hydrometer. Richer than about 70% glycol actually freezes at a higher temperature, so more is not better. Don't mix different coolant types.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Concentration Target:** 50/50 ethylene glycol and deionized water mixture providing freeze protection down to **-34°F (-37°C)**. - **Testing:** A hydrometer or refractometer measures the density of the coolant, and the reading is converted to a freeze point. We test it when the engine is cool. - **Pass:** -34°F (-37°C) or lower. - **Marginal:** -20°F to -33°F (-29°C to -36°C), so we top off with proper mix or flush the system. - **Fail:** Warmer than -20°F (-29°C). Flush and refill. - **Don't Overconcentrate:** A mix richer than 70% glycol freezes at a *higher* temperature and transfers heat less effectively. Use pre-mixed or deionized water, and never tap water. - **Boil-over & Corrosion Protection:** Fresh inhibitor additives prevent internal engine block scale and heater core pinhole corrosion. A 50/50 mix also raises the boiling point to about 265°F (129°C) with a 15 psi cap. - **Coolant Types:** Use the type your manufacturer requires (OAT, HOAT, or IAT) and don't mix types, because they can gel. Typical service interval is 30,000 to 60,000 miles for extended-life coolants (see `service_intervals_matrix.json`)."}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Wash:** Rinse the vehicle every **10 to 14 days** during salt season, and after any storm, particularly the undercarriage, wheel wells, and rocker panels. Wash when temperatures are above 32°F (0°C) so the doors and locks don't freeze. - **Inspect:** Brake lines, fuel lines, and suspension components rust first. These are checked in the DVI. - **Protect:** Undercoating or wax-based rust inhibitors in the fall protect exposed metal, and a coat of wax on the paint protects the finish. - **Dry:** Lubricate door seals with silicone spray to prevent freezing. Wipe door jambs. - **Brake Components:** Salt corrodes calipers and slide pins, so we clean and lubricate them at each brake service."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-001",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "How much does a check engine light diagnosis cost?",
    "answer": "Our comprehensive diagnostic fee is $145.00, which includes computerized OBD-II telemetry scan, circuit testing, and up to one hour of hands-on mechanical triage. If you approve the recommended repair with us, 100% of the $145.00 diagnostic fee is credited directly toward your repair labor.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MNT-003",
    "category": "Routine Maintenance",
    "question": "How do you test whether my battery will survive winter?",
    "answer": "We use a conductance tester that compares the battery's output with its rated cold cranking amps (CCA). Batteries that test below 70% of rated CCA are flagged for replacement. Batteries can lose up to 50% of their cranking power below 32\u00b0F (0\u00b0C).",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "Blanket, flashlight, jumper cables, ice scraper, small shovel, sand or kitty litter for traction, phone charger, water, and snacks. Keep your fuel tank at least **half full** at all times in winter."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-004",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "Does the warranty cover towing or a rental car?",
    "answer": "No. The warranty covers the repaired part and labor, and not towing, rentals, lost time, or consequential damage, except where state law requires otherwise.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "| Item | What We Do | Why | | :--- | :--- | :--- | | Engine oil | Check viscosity grade (0W-20 or 5W-30 full synthetic as specified) | Thick oil strains the starter | | Wiper blades | Replace if streaking, and use winter-rated washer fluid rated to -20°F (-29°C) | Visibility | | Brake fluid | Test moisture content, replace if above 3% | Moisture freezes and corrodes | | Belts and hoses | Inspect for cracks | Cold makes rubber brittle | | Heater and defroster | Test output | Safety | *Table Summary:* [5. Other Cold-Weather Checks] - Item: Engine oil | What We Do: Check viscosity grade (0W-20 or 5W-30 full synthetic as specified) | Why: Thick oil strains the starter - Item: Wiper blades | What We Do: Replace if streaking, and use winter-rated washer fluid rated to -20°F (-29°C) | Why: Visibility - Item: Brake fluid | What We Do: Test moisture content, replace if above 3% | Why: Moisture freezes and corrodes - Item: Belts and hoses | What We Do: Inspect for cracks | Why: Cold makes rubber brittle - Item: Heater and defroster | What We Do: Test output | Why: Safety"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-001",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "How do after-hours drop-offs work for commercial fleet vehicles?",
    "answer": "Park your vehicle in our secure Fleet North Lot stalls, complete the Fleet Work Order envelope with your fleet unit number, odometer, and driver notes, and place the key in the tamper-evident dual-locking drop safe at the Bay 1 exterior wall. Our early-shift dispatch team logs all vehicles at 6:30 AM for priority triage.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "- Morning dispatch begins at **06:30 AM** with the early-shift dispatch technician logging after-hours drop-offs and arranging the day's bay assignments. - **Priority Order:** (1) Safety-critical (RED) fleet repairs, (2) PM Tier 1 drop-offs received before 08:30 AM, (3) scheduled minor repairs, (4) other fleet work, (5) retail customers. - Fleet managers receive a text and email with a work-order number for each unit by **07:30 AM**. - Fleet DVI reports are issued within **90 minutes** of drop-off, with photos and a color grade for each of the 40 inspection points. - Pickup updates: Units are staged in the Fleet North Lot, and keys are available at the front desk from 7:00 AM."}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "1. Secure vehicle in designated Fleet North Lot parking stalls. 2. Complete the Fleet Work Order envelope detailing unit ID, current odometer, and primary driver complaint. 3. Deposit key into the tamper-evident dual-locking night drop safe located at the Bay 1 exterior wall. 4. Early shift dispatch technician logs intake scans into shop management software at **06:30 AM**. **Notes** - Lock the vehicle and remove valuables, fuel cards, and tools. - Any vehicle dropped after-hours is treated as received at 06:30 AM for SLA purposes. It does not qualify for the 08:30 AM same-day PM guarantee unless it was in the lot before 08:30 AM and logged by 06:30 AM, which is the standard case. - NorthStar is not responsible for items left in vehicles. - Our lot is lit and under camera surveillance."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-005",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "Do you service heavy-duty trucks?",
    "answer": "We service commercial light fleets, such as vans and light trucks. Vehicles above 14,000 lb GVWR are outside our standard scope, so please call us to discuss your unit.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}]

