[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-004",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "What happens if you find more problems after taking my car apart?",
    "answer": "Work stops immediately and we send a supplement estimate by SMS with photos. You must approve it separately before we continue. The final bill will not exceed the authorized total by more than 10% or $50.00, whichever is less, without a new approval.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-003",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "Will you start work before I approve the estimate?",
    "answer": "No. Estimates are sent by SMS and email with inspection photos, and you approve or decline each line item individually. No repair work begins without a digital or written signature.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. The service advisor sends the estimate by SMS (secure link) and email, listing each line item with parts, labor hours, tax, and the total. 2. The customer opens the link and sees the DVI photos and notes for each item. 3. The customer **approves or declines each line item individually**, then signs digitally. 4. The system timestamps the approval and sends a confirmation message with the authorized total. 5. If we haven't heard from you in **2 hours**, we call. We never begin work on silence. 6. Customers without a smartphone can approve in person or by phone with the advisor, and we record the call with consent."}, {"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "- If more work is found, the technician stops, photographs the issue, and the advisor sends a **supplement estimate** by SMS. - Supplements follow the same approval workflow, and the original authorization does not cover them. - If the supplement is declined, we reassemble the vehicle. Teardown and reassembly labor already performed is billed at the quoted rate, and we explain it before starting. - **Price Variance Rule:** The final bill won't exceed the authorized total by more than 10% or $50.00 (whichever is less) without a new written approval."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-APPT-004",
    "category": "Appointments & Loaners",
    "question": "My car was damaged while at your shop. What do I do?",
    "answer": "Please tell us right away, ideally before leaving the lot, or within 24 hours, and bring photos. A manager reviews every damage report and will contact you.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-002",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "A part you replaced failed while I'm traveling. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Call us or the nationwide warranty hotline before authorizing any repair, and have your invoice number ready. If you are at a participating facility, they diagnose the failure, and a covered repair costs you $0 for parts and labor.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Wash:** Rinse the vehicle every **10 to 14 days** during salt season, and after any storm, particularly the undercarriage, wheel wells, and rocker panels. Wash when temperatures are above 32°F (0°C) so the doors and locks don't freeze. - **Inspect:** Brake lines, fuel lines, and suspension components rust first. These are checked in the DVI. - **Protect:** Undercoating or wax-based rust inhibitors in the fall protect exposed metal, and a coat of wax on the paint protects the finish. - **Dry:** Lubricate door seals with silicone spray to prevent freezing. Wipe door jambs. - **Brake Components:** Salt corrodes calipers and slide pins, so we clean and lubricate them at each brake service."}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "1. Stop driving the vehicle if the problem is a safety issue (brakes, steering, overheating). 2. Call NorthStar or the nationwide warranty hotline with your original invoice number. 3. Bring the vehicle to NorthStar or a participating facility. A technician will diagnose the failure. If it is covered, you pay $0 for parts and labor. 4. Keep your invoice and the maintenance records for your vehicle, because the warranty requires evidence of routine fluid maintenance. If we need to diagnose a failure that turns out not to be covered, the diagnostic fee applies (see Section 3)."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-003",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "Can I pre-authorize repairs so my drivers don't wait?",
    "answer": "Yes. Fleet managers set a pre-authorized repair limit per vehicle, per visit. The standard limit is $350.00, and it can be raised in writing for approved accounts. Repairs over the limit need written authorization.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "- **Terms:** Net-30 invoicing upon credit review approval. Credit review takes up to 3 business days. - **Consolidated Monthly Statements:** Itemized billing grouped by vehicle VIN and internal company fleet unit ID. Statements issue on the **1st business day** of each month for the previous month's work, due 30 days from the statement date. - **Late Balances:** Accounts more than 15 days past due may lose priority scheduling until the account is current. A 1.5% monthly finance charge applies after 30 days. - **Disputes:** Raise invoice questions within 14 days of the statement date. - **Warranty:** Fleet repairs receive the same 24-month/24,000-mile warranty as retail repairs, subject to the severe-duty exclusions in `WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md`."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-APPT-001",
    "category": "Appointments & Loaners",
    "question": "Do you offer loaner vehicles or shuttle services while my car is being serviced?",
    "answer": "Yes. We offer complimentary local shuttle rides within a 10-mile radius. For repairs exceeding $600 or taking longer than 24 hours, complimentary courtesy loaner cars are available upon reservation request (subject to driver license and insurance verification).",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "- Fleet managers designate a **pre-authorized repair limit (standard: $350.00)** to expedite workflow without waiting for written authorizations. - Repairs at or under the limit proceed immediately after the DVI. They are documented on the invoice. - Repairs **over the limit** need written authorization through the SMS or email approval link from a designated authorized contact. Alternatively, call the fleet desk. - The limit applies **per vehicle, per visit**, not per line item, and cannot be split to avoid authorization. - Limits can be raised in writing, up to $1,000.00 for approved Net-30 accounts, and can be set per unit ID. - Safety-critical RED items are always reported to the fleet manager, even if under the limit."}]

[{"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "- Parts are warranted at the level of the manufacturer or longer. If the manufacturer's warranty is shorter than 24 months, NorthStar covers the remainder of our 24 months or 24,000 miles. - **Consequential Damage:** Towing, rental cars, lost time, and secondary damage are not covered, except where required by law. - Where state law gives you greater rights, the law applies."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-FLT-003",
    "category": "Fleet Services",
    "question": "Can I pre-authorize repairs so my drivers don't wait?",
    "answer": "Yes. Fleet managers set a pre-authorized repair limit per vehicle, per visit. The standard limit is $350.00, and it can be raised in writing for approved accounts. Repairs over the limit need written authorization.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-001",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "What is covered under the NorthStar Peace of Mind Warranty?",
    "answer": "Our warranty covers parts and labor on qualifying mechanical repairs for 24 months or 24,000 miles, whichever comes first. It is honored at over 35,000 certified facilities nationwide. It excludes customer-supplied parts, routine friction wear (wiper blades, brake pads), commercial severe-duty abuse, racing, and failures from skipped routine fluid maintenance.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "- **Terms:** Net-30 invoicing upon credit review approval. Credit review takes up to 3 business days. - **Consolidated Monthly Statements:** Itemized billing grouped by vehicle VIN and internal company fleet unit ID. Statements issue on the **1st business day** of each month for the previous month's work, due 30 days from the statement date. - **Late Balances:** Accounts more than 15 days past due may lose priority scheduling until the account is current. A 1.5% monthly finance charge applies after 30 days. - **Disputes:** Raise invoice questions within 14 days of the statement date. - **Warranty:** Fleet repairs receive the same 24-month/24,000-mile warranty as retail repairs, subject to the severe-duty exclusions in `WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md`."}]

[{"source": "service_intervals_matrix.json", "quote": "maintenance_matrix_metadata:
{
    "shop": "NorthStar Auto Care",
    "standard_version": "2024.1",
    "labor_rate_standard_hourly": 145.0,
    "currency": "USD",
    "mileage_units": "miles",
    "note": "Intervals are baselines. The manufacturer's published schedule takes priority. Whichever of mileage or months occurs first triggers service. Package costs exclude tax and any repairs found during inspection."
}"}, {"source": "service_intervals_matrix.json", "quote": "{
    "service": "Diagnostic (OBD-II scan, circuit test, up to 1 hour teardown analysis)",
    "labor_hours": 1.0,
    "flat_fee": 145.0
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MNT-002",
    "category": "Routine Maintenance",
    "question": "What happens at the 30,000-mile service?",
    "answer": "Tier 3 includes a full synthetic oil change, a DOT 4 brake fluid exchange, engine and cabin air filters, a cooling system freeze-point and pH audit, and a battery CCA conductance test. It takes about 2.5 labor hours and the base package is $349.50.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "Under state automotive repair regulations, customers retain the right to inspect and keep all replaced mechanical parts (excluding exchange items subject to manufacturer core charges, which may be inspected on-site before return to distributor). - Ask for your old parts when you authorize the work, and we will bag and tag them at the front desk. - Core-charge items (alternators, starters, brake calipers, and batteries) can be viewed on-site, but must go back to the distributor. Core charges are listed on the estimate. - Parts that are hazardous (batteries, fluids) will be handed over in sealed containers or disposed of in compliance with the rules. - Unclaimed parts are kept for **7 days** after pickup of the vehicle."}]

