[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-004",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "Does the warranty cover towing or a rental car?",
    "answer": "No. The warranty covers the repaired part and labor, and not towing, rentals, lost time, or consequential damage, except where state law requires otherwise.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-006",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "Can I keep the parts you replace?",
    "answer": "Yes. Ask when you authorize the work and we'll bag and tag them. Exchange items with a core charge, like alternators and starters, can be inspected on-site, but they must be returned to the distributor.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "- **Terms:** Net-30 invoicing upon credit review approval. Credit review takes up to 3 business days. - **Consolidated Monthly Statements:** Itemized billing grouped by vehicle VIN and internal company fleet unit ID. Statements issue on the **1st business day** of each month for the previous month's work, due 30 days from the statement date. - **Late Balances:** Accounts more than 15 days past due may lose priority scheduling until the account is current. A 1.5% monthly finance charge applies after 30 days. - **Disputes:** Raise invoice questions within 14 days of the statement date. - **Warranty:** Fleet repairs receive the same 24-month/24,000-mile warranty as retail repairs, subject to the severe-duty exclusions in `WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md`."}, {"source": "ESTIMATE_AND_AUTHORIZATION_POLICY.md", "quote": "Under state automotive repair regulations, customers retain the right to inspect and keep all replaced mechanical parts (excluding exchange items subject to manufacturer core charges, which may be inspected on-site before return to distributor). - Ask for your old parts when you authorize the work, and we will bag and tag them at the front desk. - Core-charge items (alternators, starters, brake calipers, and batteries) can be viewed on-site, but must go back to the distributor. Core charges are listed on the estimate. - Parts that are hazardous (batteries, fluids) will be handed over in sealed containers or disposed of in compliance with the rules. - Unclaimed parts are kept for **7 days** after pickup of the vehicle."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-MNT-005",
    "category": "Routine Maintenance",
    "question": "How much tread do my tires need in winter?",
    "answer": "At least 4/32 inch for snow traction, even though the legal minimum is 2/32 inch. All-season rubber also hardens below 45\u00b0F (7\u00b0C), so dedicated winter tires are recommended for sub-freezing driving.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "service_intervals_matrix.json", "quote": "{
    "service": "Tire mount, balance, and install (set of 4)",
    "labor_hours": 1.2
}"}, {"source": "WINTERIZATION_AND_PREVENTATIVE_GUIDE.md", "quote": "- **Winter Tread Minimum:** All-season tires require a minimum of **4/32 inch** tread depth for snow traction (replacing normal 2/32 inch legal limit). - **How to Check:** Insert a quarter upside down with Washington's head into the groove. If the top of his head is visible, you are below 4/32 inch. We measure all four tires with a depth gauge during the DVI. - **Compound Glass Transition:** All-season rubber compounds harden below 45°F (7°C), significantly increasing braking distances. Dedicated winter tires recommended for sub-freezing regional travel. - **Winter Tires:** Look for the three-peak mountain snowflake symbol. Install a full set of four, and never just two. - **Tire Pressure:** Pressure drops about **1 psi for every 10°F (5.5°C)** drop in temperature. Check monthly with the tires cold, and set to the pressure on the driver-door placard."}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-006",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "Can I keep the parts you replace?",
    "answer": "Yes. Ask when you authorize the work and we'll bag and tag them. Exchange items with a core charge, like alternators and starters, can be inspected on-site, but they must be returned to the distributor.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-APPT-001",
    "category": "Appointments & Loaners",
    "question": "Do you offer loaner vehicles or shuttle services while my car is being serviced?",
    "answer": "Yes. We offer complimentary local shuttle rides within a 10-mile radius. For repairs exceeding $600 or taking longer than 24 hours, complimentary courtesy loaner cars are available upon reservation request (subject to driver license and insurance verification).",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-APPT-003",
    "category": "Appointments & Loaners",
    "question": "Can I drop my car off when you are closed?",
    "answer": "Yes. Park in a designated stall, fill out a work order envelope with your name, phone, odometer reading, and a description of the problem, and put the key in the night drop safe at Bay 1. We log your car in the next morning at 6:30 AM, and a service advisor texts you.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "1. Secure vehicle in designated Fleet North Lot parking stalls. 2. Complete the Fleet Work Order envelope detailing unit ID, current odometer, and primary driver complaint. 3. Deposit key into the tamper-evident dual-locking night drop safe located at the Bay 1 exterior wall. 4. Early shift dispatch technician logs intake scans into shop management software at **06:30 AM**. **Notes** - Lock the vehicle and remove valuables, fuel cards, and tools. - Any vehicle dropped after-hours is treated as received at 06:30 AM for SLA purposes. It does not qualify for the 08:30 AM same-day PM guarantee unless it was in the lot before 08:30 AM and logged by 06:30 AM, which is the standard case. - NorthStar is not responsible for items left in vehicles. - Our lot is lit and under camera surveillance."}, {"source": "FLEET_SERVICE_SOP.md", "quote": "- Morning dispatch begins at **06:30 AM** with the early-shift dispatch technician logging after-hours drop-offs and arranging the day's bay assignments. - **Priority Order:** (1) Safety-critical (RED) fleet repairs, (2) PM Tier 1 drop-offs received before 08:30 AM, (3) scheduled minor repairs, (4) other fleet work, (5) retail customers. - Fleet managers receive a text and email with a work-order number for each unit by **07:30 AM**. - Fleet DVI reports are issued within **90 minutes** of drop-off, with photos and a color grade for each of the 40 inspection points. - Pickup updates: Units are staged in the Fleet North Lot, and keys are available at the front desk from 7:00 AM."}]

[{"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-WAR-002",
    "category": "Warranty & Guarantees",
    "question": "A part you replaced failed while I'm traveling. What should I do?",
    "answer": "Call us or the nationwide warranty hotline before authorizing any repair, and have your invoice number ready. If you are at a participating facility, they diagnose the failure, and a covered repair costs you $0 for parts and labor.",
    "escalate_to_human": true
}"}, {"source": "faq_support_knowledgebase.json", "quote": "{
    "id": "FAQ-DIAG-005",
    "category": "Diagnostics & Estimates",
    "question": "Can I bring my own parts for you to install?",
    "answer": "To uphold our strict safety standards and back our work with our 24-month/24,000-mile nationwide warranty, we do not install customer-supplied parts. All components are sourced directly through certified OEM dealer networks or premium Tier-1 manufacturers.",
    "escalate_to_human": false
}"}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "- Parts are warranted at the level of the manufacturer or longer. If the manufacturer's warranty is shorter than 24 months, NorthStar covers the remainder of our 24 months or 24,000 miles. - **Consequential Damage:** Towing, rental cars, lost time, and secondary damage are not covered, except where required by law. - Where state law gives you greater rights, the law applies."}, {"source": "WARRANTY_AND_REPAIR_POLICY.md", "quote": "NorthStar Auto Care warrants all parts and labor performed by our ASE-certified technicians for **24 months or 24,000 miles**, whichever occurs first. - **Coverage:** Mechanical parts replacement failure, installation labor defects, and hydraulic seal leaks. Both **parts and labor** are covered at no charge for the repaired component. - **Nationwide Protection:** Valid at over 35,000 certified participating repair centers across North America. If you are more than 25 miles from NorthStar, call the warranty hotline before authorizing any repair so the claim can be validated. - **Exclusions:** Commercial severe-duty abuse, auto racing, lack of subsequent routine fluid maintenance, customer-supplied parts, and normal brake pad/wiper friction wear."}]

